msgstr "# a self-contained bundle\n"

#: src/tutorial/modules.md:243
msgid ""
"The `greet` project above is complete as shown — two directories, two "
"manifests, two sources. Copy the trees into files and `rut run .` from "
"`greet/app` to see:"
msgstr "上面的 `greet` 项目如所示般完整——两个目录、两份清单、两个源文件。把这些目录树抄进文件，从 `greet/app` 运行 `rut run .`，就会看到："

#: src/tutorial/modules.md:251
msgid "Next: [async: tasks, workers, and channels](async.md)."
msgstr "下一章：[异步：任务、worker 与通道](async.md)。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's concurrency is **pull-based**. An `async fn` compiles into a _future_ "
"— a cold value that runs nothing until something drives it. There are no "
"promises that start on creation, no microtask queue, no implicit scheduling: "
"the host owns time, and code progresses only when a driving loop pumps it. "
"The model is described in [the async "
"model](../core-concepts/async-model.md), with the full surface in [async and "
"await](../reference/async.md) and [tasks](../reference/tasks.md)."
msgstr "rut 的并发是**拉取式**的。`async fn` 编译成一个 _future_——一个冷的值，在被某种东西驱动之前什么也不做。没有一创建就启动的 promise，没有微任务队列，没有隐式调度：时间由宿主掌握，代码只有在驱动循环泵动它时才前进。这个模型在[异步模型](../core-concepts/async-model.md)中描述，完整表面见[异步与 await](../reference/async.md)与[任务](../reference/tasks.md)。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:12 src/reference/async.md:18
msgid "`async fn` and `await`"
msgstr "`async fn` 与 `await`"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:14
msgid ""
"An `async fn` declares its context — `cx: RunContext` — as the _first "
"parameter_. Calling it runs nothing: it returns a cold future. `await` is "
"the one in-body suspension point, and it consumes the future:"
msgstr "`async fn` 把自己的上下文——`cx: RunContext`——声明为_第一个参数_。调用它不会运行任何东西：它返回一个冷的 future。`await` 是函数体内唯一的挂起点，而且它会消费掉这个 future："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:18
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) {\n"
"    let mut i = n;\n"
"    while (i > 0) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"t-{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(500);       // park here; the loop resumes the frame\n"
"        i -= 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"lift-off\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) {\n"
"    let mut i = n;\n"
"    while (i > 0) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"t-{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(500);       // park here; the loop resumes the frame\n"
"        i -= 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"lift-off\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:30
msgid ""
"The cx is engine-minted at call sites the way `self` is — you never pass it "
"when _calling_ an async fn:"
msgstr "cx 与 `self` 一样，在调用点由引擎铸造——_调用_ async fn 时你从不传它："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:33
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"launch_future(countdown(log, 3));   // no cx — the engine supplies it\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"launch_future(countdown(log, 3));   // no cx — the engine supplies it\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:37
msgid "Two consume paths, and exactly one per future:"
msgstr "两条消费路径，每个 future 恰好取其一："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:39
msgid ""
"**`await fut`** — drive it from this async fn's body. Legal only inside an "
"`async fn`, and only for engine-woven futures (async-fn results and `sleep`)."
msgstr "**`await fut`**——在这个 async fn 的体内驱动它。只在 `async fn` 内合法，且只适用于引擎织入的 future（async fn 的结果和 `sleep`）。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:42
msgid ""
"**`launch_future(fut)`** — hand it to the driving loop and keep a receipt. "
"Returns a `LaunchedFutureHandle<T>`, which is _not_ a future: it cannot be "
"awaited or re-launched. Its `abort()` flags cancellation; the frame notices "
"at its next checkpoint and runs its cleanup."
msgstr "**`launch_future(fut)`**——把它交给驱动循环，并保留一张回执。返回的 `LaunchedFutureHandle<T>` _不是_ future：不能 await，也不能再次 launch。它的 `abort()` 标记取消；帧在下一个检查点察觉到，并运行自己的清理。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:47
msgid ""
"`sleep(ms)` is the one built-in pender — a `Future<nil>` that parks its "
"frame until the VM's clock reaches the deadline."
msgstr "`sleep(ms)` 是唯一的内置 pender——一个 `Future<nil>`，它把自己的帧停靠住，直到 VM 的时钟走到期限为止。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:50
msgid "Both `launch_future` and `sleep` come from the `async_host` package:"
msgstr "`launch_future` 和 `sleep` 都来自 `async_host` 包："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:56
msgid "Who drives?"
msgstr "谁来驱动？"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:58
msgid ""
"You never write a driving loop — the _embedder_ does. The `rut run` CLI is "
"an embedder: after `main` returns it pumps the loop — drain ready frames, "
"advance the virtual clock to the next timer deadline, repeat — until nothing "
"is pending. So a program launches work from `main` and the output simply "
"appears:"
msgstr "你从不编写驱动循环——_嵌入方_来写。`rut run` CLI 就是一个嵌入方：`main` 返回后它泵动循环——排空就绪的帧，把虚拟时钟推进到下一个定时器期限，如此往复——直到没有任何待处理的东西。于是程序从 `main` 发起工作，输出自然就出现了："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:75
msgid ""
"Calling an async function and awaiting it in the same body is the "
"straight-line case; launching is for concurrency — independent work that "
"overlaps through the loop's interleaving."
msgstr "在同一个体内调用异步函数并 await 它，是直线情形；launch 则用于并发——经由循环的交错而彼此重叠的独立工作。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:79
msgid "Talking to the network: the `http` package"
msgstr "与网络对话：`http` 包"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:81
msgid ""
"The standard `http` package is async-only where work actually waits. "
"Everything else — the client, the verbs, the builder — is sync construction "
"sugar:"
msgstr "标准 `http` 包只在真正等待的工作处才是异步的。其余一切——客户端、各个动词、构建器——都是同步的构造糖："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:92
msgid "The shape, step by step:"
msgstr "这个形状，一步一步："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:94
msgid ""
"`client.get(url)` (or `request()`, `post`, `put`, `patch`, `del`) hands back "
"a `RequestBuilder`; `.method(..)`, `.url(..)`, `.header(k, v)` (repeatable), "
"`.body(bytes)` chain on it."
msgstr "`client.get(url)`（或 `request()`、`post`、`put`、`patch`、`del`）交还一个 `RequestBuilder`；`.method(..)`、`.url(..)`、`.header(k, v)`（可重复）、`.body(bytes)` 在它上面链式调用。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:97
msgid "`.build()` freezes a re-sendable `Request`."
msgstr "`.build()` 冻结出一个可重发的 `Request`。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:98
msgid ""
"**`.send(cx)` is the async point.** It resolves at _headers_ — the wire body "
"is still unread."
msgstr "**`.send(cx)` 是异步点。**它在_响应头_到达时完成——线上的响应体还没有读取。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:100
msgid "From the `Response`, take one of two readbacks:"
msgstr "从 `Response` 出发，有两条读取路径："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:101
msgid "`await resp.body(cx)` — drain the remaining body in one future;"
msgstr "`await resp.body(cx)`——用一个 future 排干剩余的响应体；"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:102
msgid ""
"`resp.byte_stream()` then `await stream.next(cx)` — one chunk per future, "
"`nil` at end-of-stream, for bounded-memory downloads."
msgstr "`resp.byte_stream()` 然后 `await stream.next(cx)`——每个 future 一个数据块，流结束时为 `nil`，适合有界内存的下载。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:105
msgid ""
"Errors come back as data, not traps: status `0` is reserved for transport "
"failure (`resp.transport_error()` carries the reason), any real status — 4xx "
"and 5xx included — is a normal response (`resp.ok()` is the 2xx test), and a "
"mid-read wire death surfaces as `nil` from `next()` with the reason in "
"`stream.error()`."
msgstr "错误以数据的形式回来，而不是陷阱：状态 `0` 保留给传输失败（`resp.transport_error()` 携带原因），任何真实状态——包括 4xx 和 5xx——都是正常响应（`resp.ok()` 是 2xx 测试），而读取中途线路断开则表现为 `next()` 返回 `nil`，原因在 `stream.error()` 里。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:111
msgid ""
"A complete worker from the repository's GitHub-viewer example — send, then "
"drain:"
msgstr "来自仓库 GitHub-viewer 示例的一个完整 worker——先 send，再排干："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:114
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn do_list(cx: RunContext, client: HttpClient, owner: str, repo: str, "
"rf: str) -> i32 {\n"
"    let url = "
"f\"https://data.jsdelivr.com/v1/packages/gh/{owner}/{repo}@{rf}\";\n"
"    let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"    if (resp.status() == 0) {\n"
"        let why: str = resp.transport_error();\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: network error: {why}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (!resp.ok()) {\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: CDN {resp.status()}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    let (tree, e) = decodeJsonBytes<Root>(await resp.body(cx));\n"
"    if (e != nil) {\n"
"        let why: DecodeJsonError = e;\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: bad tree JSON at {why.at}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    // ... print the tree ...\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"async fn do_list(cx: RunContext, client: HttpClient, owner: str, repo: str, "
"rf: str) -> i32 {\n"
"    let url = "
"f\"https://data.jsdelivr.com/v1/packages/gh/{owner}/{repo}@{rf}\";\n"
"    let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"    if (resp.status() == 0) {\n"
"        let why: str = resp.transport_error();\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: network error: {why}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    if (!resp.ok()) {\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: CDN {resp.status()}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    let (tree, e) = decodeJsonBytes<Root>(await resp.body(cx));\n"
"    if (e != nil) {\n"
"        let why: DecodeJsonError = e;\n"
"        eprint(f\"rgh: bad tree JSON at {why.at}\");\n"
"        return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    // ... print the tree ...\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:138
msgid "The stream lane walks chunks — send, then loop:"
msgstr "流路径逐块行走——先 send，再循环："

#: src/tutorial/async.md:140
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"let stream = resp.byte_stream();\n"
"while (true) {\n"
"    let c = await stream.next(cx);\n"
"    if (c == nil) {\n"
"        let rerr = stream.error();\n"
"        if (rerr != nil) { return 1; }   // failed mid-read\n"
"        break;                            // clean end of stream\n"
"    }\n"
"    let chunk: bytes = c;\n"
"    total += chunk.len();\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"let resp = await client.get(url).build().send(cx);\n"
"let stream = resp.byte_stream();\n"
"while (true) {\n"
"    let c = await stream.next(cx);\n"
"    if (c == nil) {\n"
"        let rerr = stream.error();\n"
"        if (rerr != nil) { return 1; }   // failed mid-read\n"
"        break;                            // clean end of stream\n"
"    }\n"
"    let chunk: bytes = c;\n"
"    total += chunk.len();\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:155
msgid "`await select`, join, and structured scopes"
msgstr "`await select`、join 与结构化作用域"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:157
msgid ""
"Racing futures (`await select { fut1 -> .., fut2 x -> .. }`) and joining a "
"launched future's value (`await handle`) are spelled in the grammar but not "
"in this build — the compiler gates them. Cancellation _is_ here: "
"`handle.abort()` flags the frame, and the probe at its next checkpoint "
"unwinds it deterministically, running cleanup in reverse declaration order. "
"See [tasks](../reference/tasks.md) for the roadmap."
msgstr "竞速 future（`await select { fut1 -> .., fut2 x -> .. }`）与接取已 launch 的 future 的值（`await handle`）在语法里写得出来，但在当前构建中不可用——编译器把它们拦下。取消_已经落地_：`handle.abort()` 给帧打上标记，下一个检查点处的探针确定性地将它展开，按声明的逆序运行清理。路线图见[任务](../reference/tasks.md)。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:167
msgid ""
"For true parallelism, a host can spawn **workers** — separate VMs on "
"separate threads with separate heaps. There is no shared memory: all data "
"crosses typed channels, and what may cross is a checked rule — primitives "
"and `str` copy; a cell (vec, record, class instance) transfers when "
"exclusively held, else deep-copies; endpoints (`Sender`/`Receiver`) "
"transfer; **closures do not cross**. A trap in a worker kills only that "
"worker. The API is a host facility (`spawn_worker`, `Channel<T>`), so its "
"shape depends on your embedder — see [workers and "
"channels](../reference/workers-and-channels.md)."
msgstr "要真正的并行，宿主可以生成 **worker**——独立线程上、拥有独立堆的独立 VM。没有共享内存：所有数据都经由类型化通道穿越，而什么可以穿越是一条受检规则——基本类型和 `str` 复制；单元（vec、记录、类实例）在独占持有时转移，否则深复制；端点（`Sender`/`Receiver`）转移；**闭包不穿越**。worker 里的陷阱只杀死那个 worker。这个 API 是宿主设施（`spawn_worker`、`Channel<T>`），它的形状取决于你的嵌入方——参见 [worker 与通道](../reference/workers-and-channels.md)。"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:179
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use async_host::{ launch_future, sleep };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) {\n"
"    let mut i = n;\n"
"    while (i > 0) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"t-{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(500);\n"
"        i -= 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"lift-off\");\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"countdown\");\n"
"    launch_future(countdown(log, 3));\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use async_host::{ launch_future, sleep };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) {\n"
"    let mut i = n;\n"
"    while (i > 0) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"t-{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(500);\n"
"        i -= 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"lift-off\");\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"countdown\");\n"
"    launch_future(countdown(log, 3));\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/async.md:206
msgid "Next: [the standard library](stdlib.md)."
msgstr "下一章：[标准库](stdlib.md)。"

#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:3
msgid ""
"The standard library splits in two. **`core`** is the only true standard — a "
"prelude of builtin names that are _ambient_: in scope in every compilation "
"unit, no `use` needed. Everything else is a set of **swappable packages** "
"shipped in the toolchain tree — a program that wants one says so (a `use` "
"line; the CLI mounts the tree packages for loose files automatically, and a "
"package program lists them in its manifest). Any of them can be replaced "
"wholesale; the engine knows none of their names."
msgstr "标准库一分为二。**`core`** 是唯一真正的标准——一组_环境自带_的内置名字组成的前奏：在每个编译单元内都在作用域中，无需 `use`。其余则是一组随工具链树分发的**可换包**——想用某个包的程序要明说（一行 `use`；CLI 会为散文件自动挂载树内的包，而包程序则在清单里列出它们）。任何一个包都可以整体替换；引擎不知道它们任何一个的名字。"

