#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:23
msgid "Integer safety ladder"
msgstr "整数安全阶梯"

#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:25
msgid ""
"Every integer width carries compiler-lowered methods. Plain `+`/`-`/`*` trap "
"on overflow; these never do:"
msgstr "每个整数宽度都带有编译器下降（compiler-lowered）的方法。普通的 `+`/`-`/`*` 在溢出时触发陷阱；下面这些绝不会："

#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:28
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"ladder\");\n"
"    let mut v: u8 = 250;\n"
"    v = v.wrapping_add(10);            // 4 — two's-complement wrap\n"
"    let over = 200u8.checked_add(100); // (44, false) — .1 false = escaped\n"
"    let sat = 200u8.saturating_add(100); // 255 — clamp at the bounds\n"
"    log.info(f\"v={v} over=({over.0}, {over.1}) sat={sat}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"ladder\");\n"
"    let mut v: u8 = 250;\n"
"    v = v.wrapping_add(10);            // 4 — two's-complement wrap\n"
"    let over = 200u8.checked_add(100); // (44, false) — .1 false = escaped\n"
"    let sat = 200u8.saturating_add(100); // 255 — clamp at the bounds\n"
"    log.info(f\"v={v} over=({over.0}, {over.1}) sat={sat}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:45
msgid ""
"`checked_*` answers `(T, bool)`; `.0` holds the wrapped bits either way. "
"Pick per call site: a checksum wraps, a length checks."
msgstr "`checked_*` 返回 `(T, bool)`；无论结果如何，`.0` 都装着回绕后的位。按调用点取舍：校验和要回绕，长度要检查。"

#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:48
