#: src/tutorial/stdlib.md:362
msgid ""
"That completes the tutorial. From here, the [core "
"concepts](../core-concepts/design-goals.md) explain _why_ the language is "
"shaped the way it is, and the [reference](../reference/lexical-structure.md) "
"pins down every rule."
msgstr "教程到此完成。从这里出发，[核心概念](../core-concepts/design-goals.md)解释这门语言_为何_被塑造成如今的形状，[参考](../reference/lexical-structure.md)则钉牢每一条规则。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:3
msgid ""
"rut is a small, statically typed, embeddable scripting language with "
"Rust-flavored syntax, implemented in Rust. It is designed to be the "
"scripting layer of host applications — UI apps in particular — in the role a "
"JavaScript engine usually plays: a safe, hot-reloadable language that drives "
"the host's object graph."
msgstr "rut 是一门小型、静态类型、可嵌入的脚本语言，语法带 Rust 风格，用 Rust 实现。它被设计为宿主应用的脚本层——尤其是 UI 应用——扮演通常由 JavaScript 引擎承担的角色：一门安全、可热重载的语言，驱动宿主的对象图。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:9
msgid ""
"The difference is structural, not cosmetic. In an embedded JS engine the "
"host's types are erased (`Element`, `Store` are empty interfaces; the real "
"types exist only in `.d.ts` files and get \"recovered\" by convention), "
"cancellation is emulated on top of promises, and every value crossing the "
"bridge is re-parsed and re-coerced by hand. rut is built so those three "
"problems cannot arise: **types are kept at runtime**, **coroutines are "
"natively poll-based**, and **host values have deterministic lifetimes**."
msgstr "差异是结构性的，不是表面文章。在嵌入式 JS 引擎里，宿主的类型被擦除（`Element`、`Store` 是空接口；真实类型只存在于 `.d.ts` 文件中，靠约定\"恢复\"回来），取消是在 promise 之上模拟的，而每一个跨越桥的值都要手工重新解析、重新转换。rut 的构建方式让这三个问题根本无从产生：**类型在运行时保留**，**协程原生基于 poll**，**宿主值拥有确定性的生命周期**。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:18
msgid "The pillars"
msgstr "支柱"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:20
msgid ""
"**Fully static, reified types.** There is no dynamic typing, no `any`, no "
"gradual typing. Every value's exact type is known to the compiler and "
"carried at runtime — type tests, checked erasure, and host-boundary checks "
"all read the same runtime truth. See [reified types and "
"layouts](reified-types.md)."
msgstr "**完全静态、具体化的类型。**没有动态类型，没有 `any`，没有渐进类型。每个值的确切类型为编译器所知，并在运行时携带——类型测试、受检擦除与宿主边界检查读取的都是同一份运行时事实。参见[具体化类型与布局](reified-types.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:26
msgid ""
"**Types make code faster.** The bytecode is typed, generics monomorphize, "
"and primitive buffers stay flat: a fixed array of `f32` is a packed `f32` "
"buffer, not an array of boxed numbers. There is no JIT and none is needed — "
"the code shape a JS JIT exists to speculate on (polymorphic property loads) "
"does not exist in rut."
msgstr "**类型让代码更快。**字节码是类型化的，泛型会单态化，原始类型缓冲区保持扁平：一个定长的 `f32` 数组就是一块打包的 `f32` 缓冲区，而不是装箱数字组成的数组。没有 JIT，也不需要 JIT——JS JIT 赖以投机优化的代码形态（多态属性加载）在 rut 里根本不存在。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:32
msgid ""
"**Everything is a value — with two honest regimes.** Primitives move by "
"value; every composite (`str`, `bytes`, records, arrays, trait objects, "
"erasure boxes) is a reference-counted cell whose handle copies in O(1). "
"Sharing is the default and visible; there is no hidden copying. See "
"[everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)."
msgstr "**一切皆值——且只有两种如实的体制。**原始类型按值移动；每个复合类型（`str`、`bytes`、记录、数组、trait 对象、擦除盒）都是引用计数单元，复制的是它的句柄，O(1) 完成。共享是默认且可见的；不存在隐藏的复制。参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:38
msgid ""
"**Poll-based coroutines.** `async`/`await` compiles to cold state machines "
"with Rust-style poll semantics: a future that nobody drives costs nothing, "
"and cancellation drops the state machine at its suspension point. No "
"promises, no microtask queue. See [the async model](async-model.md)."
msgstr "**基于 poll 的协程。**`async`/`await` 编译为带 Rust 风格 poll 语义的冷状态机：无人驱动的 future 分文不费，取消则在暂停点丢弃状态机。没有 promise，没有微任务队列。参见[异步模型](async-model.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:44
msgid ""
"**Reference counting; no collector.** Objects die the moment their last "
"reference goes away, so destructors are deterministic — host resources "
"(threads, sockets, textures) release at a knowable point, not \"sometime at "
"GC\". Strong cycles leak by design; weak references are the first-class "
"answer. See [memory](memory.md)."
msgstr "**引用计数；没有收集器。**对象在最后一个引用消失的那一刻死亡，因此析构是确定性的——宿主资源（线程、套接字、纹理）在一个可知的时点释放，而不是\"GC 某时某刻\"。强循环引用按设计就会泄漏；弱引用才是一等公民的答案。参见[内存](memory.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:50
msgid ""
"**No JIT.** All optimization happens ahead of time: fold, inline, "
"monomorphize, emit typed bytecode. What you run is what you compiled — "
"predictable startup, predictable per-op cost, no tiering."
msgstr "**没有 JIT。**一切优化都提前发生：折叠、内联、单态化，产出类型化字节码。你运行的就是你编译的——启动可预期、每操作成本可预期、没有分层编译。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:54
msgid ""
"**Embeddable by contract.** The host registers native functions whose Rust "
"signatures _are_ the declared surface; every crossing is type-checked "
"against reified types, and the host owns the event loop, the fuel budget, "
"and the clock. See [the host boundary](host-boundary.md) and [the bytecode "
"VM](the-vm.md)."
msgstr "**以契约方式嵌入。**宿主注册原生函数，其 Rust 签名_就是_所声明的接口；每次跨越都针对具体化类型做类型检查，而事件循环、燃料预算与时钟都归宿主所有。参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)与[字节码 VM](the-vm.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:60
msgid "Why not JavaScript"
msgstr "为什么不用 JavaScript"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:62
msgid ""
"The case against shipping a JS engine — not just this or that implementation "
"— is fourfold, and each item has a structural answer:"
msgstr "反对内置 JS 引擎的理由——不针对某个具体实现，而是针对整类引擎——有四条，每一条都有一个结构层面的回答："

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:65
msgid ""
"**History debt compounds.** Two nullish values, coercing `==`, `typeof "
"null`, implicit semicolons: each is a permanent liability the ecosystem "
"re-implements forever. rut starts from a closed, small grammar — absence is "
"`nil` on a nullable type, errors are values, and legacy JS keywords are "
"reserved words whose error message tells you what to write instead. Nothing "
"legacy can accrete."
msgstr "**历史债务复利式累积。**两个表示\"空\"的值、会做转换的 `==`、`typeof null`、隐式分号：每一条都是永久性的负担，生态系统要永远为之重新实现补丁。rut 从一个封闭的小语法出发——缺失即可空类型上的 `nil`，错误是值，遗留的 JS 关键字则是保留字，其错误信息会告诉你该写什么。任何遗留物都无从沉积。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:72
msgid ""
"**Conformance means implementing the world.** A compliant engine needs "
"`BigInt`, `Intl`, `Date`'s quirks, microtask ordering — thousands of "
"person-hours before user code runs. rut's built-in contract is deliberately "
"tiny: primitives, sequences, channels, string building. Everything else is "
"library — maps and sets, JSON, logging, and the host's own domain are "
"ordinary packages, several of them written _in rut_ and swappable."
msgstr "**符合规范等于实现整个世界。**一个合规引擎需要 `BigInt`、`Intl`、`Date` 的种种怪癖、微任务顺序——在用户代码能跑起来之前就要投入数千人时。rut 的内置契约刻意保持极小：原始类型、序列、通道、字符串构建。其余一切都是库——map 与 set、JSON、日志以及宿主自身的领域都是普通的包，其中几个就是_in rut_ 写成的，而且可替换。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:80
msgid ""
"**Too slow without a JIT.** Interpreter-only JS runs one to two orders of "
"magnitude slower, because a JS engine's speed _is_ its JIT. rut's no-JIT "
"stance is viable only because the language is statically typed: calls bind "
"statically whenever the call site names one concrete type, and dynamic "
"dispatch is a checked vtable hop that happens only where the program "
"actually erases types."
msgstr "**没有 JIT 就太慢。**纯解释执行的 JS 慢一到两个数量级，因为 JS 引擎的速度_就是_它的 JIT。rut 的无 JIT 立场之所以可行，恰恰因为这门语言是静态类型的：只要调用点指明了一个具体类型，调用就静态绑定；动态分派则是一次经过检查的 vtable 跳转，只发生在程序真正擦除类型的地方。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:87
msgid ""
"**Too much memory.** JS values are boxes — per-object headers, tagged "
"pointers, boxed array elements, collector overhead. rut's answer is layout: "
"untagged 8-byte slots, record payloads as slot arrays, flat primitive "
"buffers, and reference counting with no collector pass on the hot path."
msgstr "**太占内存。**JS 的值都是盒子——每对象头部、带标签的指针、装箱的数组元素、收集器开销。rut 的答案是布局：无标签的 8 字节槽位、以槽数组存放的记录载荷、扁平的原始类型缓冲区，以及热路径上没有收集器扫描的引用计数。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:93
msgid "What \"no dynamic typing\" leaves you"
msgstr "\"没有动态类型\"给你留下什么"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:95
msgid "Erasure is never silent — it is spelled and checked:"
msgstr "擦除从不悄悄发生——它被明确写出并接受检查："

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:97
msgid ""
"**Trait-typed values** (`d: Drawable`) for polymorphism. Dispatch is dynamic "
"only where a value may be one of several concrete types, and a trait-typed "
"value still carries its exact class at runtime."
msgstr "**trait 类型的值**（`d: Drawable`）用于多态。只有当值可能是若干具体类型之一时，分派才是动态的；而且 trait 类型的值在运行时仍携带其确切的类。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:100
msgid ""
"**The `opaque` box** (`opaque(v)`, `opaque.downcast<T>(o)`) for storage. "
"Erasure mints a checked box; recovery checks the runtime type and yields "
"`nil` on a mismatch — never a silent wrong-type read."
msgstr "**`opaque` 盒**（`opaque(v)`、`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`）用于存储。擦除铸造一个经过检查的盒；恢复则检查运行时类型，不匹配时给出 `nil`——绝不会悄悄读出错误类型的值。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:104
msgid ""
"JSON-shaped data, heterogeneous collections, and `any`\\-shaped host APIs "
"all route through these two doors, which is what keeps \"every value has a "
"runtime type\" true without giving up dynamism where it earns its keep."
msgstr "JSON 形状的数据、异构集合以及 `any`\\-形状的宿主 API 都经由这两扇门——\"每个值都有运行时类型\"因此保持为真，同时在动态性真正物有所值之处，它也未被放弃。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:108
msgid "The execution model"
msgstr "执行模型"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:115
msgid ""
"**One thread per VM.** A `Vm` instance runs on one thread with one heap and "
"no atomics; workers are separate VMs communicating by typed message passing."
msgstr "**每个 VM 一个线程。**一个 `Vm` 实例运行在一个线程上，拥有一套堆，不使用原子操作；worker 是彼此独立的 VM，通过类型化的消息传递通信。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:118
msgid ""
"**The host owns time.** The VM exposes stepping verbs — drain the ready "
"queue, expire timers, poll with a deadline — plus op budgets and interrupt "
"callbacks. A UI host drives script between frames and stays responsive; a "
"test host virtualizes the clock and gets fully deterministic schedules."
msgstr "**时间归宿主所有。**VM 暴露一组步进动词——排空就绪队列、让到期的定时器触发、带截止时间的 poll——外加操作预算与中断回调。UI 宿主在帧间驱动脚本并保持响应；测试宿主虚拟化时钟，得到完全确定性的调度。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:123
msgid ""
"**Traps stop at the boundary.** A panic in script (overflow, nil deref, a "
"failed `assert`) unwinds as a `Trap` value to the host call — rut code never "
"catches one. Bugs become host-visible errors with a script backtrace, not "
"corrupted state."
msgstr "**陷阱止步于边界。**脚本中的 panic（溢出、对 nil 解引用、失败的 `assert`）会以 `Trap` 值的形式沿栈展开到宿主调用——rut 代码永远捕获不到它。bug 变成宿主可见、带脚本回溯的错误，而不是被破坏的状态。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:128 src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:143
#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:233 src/core-concepts/memory.md:199
msgid "What this buys you"
msgstr "这给你带来什么"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:130
msgid ""
"If you are **writing scripts**: assignments never deep-copy; cleanup runs "
"when the last reference dies; a miss is `nil`, a failure is a returned `err` "
"string, and a crash is a loud trap with a real stack trace. If you are "
"**embedding**: you declare your API once in a rut declaration file, bind it "
"with typed Rust closures, and the compiler plus the load-time verifier "
"reject every mismatched shape before any script runs — there is no bridge "
"boilerplate to maintain."
msgstr "如果你在**写脚本**：赋值从不深拷贝；清理在最后一个引用消亡时运行；未命中是 `nil`，失败是一个返回的 `err` 字符串，崩溃则是伴随真实栈回溯的响亮陷阱。如果你在**做嵌入**：你在 rut 声明文件里一次性声明 API，用带类型的 Rust 闭包绑定它，编译器加上加载期校验器会在任何脚本运行之前拒绝每一个不匹配的形状——没有任何需要维护的桥接样板。"

#: src/core-concepts/design-goals.md:138
msgid ""
"The rest of this section walks each pillar in depth; the tutorial shows the "
"day-to-day syntax, and the reference pins down exact rules."
msgstr "本节其余部分将逐一深入每根支柱；教程展示日常语法，参考手册钉死精确规则。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's type system has one spine: **every name binds a value**, and there are "
"exactly two ways a value can exist. Primitives and `fn` values are "
"_immediate_ — moved by copying their bits. Every other type is a _cell_ — a "
"heap object whose **handle** is what gets copied. That single split explains "
"assignment, parameter passing, equality, and what `bytes.clone()` is for."
msgstr "rut 的类型系统有一条主干：**每个名字绑定的都是值**，而值只有两种存在方式。原始类型与 `fn` 值是_立即的_——通过复制其比特位来移动。其余每种类型都是_单元_——一种堆对象，被复制的是它的**句柄**。仅这一条分界就解释了赋值、传参、相等判断，以及 `bytes.clone()` 存在的意义。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:10
msgid "The two regimes"
msgstr "两种体制"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:12
msgid "immediate"
msgstr "立即"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:12
msgid "cells"
msgstr "单元"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid "types"
msgstr "类型"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid "`u8..u64`, `i8..i64`, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `fn` values"
msgstr "`u8..u64`、`i8..i64`、`f32`、`f64`、`bool`、`fn` 值"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:14
msgid ""
"`str`, `bytes`, `struct` and `class` records, `[T]` arrays, enums, trait "
"objects, `opaque` boxes, `?T` boxes, closures' captured cells"
msgstr "`str`、`bytes`、`struct` 与 `class` 记录、`[T]` 数组、枚举、trait 对象、`opaque` 盒、`?T` 盒、闭包捕获的单元"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "assignment"
msgstr "赋值"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "copies the bits"
msgstr "复制比特位"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:15
msgid "copies the handle (O(1))"
msgstr "复制句柄（O(1)）"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "mutation"
msgstr "变更"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "n/a — write the variable"
msgstr "不适用——直接写入变量"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:16
msgid "visible through every alias"
msgstr "经由每个别名都可见"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "`==`"
msgstr "`==`"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "by value"
msgstr "按值"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:17
msgid "`str`/`bytes`: by content; everything else: identity"
msgstr "`str`/`bytes` 按内容；其余一切按身份"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:19
msgid ""
"There is no third regime. No type is \"sometimes copied, sometimes shared\": "
"a `struct` value never silently deep-copies, a `str` never silently aliases. "
"The regime is a property of the _type_, known at compile time, and the "
"compiler emits the right move for it."
msgstr "没有第三种体制。没有任何类型\"有时复制、有时共享\"：`struct` 值从不悄悄深拷贝，`str` 也从不悄悄别名化。体制是_类型_的属性，编译期即知，编译器会为它生成正确的移动指令。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:24
msgid "Sharing is the law for cells"
msgstr "共享是单元的法则"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:26
msgid ""
"`let b = a` on any cell type is one handle move: the new binding retains the "
"cell, the old binding releases it. Passing a million-element array to a "
"function retains once. A loop binding iterates the _stored_ elements, not "
"copies of them."
msgstr "对任何单元类型写 `let b = a` 只是一次句柄移动：新绑定保留单元，旧绑定释放它。把一个百万元素的数组传给函数只保留一次。循环绑定迭代的是_存储的_元素，而不是它们的副本。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:31
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;          // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;            // q.x is 4 now — sharing is the law\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x = {q.x}\");   // read through the other alias\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let mut p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };\n"
"    let q = p;          // q and p name ONE cell\n"
"    p.x = 4;            // q.x is 4 now — sharing is the law\n"
"    log.info(f\"q.x = {q.x}\");   // read through the other alias\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:49
msgid ""
"Mutation through an alias is visible through all of them, in both "
"directions. What gates _writing_ is the `mut`\\-binding rule — a binding "
"must be declared `mut` to be written through — never the sharing itself. "
"Sharing is always safe: a handle keeps its referent alive, so nothing "
"dangles, and there is no borrow checker because there are no loans."
msgstr "经由别名做出的变更，会沿所有别名可见，双向皆然。真正把守_写入_的是 `mut`\\-绑定规则——绑定必须声明为 `mut` 才能通过它写入——而绝不是共享本身。共享始终安全：句柄会让其引用对象保活，因此没有任何东西悬空；没有借用检查器，因为根本不存在借用。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:55
msgid ""
"If you want a value that aliases nothing, you build one: a literal, a "
"constructor, a copy of the fields you need. The language has exactly one "
"copy escape hatch — `bytes.clone()`, a one-shot deep copy of a binary "
"buffer, for interop hand-offs. There is no generic `clone`: a divergent "
"value of any other type is unreachable by construction, which is what makes "
"aliasing something you can reason about locally."
msgstr "如果你想要一个不与任何东西别名的值，就亲手造一个：字面量、构造器，或者按需复制字段。这门语言恰好有一个复制逃生口——`bytes.clone()`，对二进制缓冲区做一次性深拷贝，服务于互操作交接。没有泛型 `clone`：任何其他类型的发散值在构造上都不可达，这正是别名可以被局部推理的原因。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:62
#: src/reference/builtin-generic-types.md:46
msgid "`?T` — the nullable"
msgstr "`?T` —— 可空类型"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:64
msgid ""
"Absence is `nil` on a nullable type, spelled as a prefix on the type: `?T` "
"is \"a `T` or `nil`\". `?` applies to the type term that follows, so `[?T]` "
"is an array of nullables while `?[T]` is a nullable array, and `??T` chains "
"(and unwraps transitively at use)."
msgstr "缺失即可空类型上的 `nil`，写作类型上的前缀：`?T` 是\"一个 `T` 或 `nil`\"。`?` 作用于其后的类型项，因此 `[?T]` 是可空数组——元素可空——而 `?[T]` 是可空数组本身，`??T` 则可链式叠加（并在使用时传递式解包）。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:69
msgid ""
"The coercions are one line: **`T → ?T` boxes; `?T → T` derefs.** The box is "
"a fresh one-slot cell that _aliases_ the value's cell — boxing a record "
"shares it, boxing a primitive copies its bits. The deref is implicit at "
"every value position: field access, method calls, indexing, iteration, "
"arithmetic all read through the box."
msgstr "这些转换一行就能说清：**`T → ?T` 装盒；`?T → T` 解引用。**盒是一个全新的一槽单元，_别名_值所在的单元——装盒一个记录就是共享它，装盒一个原始类型则复制其比特位。解引用在每个值位置都是隐式的：字段访问、方法调用、索引、迭代、算术，全都透过盒读取。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:75
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct User { id: i64; name: str }\n"
"\n"
"fn lookup(id: i64) -> ?User {\n"
"    if (id == 7) { return User { id: 7, name: \"ada\" }; }\n"
"    return nil;             // a miss is nil, nothing else\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let u = lookup(7);                // ?User\n"
"    log.info(f\"u.name = {u.name}\");   // auto-deref when non-nil\n"
"    let missing = lookup(8);\n"
"    log.info(f\"miss is nil: {missing == nil}\");   // guard where absence "
"is expected\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct User { id: i64; name: str }\n"
"\n"
"fn lookup(id: i64) -> ?User {\n"
"    if (id == 7) { return User { id: 7, name: \"ada\" }; }\n"
"    return nil;             // a miss is nil, nothing else\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let u = lookup(7);                // ?User\n"
"    log.info(f\"u.name = {u.name}\");   // auto-deref when non-nil\n"
"    let missing = lookup(8);\n"
"    log.info(f\"miss is nil: {missing == nil}\");   // guard where absence "
"is expected\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:99
msgid ""
"A `nil` reaching a value use traps (`NilDeref`) — never a silent read. Guard "
"with `u == nil` where absence is expected; the trap is the bug-catcher, not "
"the semantics. A miss is `nil` and nothing else: a lookup that finds nothing "
"returns `?V`, and callers compare against `nil`."
msgstr "抵达值用途的 `nil` 会触发陷阱（`NilDeref`）——绝不会悄悄读出一个值。在预期可能缺失之处用 `u == nil` 设守卫；陷阱是抓 bug 的工具，而不是语义本身。未命中就是 `nil`，别无他物：找不到结果的查找返回 `?V`，调用方与 `nil` 比较。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:105
msgid "`==` is honest about the regime"
msgstr "`==` 对体制如实相告"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:107
msgid "Primitives compare **by value**."
msgstr "原始类型**按值**比较。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:108
msgid "`str` compares **by content** (codepoints); `bytes` by octets."
msgstr "`str` 按**内容**（码点）比较；`bytes` 按字节（octet）比较。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:109
msgid ""
"Everything else compares **by identity** — two bindings are equal exactly "
"when they name the same cell."
msgstr "其余一切**按身份**比较——两个绑定相等，当且仅当它们指名同一个单元。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:112
msgid ""
"Identity is the only equality full sharing can defend: two separately built "
"`[1, 2]` arrays are two cells, so `[1,2] == [1,2]` is `false`. Content "
"comparison is a loop over fields, written where content is the contract. The "
"one place identity quietly behaves like value equality: enum variants are "
"immortal singletons, so `Flavor.Sour == Flavor.Sour` is `true`."
msgstr "身份是完全共享唯一能捍卫的相等：两个分别构建的 `[1, 2]` 数组是两个单元，因此 `[1,2] == [1,2]` 是 `false`。内容比较是一个遍历字段的循环，写在内容才是契约的地方。身份唯一一处悄悄表现得像值相等的地方：枚举成员是不朽的单例，所以 `Flavor.Sour == Flavor.Sour` 是 `true`。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:119
msgid "The answer channel: a pair"
msgstr "应答通道：对偶"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:121
msgid ""
"There is no exception type and no `Result` monad. Failures are data in the "
"second element of a record — `(value, err)` — with one documented convention:"
msgstr "没有异常类型，也没有 `Result` 单子。失败是对偶——`(value, err)`——第二个元素里的数据，配一条成文的约定："

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:125
msgid "an **empty err plus a value** is success;"
msgstr "**err 为空且带值**即成功；"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:126
msgid "an **empty err plus `nil`** means \"not found\";"
msgstr "**err 为空且为 `nil`** 意为\"未找到\"；"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:127
msgid "a **non-empty err** means \"failed\"."
msgstr "**err 非空**即为\"失败\"。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:129
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn parse_hex(s: str) -> (bytes, str) {\n"
"    if (s.len() % 2 != 0) {\n"
"        return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: odd-length input\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    let n = s.len() / 2;\n"
"    let mut buf: [u8] = [0u8; n];\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n"
"        let hi = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2));\n"
"        let lo = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2 + 1));\n"
"        if (hi < 0 || lo < 0) {\n"
"            return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: not a digit\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        buf[i] = ((hi * 16) + lo) as u8;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (bytes.from(buf), \"\");       // (data, \"\") on success\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn hex_digit(c: u32) -> i64 {\n"
"    if (c >= 48 && c <= 57) { return (c - 48) as i64; }   // '0'..'9'\n"
"    if (c >= 97 && c <= 102) { return (c - 87) as i64; }  // 'a'..'f'\n"
"    return -1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"4869\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); return; }   // propagate\n"
"    log.info(f\"ok: {raw.decode()} ({raw.len()} bytes)\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"486\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); }           // the failure "
"channel\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"fn parse_hex(s: str) -> (bytes, str) {\n"
"    if (s.len() % 2 != 0) {\n"
"        return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: odd-length input\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    let n = s.len() / 2;\n"
"    let mut buf: [u8] = [0u8; n];\n"
"    for (let i = 0; i < n; i += 1) {\n"
"        let hi = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2));\n"
"        let lo = hex_digit(s.code_at(i * 2 + 1));\n"
"        if (hi < 0 || lo < 0) {\n"
"            return (bytes.zeroed(0), \"hex: not a digit\");\n"
"        }\n"
"        buf[i] = ((hi * 16) + lo) as u8;\n"
"    }\n"
"    return (bytes.from(buf), \"\");       // (data, \"\") on success\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn hex_digit(c: u32) -> i64 {\n"
"    if (c >= 48 && c <= 57) { return (c - 48) as i64; }   // '0'..'9'\n"
"    if (c >= 97 && c <= 102) { return (c - 87) as i64; }  // 'a'..'f'\n"
"    return -1;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"values\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"4869\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); return; }   // propagate\n"
"    log.info(f\"ok: {raw.decode()} ({raw.len()} bytes)\");\n"
"    let (raw, err) = parse_hex(\"486\");\n"
"    if (err != \"\") { log.info(f\"err: {err}\"); }           // the failure "
"channel\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:170
msgid ""
"The pair destructure in return position is free — the compiler fuses the "
"mint away — so this shape costs nothing on hot paths. At the host boundary "
"the same pair crosses field by field, which makes `entry fn -> (?T, err)` "
"the standard answer a Rust embedder reads."
msgstr "返回位置的对偶解构是免费的——编译器会把铸造融合掉——所以这种形状在热路径上分文不费。在宿主边界，同一个对偶逐字段跨越，这让 `entry fn -> (?T, err)` 成为 Rust 嵌入方一眼即懂的标准应答。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:175
msgid "Consequences you feel day to day"
msgstr "日常能感受到的后果"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:177
msgid ""
"**Reassignment is cheap.** Moving containers around — returning them, "
"storing them, restructuring them — is handle traffic, not payload traffic. "
"Algorithms that churn records and arrays pay aliasing, not copying."
msgstr "**重新赋值很便宜。**把容器搬来搬去——返回、存储、重组——是句柄流量，不是载荷流量。大量周转记录与数组的算法付出的是别名代价，而不是复制代价。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:181
msgid ""
"**Loop variables are fresh per iteration but share elements.** A `for (let x "
"of xs)` loop hands you the stored element; writes through it mutate the "
"sequence. Each iteration is a fresh _binding_."
msgstr "**循环变量每轮都是新的，但共享元素。**`for (let x of xs)` 循环交给你的是存储的元素；通过它写入会改变序列本身。每一轮都是一个全新的_绑定_。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:184
msgid ""
"**Containers of primitives stay flat.** A fixed `[i32]` is a packed `i32` "
"buffer; growable sequences of primitives store raw payloads with a one-byte "
"nil tag — no per-element heap box."
msgstr "**原始类型容器保持扁平。**定长 `[i32]` 就是一块打包的 `i32` 缓冲区；可增长的原始类型序列直接存储裸载荷，外加一个字节的 nil 标签——没有逐元素的堆盒。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:187
msgid ""
"**Erasure is a box.** `opaque(v)` mints an erasure box; recovery is "
"`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`, checked against the runtime type. See [reified "
"types](reified-types.md) and the reference on "
"[`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md)."
msgstr "**擦除是一个盒。**`opaque(v)` 铸造一个擦除盒；恢复靠 `opaque.downcast<T>(o)`，对照运行时类型检查。参见[具体化类型](reified-types.md)以及关于 [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md) 的参考章节。"

#: src/core-concepts/everything-is-a-value.md:192
msgid ""
"The memory machinery under all of this — refcounts, deterministic "
"destructors, weak references — is the next chapter's subject: "
"[memory](memory.md). The exact rules live in the reference on [by-reference "
"and nullable](../reference/by-reference-and-nullable.md)."
msgstr "这一切底下的内存机制——引用计数、确定性析构、弱引用——是下一章的主题：[内存](memory.md)。精确规则见关于[按引用与可空](../reference/by-reference-and-nullable.md)的参考章节。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:3
msgid ""
"Types in rut are not a compile-time fiction. Every value's exact type is "
"available at runtime — generics included: a `Cache<i32>` and a `Cache<str>` "
"are _different types_ to the VM, with distinct identities and distinct "
"method sets. This chapter explains where that reified reality lives, what it "
"is used for, and how values are actually laid out."
msgstr "rut 的类型不是编译期的虚构。每个值的确切类型在运行时可得——泛型也包括在内：对 VM 而言，`Cache<i32>` 和 `Cache<str>` 是_不同的类型_，有各自独立的身份和各自的方法集。本章讲清这种具体化的实在存于何处、用来做什么，以及值究竟是如何布局的。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:10
msgid "The mental model"
msgstr "心智模型"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:12
msgid ""
"Think of the VM as keeping a **type table**: one descriptor per instantiated "
"type — its kind, its field list, its trait impls, and for composites the "
"method tables its instances point at. Every heap cell's header names an "
"entry in that table. A value never \"forgets\" its type, because its type is "
"one field read away."
msgstr "把 VM 想成在维护一张**类型表**：每个实例化的类型一个描述符——它的类别、字段列表、trait impl，复合类型还有其实例指向的方法表。每个堆单元的头部都指名该表中的一个条目。值绝不会\"忘记\"自己的类型，因为读一个字段就能拿到它。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:18
msgid ""
"Types themselves are not first-class script values — you cannot put a type "
"in a variable or write a function over types. What you get is the "
"language-facing _surfaces_ of reification:"
msgstr "类型本身不是一等公民的脚本值——你不能把类型放进变量，也不能写以类型为对象的函数。你能得到的，是具体化面向语言的几个_表面_："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:22
msgid ""
"**`is` type tests** — `x is Circle` (exact) and `x is Drawable` (capability: "
"does this value's type have a registered impl?)."
msgstr "**`is` 类型测试**——`x is Circle`（确切类型）与 `x is Drawable`（能力：这个值的类型是否注册了 impl？）。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:24
msgid ""
"**Checked erasure** — `opaque.downcast<T>(o)` reads the box's runtime type "
"and recovers the payload, or `nil` on a mismatch."
msgstr "**受检擦除**——`opaque.downcast<T>(o)` 读取盒的运行时类型并取回载荷，不匹配则得到 `nil`。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:26
msgid ""
"**Host-boundary checks** — native functions declare parameter types once; "
"every call is checked against them."
msgstr "**宿主边界检查**——原生函数一次性声明参数类型；每次调用都对照检查。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:28
msgid ""
"**Debugging and traces** — error messages, backtraces, and formatter output "
"name real runtime types."
msgstr "**调试与追踪**——错误信息、回溯与格式化输出都指名真实的运行时类型。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:31
msgid "Why reification is load-bearing"
msgstr "为什么具体化是承重墙"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:33
msgid ""
"The reason rut can check everything cheaply is that the runtime type is "
"always reachable:"
msgstr "rut 能低成本检查一切，原因是运行时类型永远可达："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:36
msgid ""
"**The host boundary needs no coercion code.** A native fn declares `(Opaque, "
"str, str) -> nil` once; the VM checks each argument's runtime type at the "
"crossing. There is no bridge-side \"re-parse-and-pray\" layer, because a "
"wrong-shaped call fails loudly at the boundary."
msgstr "**宿主边界不需要转换代码。**原生 fn 一次性声明 `(Opaque, str, str) -> nil`；VM 在跨越处检查每个实参的运行时类型。桥那一侧不存在\"重新解析然后祈祷\"的层，因为形状错误的调用会在边界响亮地失败。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:41
msgid ""
"**Erasure is checked, not blind.** `opaque(v)` stamps the box; "
"`opaque.downcast<T>` consults the stamp. A box answers type tests _by the "
"box_ — `o is T` misses for every payload type — so the only way back to the "
"payload is the checked recovery. Erasure without reification would be `any`; "
"with reification it is a sealed box."
msgstr "**擦除是受检的，不是盲目的。**`opaque(v)` 给盒盖章；`opaque.downcast<T>` 查验印章。盒回答类型测试时_以盒为准_——对每个载荷类型 `o is T` 都不命中——所以回到载荷的唯一途径是受检恢复。没有具体化的擦除就是 `any`；有了具体化，它是一个密封的盒。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:46
msgid ""
"**Distinct instantiations.** `Vec<f32>` and `Vec<f64>` are different types "
"everywhere — in the type table, in method resolution, at the host boundary. "
"Nothing about a generic's type argument is erased."
msgstr "**不同的实例化互不相同。**`Vec<f32>` 和 `Vec<f64>` 在任何地方都是不同的类型——类型表里、方法解析里、宿主边界上。泛型类型实参的任何信息都不会被擦除。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:49
msgid ""
"**Serialization and tooling.** Reflection walks the same descriptors, which "
"is how userland JSON encoding is complete without annotations or macros on "
"your types."
msgstr "**序列化与工具链。**反射遍历的正是同一批描述符，用户态的 JSON 编码因此无需在类型上加注解或宏就已然完备。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:53
msgid "Slots: the untagged hot path"
msgstr "槽位：无标签的热路径"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:55
msgid ""
"Inside the VM, registers and record fields are **untagged 8-byte slots**. "
"The bytecode is typed — every register's static type is recorded in the "
"function's signature and re-verified at load — so hot paths carry no type "
"tags at all:"
msgstr "在 VM 内部，寄存器和记录字段都是**无标签的 8 字节槽位**。字节码是类型化的——每个寄存器的静态类型都记录在函数签名中，并在加载时重新校验——所以热路径上完全不带类型标签："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:63
msgid "// ints, bool: the canonical scalar width\n"
msgstr "// 整数、bool：规范的标量宽度\n"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:64
msgid "// floats: f32 widened\n"
msgstr "// 浮点数：f32 宽化\n"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:65
msgid "// every non-primitive: a cell handle\n"
msgstr "// 每个非原始类型：一个单元句柄\n"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:69
msgid ""
"A primitive is its bits; a composite is a handle to a cell. The tagged world "
"— a value that carries its type with it — exists only at the host boundary, "
"where Rust code that cannot trust static types receives checked, typed "
"values."
msgstr "原始类型就是它的比特位；复合类型是指向单元的句柄。带标签的世界——值随身携带自己的类型——只存在于宿主边界：那里运行的是无法信任静态类型的 Rust 代码，接收的是经过检查、带类型的值。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:74
msgid "Record layout: one slot per field"
msgstr "记录布局：每个字段一个槽位"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:76
msgid ""
"Both `struct` and `class` values live in a cell: a header (refcount + type "
"id), a pointer to the type's vtable when the type has methods, and the "
"payload — **a slot array, one untagged slot per field, in declaration "
"order**."
msgstr "`struct` 和 `class` 值都住在一个单元里：一个头部（引用计数 + 类型 id）、一个指向类型 vtable 的指针（当该类型有方法时），以及载荷——**一个槽数组，按声明顺序每字段一个无标签槽位**。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:81
msgid ""
"Primitive fields are widened into their slot; composite fields are cell "
"handles."
msgstr "原始类型字段宽化后放入槽位；复合类型字段是单元句柄。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:83
msgid ""
"Visibility, generic parameters, and impl blocks elsewhere add _nothing_ — "
"the payload depends only on the field list."
msgstr "可见性、泛型参数以及别处的 impl 块都_不_占分毫——载荷只取决于字段列表。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:85
msgid ""
"Field access is by index; there are no hidden members and no inheritance, so "
"there is no base-class prefix and nothing to walk."
msgstr "字段访问按索引进行；没有隐藏成员，也没有继承，因此没有基类前缀，也无需遍历什么。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:87
msgid ""
"Fixed arrays of primitives (`[f32]`) keep their elements **flat and packed** "
"at machine width — the one place values live inline. Growable sequences are "
"rut-library classes over such arrays."
msgstr "原始类型的定长数组（`[f32]`）让元素以机器宽度**扁平且紧实**地存放——这是值唯一内联存在的地方。可增长序列是 rut 库在这类数组之上实现的类。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:91
msgid "Consequences:"
msgstr "由此带来的后果："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:93
msgid ""
"`size_of`/`align_of` do not exist, deliberately. Layout is an implementation "
"detail, not an API — rut has no C-ABI struct surface for hosts to mirror. "
"Hosts see records only through the checked boundary (see [the host "
"boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr "`size_of`/`align_of` 被刻意省去。布局是实现细节，不是 API——rut 没有可供宿主镜像的 C-ABI 结构体表面。宿主只能透过受检边界看见记录（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:97
msgid ""
"A record's memory cost is its field count times 8 bytes plus the cell "
"header, which is exactly what the heap budget charges."
msgstr "一条记录的内存开销是字段数乘 8 字节再加单元头部，而这正是堆预算所计费的。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:99
msgid ""
"Widening a value to a trait type allocates nothing: the trait-typed value "
"_is_ the same cell, reinterpreted through its vtable."
msgstr "把值宽化为 trait 类型不分配任何东西：trait 类型的值_就是_同一个单元，只是透过其 vtable 重新解释。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:102
msgid "Vtables: one per type, attached at construction"
msgstr "vtable：每个类型一张，构造时挂接"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:104
msgid ""
"A cell's vtable is filled when the value is constructed and never changes. "
"It names the exact type and holds one entry per trait method the type "
"implements, keyed by a global (trait instantiation, method) id — "
"`Slice<Point>` and `Slice<str>` have separate slot sets, because they are "
"separate trait instantiations."
msgstr "单元的 vtable 在值构造时填好，此后不再改变。它指明确切类型，并为该类型实现的每个 trait 方法持有一个条目，以全局的（trait 实例化，方法）id 为键——`Slice<Point>` 和 `Slice<str>` 拥有各自独立的槽位集，因为它们是彼此独立的 trait 实例化。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:110
msgid "A call through a trait object is two loads and an indirect jump:"
msgstr "透过 trait 对象的调用是两次加载加一次间接跳转："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:119
msgid ""
"An inherent method call — `c.area()` on a concrete `c` — compiles to a "
"direct call with no table involved. The dispatch rules that choose between "
"the two are the subject of the next chapter, [traits and "
"dispatch](traits-and-dispatch.md)."
msgstr "固有方法调用——在具体的 `c` 上调用 `c.area()`——编译为直接调用，不涉及任何表。在两者之间做出选择的分派规则是下一章的主题：[trait 与分派](traits-and-dispatch.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:124
msgid "Type tests, lowered"
msgstr "类型测试的下层形态"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:126
msgid "Every type test is a small, pure read:"
msgstr "每个类型测试都是一次小型、纯粹的读取："

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:128
msgid ""
"**Concrete test** (`d is Circle`): load the value's runtime type id, "
"compare. When the receiver's static type already answers, the compiler folds "
"it to a constant."
msgstr "**具体类型测试**（`d is Circle`）：加载值的运行时类型 id，比较。当接收者的静态类型已能作答时，编译器将其折叠为常量。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:131
msgid ""
"**Trait probe** (`x is Drawable`): load the type id, scan the descriptor's "
"registered impl list. Pure in its inputs, so repeated probes deduplicate and "
"invariant ones hoist."
msgstr "**trait 探测**（`x is Drawable`）：加载类型 id，扫描描述符中已注册的 impl 列表。输入是纯的，因此重复的探测会去重，不变的探测会被外提。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:134
msgid ""
"**Downcast** (`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`): the same type-id compare, followed "
"by the guarded payload extract."
msgstr "**向下转型**（`opaque.downcast<T>(o)`）：同样的类型 id 比较，随后是带守卫的载荷提取。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:137
msgid ""
"There is no `type_of(x)` returning a manipulable value and no runtime layout "
"introspection — the descriptors serve the VM, the checks, and tooling, not "
"userland metaprogramming. Reflection over data (walking fields to serialize) "
"is a library facility built on the same tables; see the reference on "
"[reflection](../reference/reflection.md)."
msgstr "这里没有返回可操纵值的 `type_of(x)`，也没有运行时布局内省——描述符服务于 VM、各项检查与工具链，而不是用户态元编程。对数据做反射（遍历字段以序列化）是一个建立在同一批表之上的库设施；参见关于[反射](../reference/reflection.md)的参考章节。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:145
msgid ""
"Type errors are **runtime facts, not conventions**: a host call, a downcast, "
"or a trait probe is checked against the same table the VM dispatches through."
msgstr "类型错误是**运行时事实，而不是约定**：宿主调用、向下转型或 trait 探测，对照的都是 VM 分派所用的同一张表。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:148
msgid ""
"**One runtime truth per value** — the vtable that answers dispatch is the "
"same one that answers `is`."
msgstr "**每个值只有一份运行时事实**——回答分派的 vtable 与回答 `is` 的是同一张。"

#: src/core-concepts/reified-types.md:150
msgid ""
"The tag-free hot path keeps the interpreter's arithmetic and field traffic "
"at raw slot speed while reification costs only what the program's dynamic "
"features actually use."
msgstr "无标签的热路径让解释器的算术和字段流量保持裸槽位速度，而具体化只收程序动态特性真正用到的那部分费用。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:3
msgid ""
"A trait in rut is a **named contract**: a list of method signatures that a "
"type can implement — by name, in an impl block. Satisfaction is nominal: the "
"impl block is the admission, and nothing else. A type whose members happen "
"to match a trait's shapes is _not_ an implementor; some module must say "
"`impl I for T`."
msgstr "rut 中的 trait 是一份**有名有姓的契约**：一列方法签名，类型可以按名实现——写进 impl 块。满足关系是名义上的：impl 块就是准入凭证，别无其他。成员碰巧长得像某个 trait 形状的类型_并不是_实现者；必须有某个模块写下 `impl I for T`。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:9
msgid "The shape of a trait"
msgstr "trait 的形状"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:11
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Point {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.x as f64; }\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64) { }    // the impl must list every trait method\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"area = {p.area()}\");     // a concrete receiver: static\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Point { x: f32; y: f32 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Point {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.x as f64; }\n"
"    fn scale(v: f64) { }    // the impl must list every trait method\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"traits\");\n"
"    let p = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n"
"    log.info(f\"area = {p.area()}\");     // a concrete receiver: static\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:37
msgid ""
"**Methods only, no bodies.** A trait declares signatures — no fields, no "
"properties, and no default implementations, ever. One member kind means one "
"dispatch candidate per call; a default body would be a second candidate with "
"a resolution law of its own."
msgstr "**只有方法，没有方法体。**trait 声明签名——没有字段，没有属性，也永远没有默认实现。成员只有一种，意味着每次调用只有一个分派候选；默认方法体会成为第二个候选，并自带一套独立的解析法则。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:41
msgid ""
"**Two impl forms.** `impl T { .. }` defines the type's _inherent_ methods "
"and may live only in the module that declares `T`. `impl I for T { .. }` "
"defines a trait implementation; its methods are exactly the trait's, with no "
"`pub` (they are as visible as the trait)."
msgstr "**两种 impl 形式。**`impl T { .. }` 定义类型的_固有_方法，且只能存在于声明 `T` 的模块里。`impl I for T { .. }` 定义一个 trait 实现；其方法与 trait 的完全一致，不带 `pub`（它们的可见性与 trait 相同）。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:45
msgid ""
"**One impl per pair, program-wide.** Two modules implementing the same trait "
"for the same type is a link error that names both. The impl registry — "
"merged when modules link — is the single source of truth for \"who "
"implements what\"."
msgstr "**每对组合全程序只有一个 impl。**两个模块为同一类型实现同一 trait 是一个链接错误，会同时点名双方。impl 注册表——在模块链接时合并——是\"谁实现了什么\"的唯一事实来源。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:49
msgid ""
"**Placement is pair-local.** A trait impl may live in the trait's package or "
"the type's package — at least one side of every `(trait, type)` pair must be "
"yours. Implementing two foreign types' pairing is rejected outright; there "
"is no orphan rule beyond that."
msgstr "**放置位置对组合局部。**trait impl 可以放在 trait 所在的包或类型所在的包——每个 `(trait, type)` 组合至少有一侧属于你自己。实现两个外部类型的组合会被直接拒绝；除此之外没有别的孤儿规则。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:53
msgid ""
"**Any nominal type can be a target** — classes, structs, and even primitives "
"(`impl MyTrait for i32` registers like any other impl). Traits may be "
"generic (`Wrap<T>`, `Iterator<E>`); each instantiation has its own identity "
"and its own method slots, and an impl may be parameterized by the target's "
"own type parameters — `impl Encode<T> for Store<T>` registers a template "
"that serves every instantiation, unless a concrete impl shadows it."
msgstr "**任何名义类型都可以作为目标**——类、结构体，甚至原始类型（`impl MyTrait for i32` 像其他 impl 一样注册）。trait 可以是泛型的（`Wrap<T>`、`Iterator<E>`）；每个实例化都有自己的身份和自己的方法槽位，而且 impl 可以由目标自身的类型参数参数化——`impl Encode<T> for Store<T>` 注册的是一个服务所有实例化的模板，除非某个具体 impl 将其遮蔽。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:61
msgid ""
"Type bodies are **fields only** — a `fn` inside a `struct` or `class` body "
"is a parse error. Every method, inherent or trait, lives in an impl block."
msgstr "类型体**只放字段**——`struct` 或 `class` 体内出现 `fn` 是解析错误。每个方法，无论固有还是 trait，都住在 impl 块里。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:65
msgid "Trait-typed values"
msgstr "trait 类型的值"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:67
msgid ""
"A trait name in type position is the bare name — there is no object-type "
"keyword:"
msgstr "类型位置上的 trait 名就是裸名字——没有对象类型关键字："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:70
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"struct UnitSquare { side: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159265358979 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for UnitSquare {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.side * self.side; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Canvas { log: Logger }\n"
"\n"
"impl Canvas {\n"
"    fn render(self, a: f64) { self.log.info(f\"blitted a shape of area "
"{a}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn blit(g: Canvas, s: Shape) { g.render(s.area()); }   // a parameter over "
"any Shape\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"shapes\");\n"
"    let g = Canvas { log: log };\n"
"    let mut mixed: Vec<Shape> = Vec.new();   // heterogeneous storage\n"
"    mixed.push(Circle { r: 1.0 });\n"
"    mixed.push(UnitSquare { side: 2.0 });\n"
"    for (let s of mixed) { blit(g, s); }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use pouch::{ Vec };\n"
"\n"
"trait Shape {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Circle { r: f64 }\n"
"struct UnitSquare { side: f64 }\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for Circle {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return 3.14159265358979 * self.r * self.r; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Shape for UnitSquare {\n"
"    fn area(self) -> f64 { return self.side * self.side; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"struct Canvas { log: Logger }\n"
"\n"
"impl Canvas {\n"
"    fn render(self, a: f64) { self.log.info(f\"blitted a shape of area "
"{a}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn blit(g: Canvas, s: Shape) { g.render(s.area()); }   // a parameter over "
"any Shape\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"shapes\");\n"
"    let g = Canvas { log: log };\n"
"    let mut mixed: Vec<Shape> = Vec.new();   // heterogeneous storage\n"
"    mixed.push(Circle { r: 1.0 });\n"
"    mixed.push(UnitSquare { side: 2.0 });\n"
"    for (let s of mixed) { blit(g, s); }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:112
msgid ""
"A trait-typed value is a reference to a real cell that still carries its "
"exact class. Widening a concrete value to a trait it implements is implicit "
"on assignment and argument passing, allocates nothing, and is gated by "
"exactly one question: does the registry hold an `impl I for T`? There is no "
"top type to widen to, and intersection types (`A & B`) are ruled out by "
"design — when you need both contracts, declare a trait that spells both."
msgstr "trait 类型的值是指向真实单元的引用，而且仍携带其确切的类。把具体值宽化到它实现的某个 trait，在赋值和传参时隐式发生，不分配任何东西，只受一个问题把守：注册表里有没有 `impl I for T`？没有可宽化的顶类型，交集类型（`A & B`）也被设计排除——当你同时需要两份契约时，就声明一个把两者都写明的 trait。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:120
msgid "Dispatch: the two-rule law"
msgstr "分派：两条规则的法则"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:122
msgid ""
"Every method call compiles under one of exactly two rules, fixed at compile "
"time as a property of the _call site_:"
msgstr "每个方法调用都恰好按两条规则之一编译，编译期即固定，是_调用点_的属性："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:125
msgid ""
"**Static** — the call site names exactly one concrete type. The call binds "
"directly to that type's method, no table involved:"
msgstr "**静态**——调用点指名恰好一个具体类型。调用直接绑定到该类型的方法，不涉及任何表："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:127
msgid "a concrete receiver (`c.area()` on `c: Circle`);"
msgstr "具体接收者（`c: Circle` 上的 `c.area()`）；"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:128
msgid ""
"a trait-typed local whose single concrete origin the compiler tracked (`let "
"d: Shape = Point { .. }; d.area()`);"
msgstr "编译器跟踪到唯一具体来源的 trait 类型局部变量（`let d: Shape = Point { .. }; d.area()`）；"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:130
msgid ""
"a trait-typed _parameter_ — the function specializes per concrete argument "
"at monomorphization, so a trait parameter is effectively an implicit generic "
"bound;"
msgstr "trait 类型的_参数_——函数在单态化时按具体实参特化，所以 trait 参数实际上是一个隐式的泛型约束；"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:133
msgid "inside monomorphized generics."
msgstr "单态化的泛型内部。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:134
msgid ""
"**Vtable** — the receiver is trait-typed with multiple possible concrete "
"origins:"
msgstr "**vtable**——接收者是 trait 类型，且可能有多个具体来源："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:136
msgid "elements of a heterogeneous container (`Vec<Shape>`);"
msgstr "异构容器的元素（`Vec<Shape>`）；"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:137
msgid "trait-typed field and element loads (the cell may hold any implementor);"
msgstr "trait 类型的字段与元素加载（单元里可能装着任何实现者）；"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:139
msgid ""
"branch-merged bindings (`if` arms carrying different concretes into one "
"trait-typed variable)."
msgstr "分支合并的绑定（`if` 各分支把不同的具体类型汇入同一个 trait 类型变量）。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:142
msgid ""
"The origin analysis is conservative: any merge, indirection, or "
"cross-function flow counts as multiple. Mis-analysis cannot produce wrong "
"code — an uncertain origin costs one vtable hop, never a wrong static bind. "
"And the same descriptor that answers vtable calls answers `is` probes: one "
"runtime truth per value."
msgstr "来源分析是保守的：任何合并、间接或跨函数流动都按\"多个\"计。误判不会产生错误代码——来源不确定的代价只是一次 vtable 跳转，绝不会错误地静态绑定。而回答 vtable 调用的描述符同样回答 `is` 探测：每个值只有一份运行时事实。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:148
msgid "Type tests"
msgstr "类型测试"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:150
msgid ""
"`expr is Type` yields a `bool` and is total — it never traps. Two probes, "
"one keyword:"
msgstr "`expr is Type` 产出 `bool` 且是全函数——它从不触发陷阱。两个探测，一个关键字："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:153
msgid ""
"**Concrete RHS**: is the value's exact type `T`? (No inheritance — a single "
"id compare.)"
msgstr "**具体类型右侧**：值的确切类型是不是 `T`？（没有继承——一次单独的 id 比较。）"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:155
msgid ""
"**Trait RHS**: does the value's exact type have a registered impl? A "
"capability probe, usable on any value (`k is Hashable`)."
msgstr "**trait 右侧**：值的确切类型有没有注册 impl？这是一次能力探测，可用于任何值（`k is Hashable`）。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:158
msgid ""
"`is` has no flow-sensitive effects: a true probe does not narrow `x`. When "
"the static type already answers, the probe folds at compile time. "
"Trait-typed values cannot be downcast to a concrete type at all — if you "
"need `Circle`\\-specific behavior behind a `Drawable`, put that behavior in "
"the trait. The one recovery path for erased values is the explicit `opaque` "
"box (see the reference on [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md))."
msgstr "`is` 没有流敏感效应：探测为真不会收窄 `x`。当静态类型已能作答时，探测在编译期折叠。trait 类型的值完全不能向下转型到具体类型——如果你需要在 `Drawable` 背后做 `Circle`\\-特定的行为，就把那个行为放进 trait。被擦除的值唯一的恢复路径是显式的 `opaque` 盒（见关于 [`opaque`](../reference/opaque.md) 的参考章节）。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:166
msgid "Visibility: the use-both gate"
msgstr "可见性：use 双侧闸门"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:168
msgid ""
"Calling a trait method requires **both** names in scope: the type (by "
"declaration or `use`) _and_ the trait (`use`). Inherent methods need only "
"the type. A call that matches a registered impl whose trait no `use` brings "
"in is an error — \"use `I` to call its methods on `T`\" — so an added trait "
"method can never silently change what someone else's call site means."
msgstr "调用 trait 方法要求**两个**名字都在作用域内：类型（靠声明或 `use`）_以及_ trait（靠 `use`）。固有方法只要类型在即可。如果一次调用匹配到某个已注册 impl，但其 trait 没有被任何 `use` 引入，就是错误——\"use `I` 才能在 `T` 上调用它的方法\"——因此新增一个 trait 方法永远不可能悄悄改变别人调用点的含义。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:175 src/reference/traits.md:167
msgid "The iteration protocol"
msgstr "迭代协议"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:177
msgid "A type is iterable when it implements the builtin `Iterator<E>` trait:"
msgstr "类型实现了内置的 `Iterator<E>` trait 即可迭代："

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:179
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class CountUp {\n"
"    n: i32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {\n"
"    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {\n"
"        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {\n"
"            if (!emit(i)) { return; }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");\n"
"    for (let v of CountUp { n: 3 }) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"tick {v}\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"done\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class CountUp {\n"
"    n: i32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Iterator<i32> for CountUp {\n"
"    fn __iterate(self, emit: fn(i32) -> bool) {\n"
"        for (let i = 1; i <= self.n; i += 1) {\n"
"            if (!emit(i)) { return; }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"iter\");\n"
"    for (let v of CountUp { n: 3 }) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"tick {v}\");\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(\"done\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:210
msgid ""
"`for (let v of it) { body }` desugars to `it.__iterate(emit)` with a "
"synthetic closure: the body runs, then `emit` returns `true`; `break` "
"returns `false`. The loop variable is the closure's parameter — a fresh "
"binding per iteration by construction. The builtin sequences (`[T]`, `str`, "
"`bytes`, and the standard growable `Vec`) keep fused index loops instead; "
"they never pay a per-element call."
msgstr "`for (let v of it) { body }` 会脱糖为带合成闭包的 `it.__iterate(emit)`：先跑循环体，然后 `emit` 返回 `true`；`break` 则返回 `false`。循环变量是闭包的参数——按构造每轮迭代都是全新绑定。内置序列（`[T]`、`str`、`bytes` 以及标准的可增长 `Vec`）则保留融合的索引循环；它们从不为每个元素付一次调用。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:217
msgid "Engine contracts are traits too"
msgstr "引擎契约也是 trait"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:219
msgid ""
"The async machinery is spelled as builtin traits — `Future<T>` and "
"`RunContext` — which the engine _names_ but does not close: a hand-written "
"type can `impl Future<nil> for MyFuture` through the same registry as any "
"other impl and be driven by the same loop. See [the async "
"model](async-model.md) and the worked example in [04 — Custom "
"async](../examples/04-custom-async.md)."
msgstr "异步机制写成内置 trait——`Future<T>` 与 `RunContext`——引擎_命名_它们但不封闭它们：手写的类型可以像任何其他 impl 一样，通过同一个注册表写下 `impl Future<nil> for MyFuture`，被同一个循环驱动。参见[异步模型](async-model.md)以及[04 — 自定义异步](../examples/04-custom-async.md)中的完整示例。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:226
msgid "Equality is not a trait"
msgstr "相等不是 trait"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:228
msgid ""
"`==` is builtin and cannot be opted into or out of: primitives compare by "
"value, `str`/`bytes` by content, everything else by cell identity. "
"Field-wise comparison is a loop you write, or the map packages' own key "
"rules. See [everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)."
msgstr "`==` 是内置的，不能选择加入或退出：原始类型按值比较，`str`/`bytes` 按内容，其余一切按单元身份。逐字段比较是你自己写的循环，或者 map 包自带的键规则。参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:235
msgid ""
"**Nominal satisfaction** keeps the registry exact: capability probes, "
"widening, and vtable fills all read one table, so casts stay cheap and "
"runtime identities stay meaningful."
msgstr "**名义满足**让注册表保持精确：能力探测、宽化、vtable 填充读取的都是同一张表，因此转型保持廉价，运行时身份保持有意义。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:238
msgid ""
"**The two-rule law** makes dispatch predictable: you can tell, per call "
"site, whether you are paying a hop."
msgstr "**两条规则的法则**让分派可预测：对每个调用点，你都能说出自己是否在付一次跳转的钱。"

#: src/core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md:240
msgid ""
"**Placement rules** keep coherence decidable across packages without a "
"global uniqueness proof — one of the pair is always local."
msgstr "**放置规则**让跨包的连贯性可判定，无需全局唯一性证明——组合中总有一侧是本地的。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's concurrency is **pull-based**, built on one noun: `Future<T>`. Calling "
"an `async fn` runs nothing — it produces a cold future. The future runs when "
"something _drives_ it: an `await` inside another async fn, or a launch into "
"the VM's queue. There are no promises, no microtask queue, and no implicit "
"scheduling: **the host owns time**, and nothing runs unless the driving loop "
"runs it."
msgstr "rut 的并发是**拉取式**的，建立在一个名词之上：`Future<T>`。调用 `async fn` 什么也不运行——它产出一个冷 future。future 在有什么东西_驱动_它时才运行：另一个 async fn 里的 `await`，或一次进入 VM 队列的启动。没有 promise，没有微任务队列，没有隐式调度：**时间归宿主所有**，驱动循环不运行它，它就不运行。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:10
msgid "Pull, not push"
msgstr "拉取，而非推送"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:12
msgid "push (promises)"
msgstr "推（promise）"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:12
msgid "pull (rut futures)"
msgstr "拉（rut future）"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14 src/reference/async.md:12
msgid "created"
msgstr "创建时机"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14
msgid "starts on the next microtask"
msgstr "在下一个微任务启动"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:14
msgid "cold — nothing runs until awaited or launched"
msgstr "冷——被 await 或被启动之前什么都不运行"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:15
msgid "idle cost"
msgstr "空闲开销"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:15
msgid "reactions and queues exist whether or not anyone waits"
msgstr "无论有没有人等待，反应与队列都存在"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:15 src/reference/async.md:13
msgid "nobody drives ⇒ nobody pays"
msgstr "无人驱动 ⇒ 无人付费"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:16
msgid "per-await allocation"
msgstr "每次 await 的分配"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:16
msgid "promise + callback lists"
msgstr "promise + 回调列表"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:16
msgid "one hidden frame record per call"
msgstr "每次调用一个隐藏帧记录"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:17 src/reference/async.md:15
msgid "cancellation"
msgstr "取消"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:17
msgid "abort flags layered on top"
msgstr "叠加上去的中止标志"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:17
msgid "native: the frame is dropped at a checkpoint"
msgstr "原生：帧在检查点被丢弃"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:18 src/reference/async.md:16
msgid "host integration"
msgstr "宿主集成"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:18 src/reference/async.md:16
msgid "the host must drain a job queue"
msgstr "宿主必须排空作业队列"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:18
msgid "the host polls: drain ready frames, ask for the next deadline"
msgstr "宿主做 poll：排空就绪帧，询问下一个截止时间"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:20 src/reference/opaque.md:9
msgid "The surface"
msgstr "语言表面"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:22
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use async_host::{ launch_future, sleep };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) -> nil {\n"
"    for (let i = n; i > 0; i -= 1) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(1000);             // the only suspension spelling\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() -> nil {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"countdown\");\n"
"    launch_future(countdown(log, 3));  // the other consume: launch\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use async_host::{ launch_future, sleep };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"async fn countdown(cx: RunContext, log: Logger, n: u32) -> nil {\n"
"    for (let i = n; i > 0; i -= 1) {\n"
"        log.info(f\"{i}\");\n"
"        await sleep(1000);             // the only suspension spelling\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() -> nil {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"countdown\");\n"
"    launch_future(countdown(log, 3));  // the other consume: launch\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:45
msgid "The rules:"
msgstr "规则如下："

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:47
msgid ""
"**The first parameter is the context.** `async fn f(cx: RunContext, ..)` — "
"the engine mints it at call sites and per drive, the way it mints `self`. It "
"carries the frame edge: `checkpoint()` reads the resume state, `cancelled()` "
"reads the task's abort flag."
msgstr "**第一个参数是上下文。**`async fn f(cx: RunContext, ..)`——引擎在调用点、每次驱动时铸造它，如同铸造 `self`。它携带帧的边沿：`checkpoint()` 读取恢复状态，`cancelled()` 读取任务的中止标志。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:51
msgid ""
"**Calling does not run.** `async fn f(..) -> T` describes a value that "
"widens to `Future<T>`; it runs when awaited or launched."
msgstr "**调用不等于运行。**`async fn f(..) -> T` 描述的是一个宽化为 `Future<T>` 的值；它只在被 await 或被启动时运行。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:53
msgid ""
"**One consume law.** A future is consumed by `await` _or_ by `launch_future` "
"— exactly one. The launch returns its own receipt type, which is not a "
"future and cannot be launched or awaited again."
msgstr "**单次消费法则。**future 只由 `await` _或_ `launch_future` 消费——恰好其一。启动返回它自己的回执类型，它不是 future，不能再次被启动或 await。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:56
msgid ""
"**`await` targets engine-woven futures** (async-fn results and `sleep`). "
"Hand-written futures are _launcher-drivable_ — the driving loop finds their "
"`Future::yield` in the vtable — which is how the standard `sleep` itself is "
"built over the open trait surface."
msgstr "**`await` 只面向引擎织入的 future**（async fn 的结果与 `sleep`）。手写的 future 是_可被启动器驱动_的——驱动循环在 vtable 里找到它们的 `Future::yield`——标准 `sleep` 本身正是构建在这个开放的 trait 表面之上。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:61 src/reference/async.md:109
msgid "What the compiler emits"
msgstr "编译器产出什么"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:63
msgid ""
"An `async fn` compiles to one hidden frame — an ordinary heap cell — with a "
"woven `Future::yield` that the driving loop calls once per resumption:"
msgstr "`async fn` 编译为一个隐藏帧——一个普通的堆单元——带一个织入的 `Future::yield`，驱动循环在每次恢复时调用它一次："

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:81
msgid ""
"The state field _is_ the program counter: resume dispatch is a jump table "
"over the checkpoint enum. Because locals are mirrored into the frame cell, "
"parking releases only staging registers and no liveness analysis decides "
"which locals survive a suspension. The whole weave rides existing bytecode — "
"no new opcodes, no new runtime machinery."
msgstr "state 字段_就是_程序计数器：恢复分派是检查点枚举上的一张跳转表。由于局部变量被镜像进帧单元，停车只释放暂存寄存器，没有任何活跃性分析来决定哪些局部变量能在暂停中幸存。整个织造骑在既有字节码上——没有新操作码，没有新运行时机制。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:87
msgid "Cancellation is drop"
msgstr "取消即 drop"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:89
msgid ""
"`handle.abort()` flags the frame's cancellation and re-enqueues it. The "
"probe at its next checkpoint branches to the drop path: locals release in "
"reverse binding order, `on_drop` callbacks fire by refcount, and any pending "
"`sleep` dies with the frame. Cancellation **never interrupts "
"mid-expression** — the checkpoint probe is the only place a cancellation "
"becomes observable, so a cancelled function dies at a known-clean boundary. "
"This is the same machinery that frees any heap object (see "
"[memory](memory.md)); coroutine frames get no special case."
msgstr "`handle.abort()` 标记帧的取消并将其重新入队。下一个检查点处的探测会分支到 drop 路径：局部变量按绑定的逆序释放，`on_drop` 回调按引用计数触发，任何挂起的 `sleep` 随帧一同消亡。取消**从不在表达式中途打断**——检查点探测是取消变得可观察的唯一位置，所以被取消的函数死在一个已知干净的边界上。这与释放任何堆对象用的是同一套机制（参见[内存](memory.md)）；协程帧没有特权。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:98 src/reference/async.md:140
msgid "The driving loop"
msgstr "驱动循环"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:100
msgid "The VM owns the queues; the embedder owns the loop:"
msgstr "队列归 VM 所有；循环归嵌入方所有："

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:103 src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:30
#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:98 src/reference/resource-limits.md:58
#: src/reference/host-futures.md:108
msgid "\"main\""
msgstr "\"main\""

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:103
msgid "// script boots, launches futures\n"
msgstr "// 脚本启动，发起 future\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:105
msgid "// one drive per ready frame\n"
msgstr "// 每个就绪帧驱动一次\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:106
msgid "// expire due timers into ready\n"
msgstr "// 把到期定时器转入就绪\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:107
msgid "// the wall-clock stand-in\n"
msgstr "// 墙钟的替身\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:109
msgid "// idle\n"
msgstr "// 空闲\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:113
msgid ""
"`sleep(ms)` arms a deadline on the VM's **virtual clock** (`vm.now_ms()` / "
"`vm.set_now()`). A test host advances the clock by hand and gets fully "
"deterministic schedules — a UI host just maps it to wall time."
msgstr "`sleep(ms)` 在 VM 的**虚拟时钟**（`vm.now_ms()` / `vm.set_now()`）上设一个截止时间。测试宿主手动推进时钟，得到完全确定性的调度——UI 宿主只需把它映射到墙钟时间。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:117
msgid ""
"Each queue entry owns one reference; a completed drive re-enqueues the "
"awaiting frame through a one-directional edge pair, so wake wiring never "
"forms a cycle."
msgstr "每个队列条目持有一个引用；一次完成的驱动通过单向边对把等待中的帧重新入队，因此唤醒连线永远不会形成循环引用。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:120
msgid ""
"Fuel accounting rides the ordinary per-op budget: a drive that runs out "
"parks the frame at its checkpoint and resumes there later."
msgstr "燃料核算走普通的每操作预算：燃料耗尽的驱动把帧停在它的检查点上，稍后从那里恢复。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:123
msgid "Host futures: `pub host async fn`"
msgstr "宿主 future：`pub host async fn`"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:125
msgid "Native code joins the same model. A declaration file spells the row:"
msgstr "原生代码加入同一个模型。声明文件写下这样一行："

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:133
msgid ""
"and the embedder binds it with **one closure** that starts the work and "
"returns the future's state cell:"
msgstr "嵌入方用**一个闭包**绑定它：闭包启动工作并返回 future 的状态单元："

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:137
msgid "\"http_host::http_stream_next\""
msgstr "\"http_host::http_stream_next\""

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:143
msgid "// settle from any thread\n"
msgstr "// 从任意线程落定\n"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:149
msgid ""
"`Completer<T>` is a small shared cell: `complete(v)`/`fail(msg)` are "
"callable from any thread (atomics plus a mutex — the VM stays "
"single-threaded), `fail`'s message becomes the trap **at the await**, and an "
"optional abort closure runs when the script cancels a pending future (late "
"results are then simply discarded). The macro registers the whole row family "
"the weave drives — start, probe, take, cancel — and the load-time check "
"verifies the expansion against the declaration, so a decl and its bodies "
"cannot drift apart. IO written with plain `async`/`await` Rust maps onto "
"this naturally: the work leaves the VM, and completion is one enqueue back "
"into the ready queue."
msgstr "`Completer<T>` 是一个小的共享单元：`complete(v)`/`fail(msg)` 可从任意线程调用（原子操作加互斥锁——VM 保持单线程），`fail` 的消息**在 await 处**变成陷阱；当脚本取消一个挂起的 future 时，可选的中止闭包会运行（迟到的结果随后被直接丢弃）。这个宏注册织造所驱动的整行族——start、probe、take、cancel——加载期检查则对照声明校验展开结果，声明与函数体因此不可能漂移分离。用普通 `async`/`await` Rust 写的 IO 自然映射到此：工作离开 VM，完成就是一次重新入队，回到就绪队列。"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:160
msgid "Structured concurrency, honestly"
msgstr "结构化并发，如实相告"

#: src/core-concepts/async-model.md:162
msgid ""
"The language today keeps the vocabulary deliberately small: launch, abort, "
"and await. Racing (`await select { .. }`) and joining a launched future "
"(`await handle`) parse but are compile-gated — the diagnostics name them as "
"future work, and structured scopes (a block that cancels its children on "
"exit) are the same story. What exists now is already enough to structure "
"real programs — the launch/abort receipt gives you explicit ownership of "
"background work, and drop-based cancellation gives it a clean off switch — "
"but nothing in the model silently cancels siblings on your behalf. See the "
"reference on [async and await](../reference/async.md), "
"[tasks](../reference/tasks.md), and the [host futures "
"bridge](../reference/host-futures.md); the [GitHub viewer "
"CLI](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md) example shows a full program "
"living inside this loop."
msgstr "这门语言今天刻意保持很小的词汇表：launch、abort 和 await。竞速（`await select { .. }`）与 join 已启动的 future（`await handle`）能解析但被编译期闸住——诊断把它们标为未来工作，结构化作用域（一个在退出时取消其子任务的块）也是同样的情况。现有机制已足以组织真实的程序——launch/abort 回执让你对后台工作拥有显式所有权，基于 drop 的取消给了它一个干净的开关——但模型中没有任何东西会替你悄悄取消兄弟任务。参见关于[异步与 await](../reference/async.md)、[任务](../reference/tasks.md)与[宿主 future 桥](../reference/host-futures.md)的参考章节；[GitHub 查看器 CLI](../examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md) 示例展示了一个完整程序如何活在这个循环里。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:3
msgid ""
"rut's memory management is **reference counting with deterministic "
"destructors and no collector**. An object is destroyed the moment its last "
"strong reference goes away — at a knowable statement, not \"at some future "
"GC\". The cost is honesty about cycles: a strong cycle never reaches zero, "
"so it lives until the VM is torn down. rut makes that a stated rule and "
"ships `Weak<T>` as the first-class answer, instead of hiding it behind a "
"collector."
msgstr "rut 的内存管理是**引用计数加确定性析构器，没有收集器**。对象在最后一个强引用消失的那一刻被销毁——落在一条可知的语句上，而不是\"将来某次 GC\"。代价是对循环引用的如实相告：强循环引用永远不会减到零，因此它活到 VM 被拆毁为止。rut 把这一点写成明文规则，并把 `Weak<T>` 作为一等公民的答案交付，而不是把它藏在收集器背后。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:11
msgid "Everything is a cell"
msgstr "一切皆单元"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:13
msgid ""
"Every non-primitive value — strings, byte buffers, arrays, records, enums, "
"trait objects, erasure boxes, nullable boxes, coroutine frames — is a heap "
"cell. Each cell starts with a header: a refcount, a type id, and a few "
"flags. The counts are plain integers: a VM runs on one thread with one heap, "
"workers are separate VMs, and nothing is ever shared between them, so there "
"are no atomics anywhere in the heap."
msgstr "每个非原始类型的值——字符串、字节缓冲、数组、记录、枚举、trait 对象、擦除盒、可空盒、协程帧——都是一个堆单元。每个单元以一个头部开始：引用计数、类型 id 和几个标志位。计数就是普通整数：一个 VM 运行在一个线程上、拥有一套堆，worker 是彼此独立的 VM，两者之间永不共享任何东西，所以整个堆中没有任何原子操作。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:20
msgid ""
"Because assignments and passes copy _handles_, not payloads, the refcount "
"traffic is exactly the aliasing the program performs:"
msgstr "由于赋值与传参复制的是_句柄_而非载荷，引用计数的流量恰好就是程序实施的别名数量："

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:23
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node { next: ?Node }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"cells\");\n"
"    let a: ?Node = Node { next: nil };\n"
"    let b = a;              // one retain\n"
"    log.info(f\"a == b: {a == b}\");   // one cell — it dies when the LAST "
"of a, b goes away\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct Node { next: ?Node }\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"cells\");\n"
"    let a: ?Node = Node { next: nil };\n"
"    let b = a;              // one retain\n"
"    log.info(f\"a == b: {a == b}\");   // one cell — it dies when the LAST "
"of a, b goes away\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:40
msgid ""
"The compiler knows every register's static type, so it emits ref-aware moves "
"only where references flow; scalar code pays nothing. Function boundaries do "
"the paired inc/dec; a flat primitive buffer's element traffic is plain slot "
"moves."
msgstr "编译器知道每个寄存器的静态类型，因此只在引用流动之处生成引用感知的移动；标量代码分文不费。函数边界完成成对的增/减；扁平原始类型缓冲区的元素流量就是普通的槽位移动。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:45
msgid "Deterministic destruction"
msgstr "确定性析构"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:47
msgid "When a count reaches zero, destruction runs inline, in a fixed order:"
msgstr "计数归零时，析构就地运行，顺序固定："

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:49
msgid ""
"**`on_drop` cleanups are pinned.** `on_drop<T>(p: ?T, cleanup: fn(?T))` "
"attaches a cleanup to a nullable binding — and a `?T` binding _is_ the cell "
"reference, so this is \"run this when the object dies\". One callback per "
"binding; a second attach is a compile error; the pinned callbacks drain at "
"the next call boundary."
msgstr "**`on_drop` 清理是钉住的。**`on_drop<T>(p: ?T, cleanup: fn(?T))` 给一个可空绑定挂上清理函数——而 `?T` 绑定_就是_单元引用，所以这就是\"对象死亡时运行这段代码\"。每个绑定一个回调；第二次挂载是编译错误；被钉住的回调在下一次调用边界排空。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:55
msgid ""
"**Fields release in declaration order**, recursively — a dying record's "
"strings, arrays, and boxes release their own references, so nothing is "
"pinned until VM shutdown just because its owner died."
msgstr "**字段按声明顺序释放**，递归进行——垂死记录的字符串、数组和盒各自释放自己的引用，因此不会有什么仅仅因为其主人死亡就被钉到 VM 关机。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:58
msgid ""
"**Host opaques run their Rust `Drop` at the same point.** A host handle "
"registered by the embedder releases its socket, texture, or thread when the "
"last script reference disappears — never \"someday at GC\" (see [the host "
"boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr "**宿主 opaque 在同一时点运行它们的 Rust `Drop`。**嵌入方注册的宿主句柄在最后一个脚本引用消失时释放它的套接字、纹理或线程——绝不是\"GC 某天\"（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:63
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Connection {\n"
"    url: str;\n"
"    log: Logger;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Connection {\n"
"    fn open(url: str, log: Logger) -> Connection {\n"
"        return Connection { url: url, log: log };\n"
"    }\n"
"    fn close(self) { self.log.info(f\"closed {self.url}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let conn: ?Connection = Connection.open(\"tcp://edge\", log);\n"
"    on_drop(conn, fn(c: ?Connection) { c.close(); });\n"
"    log.info(\"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Connection {\n"
"    url: str;\n"
"    log: Logger;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl Connection {\n"
"    fn open(url: str, log: Logger) -> Connection {\n"
"        return Connection { url: url, log: log };\n"
"    }\n"
"    fn close(self) { self.log.info(f\"closed {self.url}\"); }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let conn: ?Connection = Connection.open(\"tcp://edge\", log);\n"
"    on_drop(conn, fn(c: ?Connection) { c.close(); });\n"
"    log.info(\"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:86
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\n"
"closed tcp://edge\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"main is done — the count hits zero at the boundary\n"
"closed tcp://edge\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:91
msgid ""
"Compare this with finalizer-based designs: there is no finalizer that \"may "
"run later or never\", no flush phase, and no resource whose release time you "
"cannot point at in your own code."
msgstr "与基于 finalizer 的设计比较一下：没有\"可能晚点运行或永远不运行\"的 finalizer，没有冲刷阶段，也没有任何释放时间在你自己的代码里指不出来对的资源。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:95
msgid "Two edge rules worth knowing:"
msgstr "两条值得知道的边界规则："

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:97
msgid ""
"**Refcount overflow pins.** If a counter would exceed its maximum, the "
"object is deliberately immortalized (and logged) rather than wrapping — the "
"same rule Swift uses."
msgstr "**引用计数溢出即钉死。**如果某个计数器即将超过最大值，对象会被刻意永生化（并记入日志），而不是回绕——Swift 用的也是同一条规则。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:100
msgid ""
"**Weak boxes null first.** When a cell with weak watchers dies, every `Weak` "
"box to it is nulled _before_ any user code runs — a cleanup that calls "
"`upgrade()` sees `nil`, deterministically."
msgstr "**弱盒先置空。**当一个有弱观察者的单元死亡时，指向它的每个 `Weak` 盒会在_任何_用户代码运行之前被置空——调用 `upgrade()` 的清理函数确定性地看到 `nil`。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:104 src/reference/rc-dispose-identity.md:49
msgid "Weak references"
msgstr "弱引用"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:106
msgid ""
"`Weak(v)` mints a `Weak<T>` over `v`'s cell that **never keeps anything "
"alive**; `w.upgrade()` answers `?T` — the retained referent, or `nil` once "
"it died. Construction is a call of the type name, admission is checked "
"(reference types only — `Weak<i32>` diagnoses), and `weak(nil)` traps."
msgstr "`Weak(v)` 在 `v` 的单元上铸造一个 `Weak<T>`，它**永远不让任何东西保活**；`w.upgrade()` 回答 `?T`——被保留的引用对象，或它死掉之后的 `nil`。构造就是调用类型名，准入受检查（仅限引用类型——`Weak<i32>` 会被诊断），`weak(nil)` 触发陷阱。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:112
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Model {\n"
"    name: str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class View {\n"
"    model: ?Model;\n"
"    observer: ?Weak<Model>;      // a back-pointer that closes no cycle\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let mut m = Model { name: \"doc\" };\n"
"    let v = View { model: nil, observer: Weak(m) };   // observe without "
"owning\n"
"    log.info(f\"holding {m.name}; the view holds only a weak edge\");\n"
"    m = Model { name: \"next\" };   // the old cell's last strong reference "
"dies here\n"
"    log.info(f\"upgrade() answers nil: {v.observer.upgrade() == nil}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"class Model {\n"
"    name: str;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"class View {\n"
"    model: ?Model;\n"
"    observer: ?Weak<Model>;      // a back-pointer that closes no cycle\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"rc\");\n"
"    let mut m = Model { name: \"doc\" };\n"
"    let v = View { model: nil, observer: Weak(m) };   // observe without "
"owning\n"
"    log.info(f\"holding {m.name}; the view holds only a weak edge\");\n"
"    m = Model { name: \"next\" };   // the old cell's last strong reference "
"dies here\n"
"    log.info(f\"upgrade() answers nil: {v.observer.upgrade() == nil}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:139
msgid ""
"The two shapes that cause accidental cycles — **back-pointers** (child → "
"parent) and **caches** (a table that should not extend lifetimes) — are "
"exactly what `Weak` is for. A path through a `Weak` does not close a strong "
"cycle."
msgstr "造成意外循环引用的两种形状——**回指指针**（child → parent）与**缓存**（不该延长生命周期的表）——恰好就是 `Weak` 的用武之地。经过 `Weak` 的路径不会闭合强循环引用。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:144
msgid "The cycle policy"
msgstr "循环引用策略"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:146
msgid ""
"**A strong cycle is a leak — deterministically.** Its members live until the "
"VM is dropped; no collector ever runs, no pass interrupts execution, and "
"destructor ordering never surprises you. Guidance is lint-level, not runtime:"
msgstr "**强循环引用就是泄漏——确定性的泄漏。**它的成员活到 VM 被 drop 为止；收集器从不运行，没有任何阶段会打断执行，析构顺序也从不让你意外。指导是 lint 级的，不是运行时的："

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:151
msgid ""
"resource-holding types (things with `on_drop` cleanups or host handles) must "
"not participate in strong cycles;"
msgstr "持有资源的类型（带 `on_drop` 清理或宿主句柄的东西）不得参与强循环引用；"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:153
msgid "parent/child and observer shapes take `Weak` back-pointers;"
msgstr "父/子与观察者形状采用 `Weak` 回指指针；"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:154
msgid "pure-data cycles are harmless — they cost only memory."
msgstr "纯数据的循环引用无害——它们只花费内存。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:156
msgid ""
"You are not left alone with the rule: debug builds assert refcount "
"discipline (retain/release pairing, no underflow, no double free), and at "
"teardown the VM emits a **leak report** — surviving objects grouped by type "
"with allocation sites — which is the primary tool for hunting accidental "
"cycles. Behavior is fully deterministic, so a leak reproduces exactly."
msgstr "这条规则并非让你独自面对：调试构建会断言引用计数纪律（保留/释放配对、无下溢、无双重释放），而 VM 在拆除时会输出一份**泄漏报告**——按类型分组、带分配位置的存活对象清单——它是猎捕意外循环引用的首要工具。行为完全确定，因此泄漏可以精确复现。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:163
msgid "The self-managed heap"
msgstr "自管堆"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:165
msgid ""
"Host code may use `std` freely, but every byte backing a rut value is "
"allocated through the VM's own heap manager. The discipline is the point, "
"not the allocator:"
msgstr "宿主代码可以随意使用 `std`，但支撑 rut 值的每一个字节都经由 VM 自己的堆管理器分配。要点在纪律，而不在分配器："

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:169
msgid ""
"**Cells** come from fixed-size arena chunks with freelists; a dead slot is "
"reused by the next mint."
msgstr "**单元**来自带空闲列表的定长 arena 块；死槽位会被下一次铸造复用。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:171
msgid ""
"**Variable-size payloads** (string octets, array element runs) live in "
"size-classed blocks that never move; in-place geometric growth keeps append "
"loops linear, and freelists recycle the common sizes."
msgstr "**可变尺寸载荷**（字符串字节、数组元素段）住在按尺寸分级的块里，永不移动；就地几何增长让追加循环保持线性，空闲列表回收常见尺寸。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:174
msgid ""
"**Immortal singletons** — interned string literals, enum variants — live in "
"a slab freed only at VM drop, carrying the \"no refcount\" sentinel."
msgstr "**不朽单例**——驻留的字符串字面量、枚举成员——住在只在 VM drop 时释放的 slab 里，携带\"无引用计数\"哨兵。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:177
msgid ""
"**Nothing compacts.** The heap never moves cells, which is precisely what "
"lets the boundary hand Rust zero-copy views into buffers (see [the host "
"boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr "**永不压缩。**堆从不移动单元，这正是边界能把指向缓冲区的零拷贝视图交到 Rust 手里的原因（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:181
msgid "Why self-manage instead of using the host's allocator?"
msgstr "为什么自管，而不用宿主的分配器？"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:183
msgid ""
"**Budgets.** An embedder can say \"this script gets N bytes\" and get a "
"clean, resumable out-of-memory trap instead of an OS abort. "
"`vm.heap_usage()` is exact because every allocation is accounted."
msgstr "**预算。**嵌入方可以说\"这个脚本只有 N 字节\"，然后得到一个干净、可恢复的内存耗尽陷阱，而不是操作系统级的中止。`vm.heap_usage()` 是精确的，因为每次分配都被记账。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:186
msgid ""
"**Teardown.** `Vm::drop` frees the whole heap in slab units after the leak "
"report; nothing per-object leaks past the VM — important for wasm pages and "
"plugin hosts that spawn and kill scripts."
msgstr "**拆除。**`Vm::drop` 在泄漏报告之后按 slab 单位释放整个堆；没有任何按对象的东西泄漏出 VM 之外——这对会反复生成、杀掉脚本的 wasm 页面和插件宿主很重要。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:189
msgid ""
"**Leak reporting** walks the VM's own headers, which requires the VM's own "
"headers everywhere."
msgstr "**泄漏报告**遍历的是 VM 自己的头部，这要求处处都是 VM 自己的头部。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:192
msgid ""
"The budget check runs _before_ any write — a failed allocation leaves the "
"heap byte-identical — and traps resumably: raise the limit and continue, or "
"drop references and retry. See the reference on [resource "
"limits](../reference/resource-limits.md) for the full knob set, and [the "
"bytecode VM](the-vm.md) for how budgets interleave with execution."
msgstr "预算检查在任何写入_之前_运行——失败的分配让堆保持逐字节相同——而且陷阱可恢复：调高限额继续，或者丢掉引用再试。完整的旋钮清单见关于[资源限制](../reference/resource-limits.md)的参考章节；预算如何与执行交织，见[字节码 VM](the-vm.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:201
msgid ""
"**Deterministic resource release** — the property the whole design is "
"organized around. If your script opened something, the closing statement is "
"knowable."
msgstr "**确定性的资源释放**——整个设计围绕它组织。如果你的脚本打开了什么，关闭它的语句是可知的。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:204
msgid ""
"**No pauses.** There is no collection pass; destruction happens inline at "
"release-to-zero, so nothing ever interrupts a frame."
msgstr "**没有停顿。**没有收集阶段；析构在计数释放到零时就地发生，所以没有任何东西会打断一帧。"

#: src/core-concepts/memory.md:206
msgid ""
"**A small, honest mental model.** Sharing is by reference, copies are built "
"explicitly (see [everything is a value](everything-is-a-value.md)), "
"lifetimes are refcounts, and the one thing refcounts cannot do — cycles — is "
"a documented rule with a first-class tool."
msgstr "**一个小而诚实的心智模型。**共享靠引用，副本靠显式构建（参见[一切皆值](everything-is-a-value.md)），生命周期就是引用计数，而引用计数唯一做不到的事——循环引用——是一条成文规则配一件一等工具。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:3
msgid ""
"rut exists to be embedded. The host — a Rust program — owns a VM, declares "
"its API once in rut source, binds the implementations with typed Rust "
"closures, and drives everything. The design rule for the whole boundary: "
"**the type system does the checking, not your bridge code.** There is no "
"argument re-parsing, no `as number`, no \"trust-me\" coercion — a value "
"crossing either direction is checked against a reified runtime type, and a "
"mismatch is a loud error naming both sides."
msgstr "rut 生而为嵌入。宿主——一个 Rust 程序——拥有一台 VM，在 rut 源码里一次性声明自己的 API，用带类型的 Rust 闭包绑定实现，然后驱动一切。整个边界的设计规则：**做检查的是类型系统，而不是你的桥接代码。**没有实参重新解析，没有 `as number`，没有\"信我\"式强转——双向跨越的值都对照具体化运行时类型检查，不匹配就是一个点名双方的响亮错误。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:12
msgid "The embedding model"
msgstr "嵌入模型"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:17
msgid "\"app:gfx\""
msgstr "\"app:gfx\""

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:17
msgid "\"gfx.d.rut\""
msgstr "\"gfx.d.rut\""

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:21
msgid "\"app:gfx::newCanvas\""
msgstr "\"app:gfx::newCanvas\""

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:24
msgid ""
"// the join: every declared row must have a binding, and vice versa —\n"
"// verified BEFORE any script runs\n"
msgstr "// 接合：每一条声明的行都必须有绑定，反之亦然——\n// 在任何脚本运行之前校验\n"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:30
msgid "// an entry point\n"
msgstr "// 一个入口点\n"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:31
msgid "// drive async work to idle\n"
msgstr "// 把异步工作驱动到空闲\n"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:34
msgid "The declaration file (a _host package_) spells the surface in rut:"
msgstr "声明文件（一个_宿主包_）用 rut 写下接口："

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:41
msgid ""
"and the load-time join rejects three wiring bugs as panics — an embedder "
"mistake, never a script diagnostic: a declared row with no binding, a "
"binding with no declaration, and signature drift. \"Mount what you bind\": "
"an embedder that mounts a package declares its rows and must bind them."
msgstr "加载期接合会把三种接线错误当作 panic 拒绝——那是嵌入方的失误，绝不是脚本诊断：声明了行却没有绑定、有绑定却没有声明，以及签名漂移。\"挂载什么就绑定什么\"：挂载一个包的嵌入方声明了它的行，就必须绑定它们。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:47 src/reference/value-boundary.md:10
msgid "The crossing set"
msgstr "可跨越集合"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:49
msgid ""
"What may cross is a **compile-time property of the surface**, not a runtime "
"negotiation:"
msgstr "什么可以跨越，是**接口的编译期属性**，不是运行时协商："

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:52
msgid "**Parameters**: the primitives, `str`, `bytes`, and `opaque`."
msgstr "**参数**：原始类型、`str`、`bytes` 与 `opaque`。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:53
msgid ""
"**Returns**: the same set _plus_ the answer optionals `?str`, `?bytes`, "
"`?opaque` — `Option<String>`, `Option<Vec<u8>>`, and the opaque handles mint "
"the nullable box, with `None` as the flat `nil`."
msgstr "**返回**：同一个集合_加上_应答可空类型 `?str`、`?bytes`、`?opaque`——`Option<String>`、`Option<Vec<u8>>` 与 opaque 句柄会铸造可空盒，`None` 就是扁平的 `nil`。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:56
msgid ""
"**Tuples** cross field by field, which makes the error convention — `(value, "
"err)` — a first-class entry answer. The two channels stay distinct by law: a "
"_returned_ `err` is data the host reads and acts on; a _panic_ is drift and "
"arrives on the trap channel, never filling an err field."
msgstr "**对偶**逐字段跨越，这让错误约定——`(value, err)`——成为一等公民的入口应答。两条通道依律保持区分：_返回的_ `err` 是宿主读取并处置的数据；_panic_ 是漂移，走陷阱通道抵达，绝不会填进 err 字段。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:62
msgid ""
"Everything else — user structs and classes, `Vec`s, trait-typed values, "
"closures — stays inside the VM. A declaration that violates the set is a "
"compile error at the declaration, not a failed call at 2 a.m. There is no "
"`any`: a polymorphic crossing seals its value in an erasure box (`opaque(v)` "
"at the call, `opaque.downcast<T>` after), checked, never silent — see "
"[reified types](reified-types.md)."
msgstr "其余一切——用户的 struct 与 class、`Vec`、trait 类型的值、闭包——都留在 VM 内部。违反该集合的声明在声明处就是编译错误，而不是凌晨两点的失败调用。没有 `any`：多态跨越把它的值封进擦除盒（调用处 `opaque(v)`，之后 `opaque.downcast<T>`），受检、绝不无声——参见[具体化类型](reified-types.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:69
msgid "The currency is typed Rust"
msgstr "通货是带类型的 Rust"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:71
msgid ""
"On the Rust side the boundary speaks ordinary Rust types. Each type declares "
"the rut type it binds against and converts checked:"
msgstr "在 Rust 一侧，边界说的是普通的 Rust 类型。每种类型声明它绑定到的 rut 类型，并受检转换："

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:74
msgid ""
"**Borrow, don't copy.** `&str` and `&[u8]` parameters read the VM's buffers "
"zero-copy. The borrow is call-scoped — the type system makes smuggling it "
"past the return a compile error."
msgstr "**借用，不复制。**`&str` 与 `&[u8]` 参数零拷贝地读取 VM 的缓冲区。借用以调用为作用域——类型系统会让把它偷运过返回点成为编译错误。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:77
msgid ""
"**Copy on purpose.** Owned `String`/`Vec<u8>` parameters are the explicit "
"\"I keep this data\" choice."
msgstr "**有意地复制。**拿到所有权的 `String`/`Vec<u8>` 参数是\"我要留下这份数据\"的显式选择。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:79
msgid ""
"**`Opaque<T>`** is the typed view of a host handle: an 8-byte store handle "
"the host holds and passes back; the payload stays host-owned (`Box<dyn Any>` "
"plus an optional finalize hook)."
msgstr "**`Opaque<T>`** 是宿主句柄的带类型视图：一个 8 字节的存储句柄，宿主持有并回传；载荷保持宿主所有（`Box<dyn Any>` 加一个可选的 finalize 钩子）。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:83
msgid ""
"**Borrow guards** make the zero-copy views safe while script runs: a "
"borrowed object is flagged, and script-side mutation through a re-entrant "
"call traps with `borrowed by host` instead of racing. Guards clear on "
"return. This is sound forever because the heap never moves objects (see "
"[memory](memory.md))."
msgstr "**借用守卫**让零拷贝视图在脚本运行期间安全：被借用的对象会被标记，脚本一侧经由重入调用做出的变更将以 `borrowed by host` 触发陷阱，而不是形成数据竞争。守卫在返回时清除。它永远健全，因为堆从不移动对象（参见[内存](memory.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:89
msgid "Wrapping host state: the class-in-rut pattern"
msgstr "包装宿主状态：rut 类模式"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:91
msgid ""
"There is no \"host class\". Native state crosses as an `opaque` handle and a "
"rut class wraps it — ordinary source the compiler can see and optimize "
"around:"
msgstr "没有\"宿主类\"。原生状态以 `opaque` 句柄跨越，rut 类包裹它——编译器看得见、也能围绕它优化的普通源码："

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:105
msgid ""
"Every method is exactly one host call — the same crossing a magic host class "
"would have paid — but the wrapper can also carry impl blocks, validation, "
"and convenience the native side never needed to know about. The payoff for "
"keeping the boundary this small: host resources die deterministically. When "
"the wrapper's last reference goes, the handle's refcount hits zero and the "
"payload's Rust `Drop` runs _at that point_ — sockets and textures close on "
"script schedule, not at some future collection."
msgstr "每个方法恰好就是一次宿主调用——魔法宿主类同样要付的跨越——但包装器还能承载 impl 块、校验，以及原生一侧从不需要知道的便利。边界保持这样小的回报：宿主资源确定性地死亡。包装器的最后一个引用消失时，句柄的引用计数归零，载荷的 Rust `Drop` _在那一刻_运行——套接字与纹理按脚本的日程关闭，而不是在将来某次收集中。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:114
msgid "Host functions are rows, dispatched by slot"
msgstr "宿主函数是行，按槽位分派"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:116
msgid ""
"Each declared row gets a stable slot id at compile time; calls compile to "
"slot dispatch, so names are binding-time labels only — renaming a Rust-side "
"binding target fails the join instead of silently rebinding. The surface "
"grammar is small:"
msgstr "每条声明的行在编译期得到一个稳定的槽位 id；调用编译为槽位分派，所以名字只是绑定期的标签——重命名 Rust 侧的绑定目标会让接合失败，而不是悄悄重绑。表面语法很小："

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:121
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"host fn name(params) -> T;        // concrete signature; no generics —\n"
"                                  // a generic has no shape to check\n"
"host struct Name { fields };      // flat record of crossing fields\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"host fn name(params) -> T;        // concrete signature; no generics —\n"
"                                  // a generic has no shape to check\n"
"host struct Name { fields };      // flat record of crossing fields\n"
"```"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:127
msgid ""
"`builtin` declarations (the engine's own fns, classes, and traits — `str` "
"methods, `Weak`, `Future`) are engine surface: the embedder cannot spell "
"them, and users implement their traits with ordinary impl blocks. Async rows "
"(`pub host async fn`) are declared like any row and expand into a small row "
"family the driving loop uses — the embedder binds them with one closure per "
"future; see [the async model](async-model.md)."
msgstr "`builtin` 声明（引擎自己的 fn、类和 trait——`str` 方法、`Weak`、`Future`）是引擎表面：嵌入方写不出它们，用户用普通 impl 块实现它们的 trait。异步行（`pub host async fn`）与任何行一样声明，并展开为驱动循环所用的一小组行族——嵌入方为每个 future 绑定一个闭包；参见[异步模型](async-model.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:135
msgid "Re-entrancy, traps, budgets"
msgstr "重入、陷阱、预算"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:137
msgid ""
"A native fn receives a context that may call **back into rut** (`vm.call`) — "
"nested calls run under the same budget on a fresh frame stack."
msgstr "原生 fn 收到的上下文可以**回调进 rut**（`vm.call`）——嵌套调用在同一预算下、崭新的一套帧栈上运行。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:140
msgid ""
"Native code runs **outside the op budget**: the host is trusted to be fast, "
"or to hand back a future instead of blocking. A trap raised inside a native "
"fn propagates to the host as an `Err(Trap)` with the native frame visible in "
"the backtrace."
msgstr "原生代码运行在**操作预算之外**：宿主被信任为快，或者会交还一个 future 而不是阻塞。原生 fn 内部抛出的陷阱以 `Err(Trap)` 传播到宿主，原生帧在回溯中可见。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:144
msgid ""
"Traps are catchable **only at the boundary** — script never catches one. "
"That is what keeps panics loud and state uncorrupted."
msgstr "陷阱**只能在边界**被捕获——脚本永远捕获不到。正是这一点让 panic 保持响亮、状态保持完好。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:147
msgid "What was deliberately left out"
msgstr "刻意留下的空白"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:149
msgid ""
"No C ABI. There is no `register_struct`, no `size_of`, no pointer mirroring "
"of record layouts: records are slot arrays internal to the VM, and a host "
"sees them only through the checked crossing. The few bytes you give up to "
"the checked boundary buy the property that makes embedding pleasant — every "
"mismatch is a named, typed, load-time diagnostic instead of a runtime "
"mystery."
msgstr "没有 C ABI。没有 `register_struct`，没有 `size_of`，没有对记录布局的指针镜像：记录是 VM 内部的槽数组，宿主只能透过受检跨越看见它们。你在受检边界上让出的那几个字节，换来的是让嵌入舒心的性质——每个不匹配都是一个指名道姓、带类型、加载期的诊断，而不是运行时的谜团。"

#: src/core-concepts/host-boundary.md:156
msgid ""
"The full details live in the reference: [embedding and native "
"modules](../reference/embedding.md), [the value boundary and "
"borrows](../reference/value-boundary.md), [host fns and declaration "
"files](../reference/host-fns.md), and the withdrawn C-struct experiment "
"recorded at [repr(C) interop](../reference/repr-c.md)."
msgstr "全部细节住在参考手册里：[嵌入与原生模块](../reference/embedding.md)、[值边界与借用](../reference/value-boundary.md)、[宿主 fn 与声明文件](../reference/host-fns.md)，以及记录在 [repr(C) 互操作](../reference/repr-c.md)的已撤回 C 结构体实验。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:3
msgid ""
"Everything a rut program becomes is a **typed bytecode** executed by a "
"register VM. There is no JIT, no interpreter tiering, no runtime "
"speculation: the compiler does all optimization ahead of time, and what runs "
"is exactly what was compiled. This chapter is the tour of that artifact — "
"the instruction set, the module binary, the load-time verification, and the "
"interpreter's execution and budgeting model."
msgstr "rut 程序最终成为的一切，就是由寄存器 VM 执行的**类型化字节码**。没有 JIT，没有解释器分层，没有运行时投机：编译器提前完成一切优化，运行的就是编译过的东西。本章导览这个产物——指令集、模块二进制、加载期校验，以及解释器的执行与预算模型。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:10
msgid "One struct, one thread, one heap"
msgstr "一个结构体，一个线程，一套堆"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:14
msgid "// runtime type descriptors + vtables\n"
msgstr "// 运行时类型描述符 + vtable\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:15
msgid "// the refcounted, self-managed heap\n"
msgstr "// 引用计数的自管堆\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:16
msgid "// linked binaries\n"
msgstr "// 已链接的二进制\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:17
msgid "// the call stack\n"
msgstr "// 调用栈\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:18
msgid "// woken async frames\n"
msgstr "// 被唤醒的异步帧\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:19
msgid "// the virtual clock's wheel\n"
msgstr "// 虚拟时钟的轮盘\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:20
msgid "// fuel, heap budget, interrupt interval\n"
msgstr "// 燃料、堆预算、中断间隔\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:21
msgid "// registered native bodies, clock, loader\n"
msgstr "// 已注册的原生函数体、时钟、加载器\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:25
msgid ""
"A VM is single-threaded by construction (`!Send`); workers are separate VM "
"instances communicating by messages. The host holds one and drives it with "
"methods: `call` an entry point, `run_ready` to drain woken frames, "
"`next_deadline` for the timer wheel, `drive` for a single resumption. See "
"[the host boundary](host-boundary.md) for the embed loop and [the async "
"model](async-model.md) for the queues' role in scheduling."
msgstr "VM 在构造上就是单线程的（`!Send`）；worker 是通过消息通信的独立 VM 实例。宿主持有一台并用方法驱动它：用 `call` 调入口点，用 `run_ready` 排空被唤醒的帧，用 `next_deadline` 查定时器轮盘，用 `drive` 做单次恢复。嵌入循环见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)；队列在调度中的角色见[异步模型](async-model.md)。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:35
msgid ""
"The instruction set is register-based: operands are `u16` indices into a "
"per-frame slot file, and **every register has a static type recorded in the "
"function's signature**. That single decision is what lets the hot path stay "
"tag-free (see [reified types](reified-types.md)) and what makes refcounting "
"precise: the compiler emits plain moves for scalars and retain/release moves "
"for references, with no runtime tag checks."
msgstr "指令集基于寄存器：操作数是指向每帧槽位文件的 `u16` 索引，而**每个寄存器都有记录在函数签名中的静态类型**。正是这一个决定让热路径保持无标签（参见[具体化类型](reified-types.md)），也让引用计数精确：编译器为标量生成普通移动，为引用生成保留/释放移动，没有任何运行时标签检查。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:42
msgid ""
"Ops are small and fixed-size, with variadic operand lists (call arguments, "
"branch tables) living in per-function pools. A representative sample:"
msgstr "操作小而定长，变长的操作数列表（调用实参、分支表）放在每函数的池子里。一份代表性样本："

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:60
msgid "The type system also decides what is _not_ an op:"
msgstr "类型系统同样决定什么_不是_操作："

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:62
msgid ""
"**Nothing static.** What the type table can answer at compile time becomes a "
"constant — no \"get type id\" instruction, no length load for a fixed-size "
"array."
msgstr "**没有静态之事。**类型表在编译期能回答的都会变成常量——没有\"取类型 id\"指令，定长数组也没有长度加载。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:65
msgid ""
"**Nothing polymorphic and nothing named.** A trait-typed receiver has "
"exactly one op (the vtable call); string concatenation is a native call, not "
"an opcode."
msgstr "**没有多态之事，也没有按名之事。**trait 类型的接收者恰好对应一个操作（vtable 调用）；字符串拼接是一次原生调用，不是操作码。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:68
msgid ""
"**Concrete memory, control flow, and two readbacks.** Ops touch memory only "
"through compile-time-known layouts, plus the two reads reification needs: "
"\"what is it\" (`tidof`) and the guarded payload extract behind a downcast."
msgstr "**具体的内存、控制流，外加两个读回。**操作只透过编译期已知的布局触碰内存，再加上具体化需要的两次读取：\"它是什么\"（`tidof`）与向下转型背后带守卫的载荷提取。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:73
msgid "The module binary"
msgstr "模块二进制"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:75
msgid ""
"Compilation produces a versioned, self-contained binary per module: types, "
"constants, functions (with their typed register signatures), imports, and a "
"symbol table for backtraces. Its properties matter more than its layout:"
msgstr "编译为每个模块产出一个带版本、自包含的二进制：类型、常量、函数（带各自的类型化寄存器签名）、导入，以及用于回溯的符号表。它的性质比它的布局更重要："

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:80
msgid ""
"**Deterministic.** The same sources plus the same dependency versions "
"produce byte-identical binaries, so artifacts are cacheable by content hash "
"and shippable instead of sources."
msgstr "**确定性。**同样的源码加同样的依赖版本产出逐字节相同的二进制，因此产物可以按内容哈希缓存，可以交付二进制而非源码。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:83
msgid ""
"**Self-describing but strippable.** Names and source spans are retained for "
"traces by default; a release build can strip them, and a sidecar map file "
"(keyed by content hash) can restore symbolication later. See the reference "
"on [diagnostics](../reference/diagnostics.md)."
msgstr "**自描述但可剥离。**名字与源码区间默认为追踪保留；release 构建可以剥离它们，而一个旁车 map 文件（按内容哈希为键）可以在日后恢复符号化。参见关于[诊断](../reference/diagnostics.md)的参考章节。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:88
msgid ""
"**Link-time identity.** Type ids are module-local at rest and rebased into "
"the VM's global table at link, where impl registries merge and duplicates "
"are rejected. Cross-module trait calls specialize per concrete argument here "
"too — the static-dispatch rule of [traits and "
"dispatch](traits-and-dispatch.md) holds across module boundaries."
msgstr "**链接期身份。**类型 id 静止时是模块局部的，链接时重定基到 VM 的全局表——impl 注册表在那里合并，重复被拒绝。跨模块 trait 调用也在这里按具体实参特化——[trait 与分派](traits-and-dispatch.md)的静态分派规则跨越模块边界依然成立。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:94
msgid ""
"**Little-endian everywhere**, by law — every serialized word, so artifacts "
"are platform-independent by construction rather than by luck."
msgstr "**处处小端**，依律而行——每个序列化的字都是——产物因此从构造上就平台无关，而不是靠运气。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:98
msgid "Verification at load"
msgstr "加载时校验"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:100
msgid ""
"Loading re-checks each function before anything executes: register operands "
"against the signature, operand pools and jump targets in range, type "
"operands present in the type table, native slots declared, and async state "
"tables closed. A failed verification is a load error naming the module and "
"function — **corrupted binaries never execute**. This is also where crossing "
"rules are enforced for host-facing signatures, so a non-crossing shape is "
"rejected before any script runs."
msgstr "加载会在任何东西执行之前重新检查每个函数：寄存器操作数对照签名、操作数池与跳转目标在范围内、类型操作数在类型表中存在、原生槽位已声明、异步状态表封闭。校验失败是一个指名模块与函数的加载错误——**损坏的二进制永不执行**。这里也是宿主向签名的跨越规则被强制之处，因此不可跨越的形状在任何脚本运行之前就被拒绝。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:108
msgid ""
"Module-level initialization is folded at compile time: literals, enum "
"members, constant expressions, and interned string literals become constants "
"in the binary. A user function call in a module initializer is a compile "
"error — there is no load-time execution at all. Loading a module runs "
"nothing."
msgstr "模块级初始化在编译期折叠：字面量、枚举成员、常量表达式与驻留字符串字面量都成为二进制中的常量。模块初始化器里的用户函数调用是编译错误——根本不存在加载期执行。加载模块不运行任何东西。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:114
msgid "The interpreter loop and traps"
msgstr "解释器循环与陷阱"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:116
msgid ""
"Execution is a decode-dispatch loop over frames. A frame is the function's "
"code, a program counter, its typed register file, and (for async frames) the "
"resume state. Calls push frames; returns pop them; direct calls are an index "
"plus jump, and trait calls are two loads plus an indirect jump through the "
"vtable."
msgstr "执行是一个跨帧的解码-分派循环。一个帧就是函数的代码、一个程序计数器、它的类型化寄存器文件，以及（对异步帧而言）恢复状态。调用压帧；返回弹帧；直接调用是一次索引加跳转，trait 调用是两次加载加一次透过 vtable 的间接跳转。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:122
msgid ""
"Failure is a **trap**, not an exception and not a Rust panic: integer "
"overflow on the plain operators, a `nil` deref, an out-of-bounds index, a "
"failed `assert` or `panic(..)`, or an exhausted budget. A trap captures the "
"raw frame chain (rendered lazily — symbolication happens only if someone "
"prints it), runs destructors on the way out, and unwinds as an `Err(Trap)` "
"to the host call. Rut code cannot catch one; the boundary is the catch point "
"(see [the host boundary](host-boundary.md))."
msgstr "失败是**陷阱**，不是异常，也不是 Rust panic：普通运算符上的整数溢出、对 `nil` 解引用、越界索引、失败的 `assert` 或 `panic(..)`，或者耗尽的预算。陷阱捕获原始帧链（惰性渲染——只有当有人打印它时才做符号化），在退出路上运行析构器，并以 `Err(Trap)` 的形式沿栈展开到宿主调用。Rut 代码无法捕获它；边界就是捕获点（参见[宿主边界](host-boundary.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:131 src/reference/vm-core.md:104
msgid "Budgets and interrupts"
msgstr "预算与中断"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:133
msgid ""
"Two knobs make it safe to run third-party code, both set at construction and "
"mutable while running:"
msgstr "两个旋钮让运行第三方代码变得安全，两者都在构造时设置、运行期间可变："

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:137
msgid "// one unit per op, counts down\n"
msgstr "// 每操作一个单位，倒数\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:138
msgid "// checked at every allocation\n"
msgstr "// 每次分配都检查\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:139
msgid "// default: check every 1024 ops\n"
msgstr "// 默认：每 1024 个操作检查一次\n"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:142
msgid ""
"Exhaustion is **resumable**: the trap parks the frame exactly where it was — "
"the frame _is_ the loop state — so the host can add fuel, raise the heap "
"limit, or flip the interrupt flag and resume. A UI host yields mid-frame; a "
"wasm page grants finite fuel; a test sets finite fuel plus a virtual clock "
"and gets a deterministic hang proof."
msgstr "耗尽是**可恢复的**：陷阱把帧停在原地——帧_就是_循环状态——宿主因此可以加燃料、调高堆限额或翻转中断标志然后恢复。UI 宿主在帧中途让步；wasm 页面发放有限燃料；测试设有限燃料加虚拟时钟，得到一份确定性的挂起证明。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:147
msgid ""
"The heap check runs _before_ any write, so an out-of-memory failure leaves "
"the heap byte-identical (see [memory](memory.md))."
msgstr "堆检查在任何写入_之前_运行，所以内存耗尽的失败让堆保持逐字节相同（参见[内存](memory.md)）。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:150
msgid ""
"Native functions run outside the fuel budget — a hanging native is a host "
"bug by contract — and the interrupt hook is the host's lever at native "
"return points."
msgstr "原生函数运行在燃料预算之外——挂死的原生函数按契约就是宿主的 bug——而中断钩子是宿主在原生返回点上的操纵杆。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:154
msgid "Why no JIT is viable"
msgstr "为什么无 JIT 是可行的"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:156
msgid ""
"A JS engine's speed is its JIT, and the JIT exists to speculate about "
"polymorphic property loads. rut has no polymorphic loads: field access is by "
"known index, calls bind statically whenever the site names one concrete "
"type, generics are monomorphized, and the remaining dynamic dispatch is an "
"honest checked vtable hop. The optimizer's currency is **type stability** — "
"what the checker proves is everything the optimizer gets — and its passes "
"(constant folding, inlining, monomorphization, register-level cleanup) all "
"run ahead of time. The result is a runtime with no warmup curve, no "
"deoptimization asymmetries, and per-op costs you can reason about from the "
"bytecode alone."
msgstr "JS 引擎的速度就是它的 JIT，而 JIT 的存在是为了对多态属性加载做投机。rut 没有多态加载：字段访问按已知索引，调用点指名一个具体类型时调用就静态绑定，泛型被单态化，剩下的动态分派是一次如实且受检的 vtable 跳转。优化器的通货是**类型稳定性**——检查器证明的一切就是优化器得到的全部——而它的各个 pass（常量折叠、内联、单态化、寄存器级清理）全部提前运行。结果是一个没有预热曲线、没有反优化不对称性的运行时，每操作的成本可以从字节码本身推演。"

#: src/core-concepts/the-vm.md:168
msgid ""
"The full tables and laws live in the reference: [typed "
"bytecode](../reference/typed-bytecode.md), [the module binary and "
"verification](../reference/module-binary.md), [VM "
"core](../reference/vm-core.md), and [resource limits and "
"fuel](../reference/resource-limits.md)."
msgstr "完整的表与法则住在参考手册里：[类型化字节码](../reference/typed-bytecode.md)、[模块二进制与校验](../reference/module-binary.md)、[VM 核心](../reference/vm-core.md)，以及[资源限制与燃料](../reference/resource-limits.md)。"

