#: src/examples/index.md:30
msgid "The three dependency kinds"
msgstr "三种依赖类型"

#: src/examples/index.md:32
msgid ""
"Every package carries a `rut.toml` manifest (see [Project structure and "
"rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)), and a manifest relates a "
"package to other packages through **three tables**, all visible in the "
"examples:"
msgstr "每个包都带一份 `rut.toml` 清单（参见[项目结构与 rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)），清单通过**三张表**把一个包与其他包关联起来——在示例中全部可见："

#: src/examples/index.md:37
msgid ""
"**`[deps]`** — ordinary dependencies, transitively mounted. The common case: "
"`03-plugin`'s `plugin/rut.toml` declares `server = { path = \"../server\" "
"}`, and [05 — Todolist web](05-todolist-web.md)'s `biz` package declares "
"`ui` (which itself pulls the collection packages)."
msgstr "**`[deps]`**——普通依赖，传递式挂载。常见情形：`03-plugin` 的 `plugin/rut.toml` 声明 `server = { path = \"../server\" }`，而[05 — Web 待办清单](05-todolist-web.md)的 `biz` 包声明 `ui`（后者自己再拉取集合包）。"

#: src/examples/index.md:42
msgid ""
"**`[peer-deps]`** — required by default: the _consumer_ supplies the peer "
"and the peer is never pulled transitively. Marking a peer `optional = true` "
"flips it to a presence relation: its integration file (impl-only code the "
"peer makes compilable) mounts only when the peer is anywhere in the "
"program's closure. The in-tree example is the std `json` package's "
"serde-model impls — `impl JsonSerialize for Vec<T>` is written in json but "
"must not force every json consumer to mount the collection packages, so "
"those live as optional peers and as `[dev-deps]` for json's own tests. [02 — "
"Digest](02-digest.md) consumes json _light_; [06 — GitHub viewer "
"CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md) calls `assemble_peers` and mounts the impl "
"groups for real because the collections are in its closure."
msgstr "**`[peer-deps]`**——默认必填：_消费方_提供对等包，而对等包永远不会被传递式拉取。把对等包标为 `optional = true` 会把它翻转成一种存在关系：它的集成文件（对等包使之可编译的纯 impl 代码）只在该对等包出现在程序闭包中的任何位置时才挂载。树内的例子是 std `json` 包的 serde 模型 impl——`impl JsonSerialize for Vec<T>` 写在 json 里，但绝不能强迫 json 的每个消费者都挂载集合包，所以那些 impl 作为可选对等包存在，并作为 json 自身测试的 `[dev-deps]`。[02 — 摘要](02-digest.md)轻量地消费 json；[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md) 调用 `assemble_peers` 真正挂载 impl 组，因为集合包在它的闭包里。"

#: src/examples/index.md:54
msgid ""
"**`[dev-deps]`** — mounted only while building the package itself, never in "
"a consumer's world. json develops against the real collection packages "
"through the both-kinds pairing while its consumers mount it without them."
msgstr "**`[dev-deps]`**——只在构建包本身时挂载，绝不进入消费者的世界。json 透过这种双类型配对对着真实的集合包开发，而它的消费者挂载它时并不带这些包。"

#: src/examples/index.md:59
msgid ""
"The full rules — the loud missing-required-peer error, the silence of absent "
"optional peers, dedup-by-origin at the splice, and what bundle format the "
"packer emits — are on [Dependency kinds](../reference/dependency-kinds.md)."
msgstr "完整的规则——缺必填对等包的响亮错误、可选对等包缺席时的静默、拼接处按来源去重，以及打包器产出什么捆绑包格式——都在[依赖类型](../reference/dependency-kinds.md)。"

#: src/examples/index.md:64
msgid "Reading order"
msgstr "阅读顺序"

#: src/examples/index.md:66
msgid ""
"New to the language: read [00 — Todolist](00-todolist.md) and [01 — "
"Sort](01-sort.md) for the embedding shape, then [The playground "
"corpus](playground-corpus.md) for the language surface in small doses. For "
"the web story, [05 — Todolist web](05-todolist-web.md) is the centerpiece "
"and [06 — GitHub viewer CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md) is the networking "
"counterpart. [03 — Plugin](03-plugin.md) is the one to study for packaging "
"and module loading, and [04 — Custom async](04-custom-async.md) for what the "
"future trait looks like from user code."
msgstr "语言新手：先读[00 — 待办清单](00-todolist.md)和[01 — 排序](01-sort.md)了解嵌入形态，再读[Playground 语料](playground-corpus.md)小口尝语言表面。Web 这条线，[05 — Web 待办清单](05-todolist-web.md)是主角，[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)是它的网络对应物。打包与模块加载要研究的是[03 — 插件](03-plugin.md)；future trait 从用户代码看长什么样，看[04 — 自定义异步](04-custom-async.md)。"

#: src/examples/00-todolist.md:3
msgid ""
"The first runnable host example, and the template for the rest of the "
"chapter: a Rust program embeds rut, compiles a rut **library** (there is no "
"`main` in it), and drives the library through its `entry fn` surface. The "
"split is two files — `todolist.rut` owns the data and the logic as a "
"`TodoList` class with full CRUD; `src/main.rs` owns the session: compile, "
"verify, then a scripted conversation of `vm.call`s. The one-sentence design "
"rule: **the host owns the session, rut owns the data.**"
msgstr "第一个可运行的宿主示例，也是本章其余部分的模板：一个 Rust 程序嵌入 rut，编译一个 rut **库**（其中没有 `main`），并经由其 `entry fn` 接口驱动这个库。划分是两个文件——`todolist.rut` 作为一个带完整 CRUD 的 `TodoList` 类，掌管数据与逻辑；`src/main.rs` 掌管会话：编译、校验，然后是一段按脚本进行的 `vm.call` 对话。一句话设计规则：**宿主拥有会话，rut 拥有数据。**"

