#: src/examples/02-digest.md:53
msgid "The integer surface is enough for real algorithms"
msgstr "整数表面足以支撑真实算法"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:55
msgid ""
"`digest.rut` runs on hex literals, `u32`/`u64`, the wrapping family, and "
"signedness-correct shifts. CRC-32 is the compact showcase — table-free, "
"bitwise, and exactly the textbook loop. The entry is pure rut — no host, no "
"manifest — so it runs on its own, here checked against the algorithm's "
"canonical test value:"
msgstr "`digest.rut` 跑在十六进制字面量、`u32`/`u64`、回绕家族和符号正确的移位上。CRC-32 是紧凑的展示品——无表、逐位、与教科书循环一模一样。入口是纯 rut——没有宿主、没有清单——所以它能独立运行，这里对照该算法的规范测试值："

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:61
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn crc32(data: bytes) -> u32 {\n"
"    let mut crc: u32 = 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"    for (let b of data) {\n"
"        crc = crc ^ b as u32;\n"
"        for (let k = 0; k < 8; k += 1) {\n"
"            if ((crc & 1) == 1) {\n"
"                crc = (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320u32;\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                crc = crc >> 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return crc ^ 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"crc\");\n"
"    let vector = \"123456789\".encode();   // the canonical CRC-32 test "
"vector\n"
"    log.info(f\"crc32(vector) = {crc32(vector)} — check value 0xCBF43926: "
"{crc32(vector) == 0xCBF43926u32}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn crc32(data: bytes) -> u32 {\n"
"    let mut crc: u32 = 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"    for (let b of data) {\n"
"        crc = crc ^ b as u32;\n"
"        for (let k = 0; k < 8; k += 1) {\n"
"            if ((crc & 1) == 1) {\n"
"                crc = (crc >> 1) ^ 0xEDB88320u32;\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                crc = crc >> 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return crc ^ 0xFFFFFFFFu32;\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"crc\");\n"
"    let vector = \"123456789\".encode();   // the canonical CRC-32 test "
"vector\n"
"    log.info(f\"crc32(vector) = {crc32(vector)} — check value 0xCBF43926: "
"{crc32(vector) == 0xCBF43926u32}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:90
msgid ""
"SHA-512 is the demanding one: its 64-bit rotations need `>>` to be a "
"_logical_ shift on `u64` and `wrapping_shl` to truncate to the operand "
"width. The FNV/djb2/sdbm trio, by contrast, deliberately never shifts a "
"64-bit word — `wrapping_mul`, `wrapping_add`, and `^` carry them, showing "
"how far the primitive surface alone goes."
msgstr "SHA-512 是最挑剔的那个：它的 64 位旋转需要 `>>` 在 `u64` 上是_逻辑_移位，需要 `wrapping_shl` 截断到操作数宽度。相比之下，FNV/djb2/sdbm 三件套刻意从不移位 64 位字——`wrapping_mul`、`wrapping_add` 与 `^` 撑起它们，展示了仅凭原始类型表面能走多远。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:96
msgid "`bytes` crosses directly; `opaque` appears exactly once"
msgstr "`bytes` 直接跨越；`opaque` 恰好出现一次"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:98
msgid ""
"Byte payloads need no wrapper — `bytes` is in the crossing set, so `entry fn "
"hex_enc(data: bytes) -> str` takes a host byte slice head-on ([primitive "
"types](../reference/primitive-types.md)). The one erasure in the file is the "
"recursive JSON tree: rut has no recursive dataclass, so the tree is a tagged "
"union by hand with children boxed in `opaque` to break the recursion "
"([opaque — erasure and downcast](../reference/opaque.md)):"
msgstr "字节载荷不需要包装器——`bytes` 在可跨越集合里，所以 `entry fn hex_enc(data: bytes) -> str` 迎面接下宿主的字节切片（[原始类型](../reference/primitive-types.md)）。文件中唯一一处擦除是递归的 JSON 树：rut 没有递归数据类，所以这棵树是手工打造的带标签联合，子节点装进 `opaque` 盒以打断递归（[opaque — 擦除与向下转型](../reference/opaque.md)）："

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:106
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"enum JTag { Null, False, True, Num, Str, Arr, Obj }\n"
"\n"
"struct Json {\n"
"    tag:  JTag;\n"
"    num: str;          // verbatim lexeme — exact round-trips, no\n"
"    str: str;          // float formatting anywhere in this file\n"
"    arr:  Vec<opaque>;\n"
"    keys: Vec<str>;\n"
"    vals: Vec<opaque>;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"enum JTag { Null, False, True, Num, Str, Arr, Obj }\n"
"\n"
"struct Json {\n"
"    tag:  JTag;\n"
"    num: str;          // verbatim lexeme — exact round-trips, no\n"
"    str: str;          // float formatting anywhere in this file\n"
"    arr:  Vec<opaque>;\n"
"    keys: Vec<str>;\n"
"    vals: Vec<opaque>;\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:119
msgid ""
"Storing numbers as their **verbatim lexemes** is what makes round-trips "
"exact: `-3e2` decodes and re-encodes as `-3e2`, with no float formatting "
"anywhere in the file."
msgstr "把数字按**原样词素**存储正是往返精确的原因：`-3e2` 解码再编码还是 `-3e2`，全文件没有任何浮点格式化。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:123
msgid "The encode half rides the std `json` package"
msgstr "编码半边骑在 std `json` 包上"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:125
msgid ""
"The encode side is not private code: it is an `impl` of the std `json` "
"package's serialization trait, driving the package's writer. This is the "
"orphan rule's type-local case — json owns the trait, this file owns `Json`, "
"so the pair is legal exactly here ([Traits and "
"dispatch](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)):"
msgstr "编码一侧不是私有代码：它是 std `json` 包序列化 trait 的一个 `impl`，驱动该包的 writer。这是孤儿规则的类型本地情形——json 拥有 trait，本文件拥有 `Json`，所以这个组合恰好在这里合法（[trait 与分派](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)）："

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:131
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"impl JsonSerialize for Json {\n"
"    fn encode(self, mut w: JsonWriter) -> ?EncodeJsonError {\n"
"        when (self.tag) {\n"
"            JTag.Null -> { w.write_raw(\"null\"); },\n"
"            JTag.False -> { w.write_raw(\"false\"); },\n"
"            JTag.True -> { w.write_raw(\"true\"); },\n"
"            JTag.Num -> { w.write_raw(self.num); },\n"
"            JTag.Str -> { w.write_str(self.str); },\n"
"            JTag.Arr -> {\n"
"                w.begin_array();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.arr.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    let ae: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.arr[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ae.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_array();\n"
"            },\n"
"            JTag.Obj -> {\n"
"                w.begin_object();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.keys.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    w.key(self.keys[i]);\n"
"                    let ve: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.vals[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ve.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_object();\n"
"            },\n"
"        }\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"impl JsonSerialize for Json {\n"
"    fn encode(self, mut w: JsonWriter) -> ?EncodeJsonError {\n"
"        when (self.tag) {\n"
"            JTag.Null -> { w.write_raw(\"null\"); },\n"
"            JTag.False -> { w.write_raw(\"false\"); },\n"
"            JTag.True -> { w.write_raw(\"true\"); },\n"
"            JTag.Num -> { w.write_raw(self.num); },\n"
"            JTag.Str -> { w.write_str(self.str); },\n"
"            JTag.Arr -> {\n"
"                w.begin_array();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.arr.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    let ae: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.arr[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ae.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_array();\n"
"            },\n"
"            JTag.Obj -> {\n"
"                w.begin_object();\n"
"                for (let i = 0; i < self.keys.len(); i += 1) {\n"
"                    w.key(self.keys[i]);\n"
"                    let ve: Json = opaque.downcast<Json>(self.vals[i]);\n"
"                    let e = ve.encode(w);\n"
"                    if (e != nil) { return e; }\n"
"                }\n"
"                w.end_object();\n"
"            },\n"
"        }\n"
"        return nil;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:165
msgid ""
"The entry surface then hands the tree to `encodeJson` and flattens the "
"`(str, err)` pair it answers. The decode half stays a private cursor parser "
"(strings iterate as codepoints, so the source is split once into single-char "
"strings and walked by index) — and every decode error is an honest string "
"value, never a trap:"
msgstr "入口接口随后把树交给 `encodeJson`，并把它回答的 `(str, err)` 对偶摊平。解码半边保持为一个私有的游标解析器（字符串按码点迭代，所以源串被一次性切成单字符字符串再按索引走）——而每个解码错误都是诚实的字符串值，绝不是陷阱："

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:171
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"hex_dec(\"zz\")   = \"hex: invalid character at index 0\"\n"
"b64_dec(\"!*\")   = \"base64: invalid character `!`\"\n"
"json_dec(\"{,}\") = \"json: expected a key string at index 1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"hex_dec(\"zz\")   = \"hex: invalid character at index 0\"\n"
"b64_dec(\"!*\")   = \"base64: invalid character `!`\"\n"
"json_dec(\"{,}\") = \"json: expected a key string at index 1\"\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:177
msgid "The host oracle, in miniature"
msgstr "宿主 oracle，微缩版"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:179
msgid ""
"The host keeps three-line reference implementations for the hash keys with "
"no canonical crate, and crates for everything else — then compares:"
msgstr "对没有规范 crate 的哈希键，宿主备有三行参考实现；其余一切都用 crate——然后比较："

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:184
msgid "// the hash-key trio with no canonical crate: three-line references\n"
msgstr "// 没有规范 crate 的哈希键三件套：三行参考实现\n"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:195
msgid ""
"The same session runs under 50 M fuel for the demos and raises to 500 M for "
"the 64 KiB stress blob — budgets are the host's call, per call."
msgstr "同一会话在演示时跑在 50 M 燃料下，对 64 KiB 压力数据块上调到 500 M——预算由宿主逐次调用决定。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:201
msgid ""
"The integer surface (hex literals, `u32`/`u64`, wrapping ops, logical "
"shifts) is enough for MD5-through-SHA-512 — verified, not asserted, against "
"independent Rust."
msgstr "整数表面（十六进制字面量、`u32`/`u64`、回绕运算、逻辑移位）足以支撑从 MD5 到 SHA-512——是对独立 Rust 验证过的，不是口头断言。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:204
msgid ""
"`bytes` crosses the boundary directly; `opaque` is for the one place "
"recursion needs breaking."
msgstr "`bytes` 直接跨越边界；`opaque` 只用在递归需要被打断的那一处。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:206
msgid ""
"The std `json` package is usable from day one: implement its serialize trait "
"for your own type and its writer does the byte work ([core and the swappable "
"packages](../reference/stdlib.md))."
msgstr "std `json` 包从第一天就能用：为你的类型实现它的序列化 trait，它的 writer 替你做字节的活（[core 与可替换的包](../reference/stdlib.md)）。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:209
msgid ""
"Errors are values, and the host-as-oracle pattern is the strongest test "
"shape in this chapter."
msgstr "错误是值，而宿主即 oracle 是本章最强的测试形态。"

#: src/examples/02-digest.md:212
msgid ""
"The oracle pattern returns in [06 — GitHub viewer "
"CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md), where the fixture is a recorded HTTP lane "
"instead of hash crates."
msgstr "oracle 模式会在[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)回归，只是夹具换成录制的 HTTP 链路，而不是哈希 crate。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:3
msgid ""
"A Rust chat-room **server** with a rut **moderator plugin** — the first "
"example built on two things at once: **re-entrant `vm.call`** (the host "
"calls rut, and a host fn called _by_ rut calls back into rut while the first "
"call is still parked) and **both `opaque` directions** (rut hands the host a "
"handle to its own state; the host hands rut a handle to the server's event "
"bus). It is also the packaging example: the plugin loads from a **module "
"directory** and from a **`.rutbundle`** packed from that directory at "
"runtime — the two forms of one contract ([Module "
"bundles](../reference/bundles.md))."
msgstr "一个 Rust 聊天室**服务器**配一个 rut **审核插件**——第一个同时建立在两件事之上的示例：**重入的 `vm.call`**（宿主调用 rut，而被 rut 调用的宿主 fn 在第一次调用还停着时又回调进 rut）与 **`opaque` 双向**（rut 递给宿主一个指向自己状态的句柄；宿主递给 rut 一个指向服务器事件总线的句柄）。它也是打包示例：插件从**模块目录**加载，也从运行时由该目录打包出的 **`.rutbundle`** 加载——同一契约的两种形态（[模块捆绑包](../reference/bundles.md)）。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:18
msgid "# transcript asserted + bundle round-trip gates\n"
msgstr "# 对话记录断言 + 捆绑包往返门禁\n"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:21
msgid ""
"The demo drives one scripted session twice — once against the directory, "
"once against the packed bundle — and prints both transcripts plus the "
"round-trip proof. Abridged:"
msgstr "演示把同一段脚本化会话跑两遍——一遍对着目录，一遍对着打包后的捆绑包——并打印两份对话记录加往返证明。节选："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:37
msgid ""
"The test suite asserts the transcript exactly, proves every line crossed the "
"nested render (`emits == renders`), and gates the bundle form: round-trip "
"equality, byte-determinism, and refusal on an unknown format version or CRC "
"corruption."
msgstr "测试套件逐字断言对话记录，证明每一行都穿过了嵌套 render（`emits == renders`），并为捆绑包形态设门禁：往返相等、逐字节确定性，以及对未知格式版本或 CRC 损坏的拒绝。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:44
msgid "The layering: callbacks at the edges, classes in the middle"
msgstr "分层：回调在边缘，类在中间"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:46
msgid ""
"Four layers, and neither business layer ever touches the crossing protocol:"
msgstr "四层，两个业务层都不触碰跨越协议："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:56
msgid ""
"The moderator rules themselves are plain rut — flood control (three "
"consecutive messages from one sender mutes them), muted users rejected on "
"rejoin, a `!stats` command, tick heartbeats:"
msgstr "审核规则本身就是普通的 rut——刷屏控制（同一发送者连续三条消息即被禁言）、被禁言用户重进即拒、一条 `!stats` 命令、tick 心跳："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:60
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"pub fn on_msg(mut self, user: str, text: str) {\n"
"    if (self.is_muted(user)) {\n"
"        self.say(\"muted\", user);\n"
"    } else if (text == \"!stats\") {\n"
"        self.say(\"direct\", f\"{user}: {self.stats()}\");\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        if (user == self.last_sender) {\n"
"            self.streak += 1;\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.last_sender = user;\n"
"            self.streak = 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (self.streak == 3) {\n"
"            self.muted.push(user);\n"
"            self.mutes += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"system\", f\"{user} muted for flooding\");\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.msgs += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"broadcast\", f\"<{user}> {text}\");\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"pub fn on_msg(mut self, user: str, text: str) {\n"
"    if (self.is_muted(user)) {\n"
"        self.say(\"muted\", user);\n"
"    } else if (text == \"!stats\") {\n"
"        self.say(\"direct\", f\"{user}: {self.stats()}\");\n"
"    } else {\n"
"        if (user == self.last_sender) {\n"
"            self.streak += 1;\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.last_sender = user;\n"
"            self.streak = 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (self.streak == 3) {\n"
"            self.muted.push(user);\n"
"            self.mutes += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"system\", f\"{user} muted for flooding\");\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            self.msgs += 1;\n"
"            self.say(\"broadcast\", f\"<{user}> {text}\");\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:85
msgid ""
"Every bus write funnels through one private `say(topic, payload)` — the "
"business logic never spells a crossing."
msgstr "每一次总线写入都汇入同一个私有的 `say(topic, payload)`——业务逻辑从不拼写跨越。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:88
msgid "The handshake: both opaque directions meet"
msgstr "握手：两个 opaque 方向会师"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:90
msgid ""
"Closures cannot cross the boundary in either direction, so callbacks "
"register **by name**: the plugin hands the host the export names it wants "
"wired to each topic, and returns the handle to its own state (`init` is the "
"entire handshake — bus box in, state handle out):"
msgstr "闭包无法沿任一方向跨越边界，所以回调**按名注册**：插件把自己想接到各 topic 的导出名交给宿主，并返回指向自己状态的句柄（`init` 就是全部握手——总线盒进，状态句柄出）："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:95
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn init(bus: opaque) -> opaque {\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"join\", \"on_join\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"msg\", \"on_msg\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"leave\", \"on_leave\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"tick\", \"on_tick\");\n"
"    let mod_: ?Moderator = Moderator.new(bus);\n"
"    return opaque(mod_);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn init(bus: opaque) -> opaque {\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"join\", \"on_join\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"msg\", \"on_msg\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"leave\", \"on_leave\");\n"
"    subscribe(bus, \"tick\", \"on_tick\");\n"
"    let mod_: ?Moderator = Moderator.new(bus);\n"
"    return opaque(mod_);\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:106
msgid ""
"rut's moderator state comes back as a **rut-constructed** `opaque` — the "
"host holds the handle and passes it back on every event."
msgstr "rut 的审核状态以一个 **rut 构造的** `opaque` 返回——宿主持有句柄，并在每个事件上回传。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:108
msgid ""
"the host's `EventBus` goes in as a **host-constructed** `Opaque<EventBus>` — "
"`subscribe` and `emit` are that box's callbacks, reached only through the "
"borrow guards ([Value boundary and borrows](../reference/value-boundary.md), "
"[Embedding and native modules](../reference/embedding.md))."
msgstr "宿主的 `EventBus` 以一个**宿主构造的** `Opaque<EventBus>` 进入——`subscribe` 与 `emit` 是这个盒的回调，只能透过借用守卫触及（[值边界与借用](../reference/value-boundary.md)、[嵌入与原生模块](../reference/embedding.md)）。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:114
msgid "The re-entrant call: `emit` re-enters rut mid-op"
msgstr "重入调用：`emit` 在操作中途重新进入 rut"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:116
msgid ""
"The host binds the two `server` rows over its bus. The `emit` body is the "
"interesting one — while the emitting handler is still parked mid-op, it "
"makes a **nested** `vm.call(\"render_line\")` to format the wire line:"
msgstr "宿主把 `server` 的两行绑定到自己的总线上。`emit` 的函数体是有趣的那个——当正在发事件的处理器还停在操作中途时，它发起一次**嵌套的** `vm.call(\"render_line\")` 来格式化线上的一行："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:124 src/reference/embedding.md:35
#: src/reference/host-fns.md:122
msgid "\"server::emit\""
msgstr "\"server::emit\""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:129
msgid "\"render_line\""
msgstr "\"render_line\""

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:139
msgid ""
"(The comment above this code in the source is worth reading too.) The bus "
"stays mutably borrowed _across_ the nested call — the value boundary's "
"borrow guard is what makes that sound: a second `emit` fired from inside "
"`render_line` would trap on the guard instead of racing. On the rut side, "
"`render_line` is the one-line entry the host re-enters — pure string work, "
"so it runs on its own (the line it prints below is the transcript's "
"broadcast row):"
msgstr "（源码里这段代码上方的注释也值得一读。）总线在嵌套调用_期间_保持可变借用——值边界的借用守卫正是让这一切健全的机制：从 `render_line` 内部再发一次 `emit` 会在守卫上触发陷阱，而不是形成竞争。rut 一侧，`render_line` 是宿主重入的那行入口——纯字符串工作，所以它能独立运行（下面打印的那一行就是对话记录里的 broadcast 行）："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:147
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn render_line(topic: str, payload: str) -> str {\n"
"    return f\"[{topic}] {payload}\";\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"bus\");\n"
"    log.info(render_line(\"broadcast\", \"<ada> hello world\"));\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"entry fn render_line(topic: str, payload: str) -> str {\n"
"    return f\"[{topic}] {payload}\";\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"bus\");\n"
"    log.info(render_line(\"broadcast\", \"<ada> hello world\"));\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:164
msgid "The packaging: one directory, two load forms"
msgstr "打包：一个目录，两种加载形态"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:166
msgid ""
"The plugin is a **module directory** — a manifest naming the entry plus its "
"deps, loadable as-is and packable unchanged ([Project structure and "
"rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)):"
msgstr "插件是一个**模块目录**——一份清单写明入口及其依赖，可以原样加载、原样打包（[项目结构与 rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)）："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:170
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# plugin/rut.toml\n"
"format = \"rutbundle\"\n"
"format_version = 4\n"
"name = \"plugin\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./plugin.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"server = { path = \"../server\" }\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../../../rut/pouch\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"# plugin/rut.toml\n"
"format = \"rutbundle\"\n"
"format_version = 4\n"
"name = \"plugin\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./plugin.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"server = { path = \"../server\" }\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../../../rut/pouch\" }\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:182
msgid ""
"`server/` is the interesting dependency: a **pure declaration surface** — a "
"host package whose manifest points at a `.d.rut` decl file, with the Rust "
"embedder binding the bodies ([Host fns and declaration "
"files](../reference/host-fns.md)):"
msgstr "`server/` 是有意思的那个依赖：一个**纯声明表面**——一个宿主包，其清单指向一个 `.d.rut` 声明文件，函数体由 Rust 嵌入方绑定（[宿主 fn 与声明文件](../reference/host-fns.md)）："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:193
msgid ""
"`main.rs` packs the same directory with `rut_driver::pack_dir`, writes "
"`plugin.rutbundle` to temp, and loads it back through the identical "
"`Plugin::load` — the transcript equality print is the proof. The CLI drives "
"the same loader for any self-contained module:"
msgstr "`main.rs` 用 `rut_driver::pack_dir` 打包同一个目录，把 `plugin.rutbundle` 写进临时目录，再经完全相同的 `Plugin::load` 加载回来——对话记录相等的打印就是证明。CLI 对任何自包含模块都驱动同一个加载器："

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:199
msgid "# a module directory (rut.toml)\n"
msgstr "# 一个模块目录（rut.toml）\n"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:200
msgid "# -> mod.rutbundle\n"
msgstr "# -> mod.rutbundle\n"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:201
msgid "# the packed form\n"
msgstr "# 打包形态\n"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:204
msgid ""
"The Rust side mirrors the rut layering: business code calls typed methods "
"(`p.join(\"ada\")`, `p.msg(...)`), and `vm.call` happens in exactly one "
"dispatcher that looks up the subscribed export name per topic — unknown "
"topics are dropped, not trapped, so a server keeps running when a plugin "
"didn't subscribe."
msgstr "Rust 一侧镜像 rut 的分层：业务代码调用带类型的方法（`p.join(\"ada\")`、`p.msg(...)`），而 `vm.call` 只发生在一个分派器里，它按 topic 查订阅的导出名——未知 topic 被丢弃而不是触发陷阱，所以插件没订阅时服务器照常运转。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:212
msgid ""
"**One directory is one module**; the manifest names the entry and the deps, "
"and the same directory packs to a `.rutbundle` unchanged."
msgstr "**一个目录就是一个模块**；清单写明入口与依赖，同一目录原样打包成 `.rutbundle`。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:214
msgid ""
"**Registration by name, not by closure** — callbacks never cross the "
"boundary as values, in either direction."
msgstr "**按名注册，而非按闭包**——回调永不作为值跨越边界，任一方向都不例外。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:216
msgid ""
"**Re-entrancy is sound by construction**: a host fn can call back into rut "
"mid-op, and the borrow guard turns a would-be data race into a loud trap."
msgstr "**重入在构造上就是健全的**：宿主 fn 可以在操作中途回调进 rut，而借用守卫把本会成为数据竞争的东西变成一声响亮的陷阱。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:219
msgid ""
"**Both `opaque` directions** compose: rut-state-out, host-state-in, and "
"neither side can inspect what the other erased."
msgstr "**`opaque` 两个方向**可组合：rut 状态出、宿主状态进，双方都无法窥视对方擦除了什么。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:221
msgid ""
"The layering discipline — adapters own the crossing protocol, business logic "
"stays pure — is what keeps a plugin auditable."
msgstr "分层纪律——适配器独占跨越协议，业务逻辑保持纯粹——正是插件可审计的缘由。"

#: src/examples/03-plugin.md:224
msgid ""
"The crossing rules this example lives on are in [the host "
"boundary](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md); the load forms are specified "
"in [Module bundles](../reference/bundles.md)."
msgstr "本示例赖以立足的跨越规则在[宿主边界](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)；加载形态规定在[模块捆绑包](../reference/bundles.md)。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:3
msgid ""
"A **parse-only** example: `examples/04-custom-async/custom_async.rut` is a "
"single rut file with no Cargo harness — you cannot run it today, and that is "
"a deliberate disclosure, not an oversight. What it shows is the async "
"vocabulary from the _user_ side: a hand-written future type, an `impl` of "
"the engine's built-in `Future` trait, and a user-written launcher with "
"per-checkpoint stats and cancellation audits. The runnable harness that "
"would drive it end to end is the follow-up work; the file is kept in the "
"repo now because the parser's conformance suite compiles every example, so "
"this vocabulary is checked to stay parseable ([Async and "
"await](../reference/async.md))."
msgstr "一个**仅解析**的示例：`examples/04-custom-async/custom_async.rut` 是单个 rut 文件，没有 Cargo 骨架——今天你没法运行它，而这是刻意的明示，不是疏忽。它展示的是从_用户_一侧看到的异步词汇：一个手写的 future 类型、一个引擎内置 `Future` trait 的 `impl`，以及一个带逐检查点统计与取消审计的用户自写启动器。能端到端驱动它的可运行骨架是后续工作；这个文件如今仍留在仓库里，因为解析器一致性套件会编译每个示例，所以这套词汇被持续检查着保持可解析（[异步与 await](../reference/async.md)）。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:15
msgid "\"Run\" it"
msgstr "\"运行\"它"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:17
msgid ""
"There is no harness. The file is exercised by the parser conformance test, "
"which walks every `.rut` file in `examples/`:"
msgstr "没有骨架。这个文件由解析器一致性测试操练，该测试遍历 `examples/` 里的每个 `.rut` 文件："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:21
msgid "# parses every example, incl. this one\n"
msgstr "# 解析每个示例，包括本例\n"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:24
msgid ""
"To _read_ the same machinery running, see [06 — GitHub viewer "
"CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md): its brain is an `async fn` driven by the "
"standard launcher this file re-spells by hand."
msgstr "想_读_同一套机制运行起来的样子，见[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)：它的大脑是一个 `async fn`，由本文件手工重新拼写的标准启动器驱动。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:31
msgid "The audit log — the example's reason to exist"
msgstr "审计日志——这个示例存在的理由"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:33
msgid ""
"`CustomFuture` is a stage machine, but the _point_ of the file is the "
"accounting around it: every launch, resumption, cancellation, and completion "
"lands in one module-owned record the embedder can read after the run:"
msgstr "`CustomFuture` 是一台阶段机器，但这个文件的_要点_在围绕它的记账上：每次启动、恢复、取消和完成都落进一条模块私有的记录，嵌入方可以在运行结束后读取："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:38
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"struct AuditLog {\n"
"    launches: u32;      // futures this log saw started\n"
"    yields: u32;        // resumptions driven — one per checkpoint\n"
"    cancels: u32;       // cancellation probes that answered true\n"
"    checkpoints: u32;   // high-water mark of the context ledger\n"
"    finished: u32;      // runs that walked every step they booked\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"struct AuditLog {\n"
"    launches: u32;      // futures this log saw started\n"
"    yields: u32;        // resumptions driven — one per checkpoint\n"
"    cancels: u32;       // cancellation probes that answered true\n"
"    checkpoints: u32;   // high-water mark of the context ledger\n"
"    finished: u32;      // runs that walked every step they booked\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:48
msgid ""
"The launcher takes a shared `?AuditLog`, so the embedder holds one cell and "
"reads the whole run's story out of it afterwards — `summary` renders the "
"one-line audit."
msgstr "启动器持有一个共享的 `?AuditLog`，嵌入方因此握着一个单元，之后从中读出整场运行的故事——`summary` 渲染单行审计。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:52
msgid "The machine — what `async fn` weaves, spelled out"
msgstr "机器——`async fn` 织出的东西，摊开在明处"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:54
msgid ""
"When you write `async fn`, the engine weaves a hidden frame whose shape is "
"exactly this: a stage counter, the payload the stages carry, and a done "
"flag. `CustomFuture` spells that shape out in source, so you can see what "
"the keyword hides. The machine itself is plain rut — only the _driving "
"harness_ is missing — so the block below adds a `main` that advances it by "
"hand; that is as far as one can run it today:"
msgstr "当你写下 `async fn`，引擎会织出一个隐藏帧，其形状正是如此：一个阶段计数器、各阶段携带的载荷、一个 done 标志。`CustomFuture` 把这个形状在源码里拼写出来，让你看清关键字背后藏着什么。机器本身就是普通 rut——缺的只是_驱动骨架_——所以下面的代码块补了一个手动推进它的 `main`；这是今天能跑到的最远处："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:62
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct CustomFuture {\n"
"    steps: u32;      // checkpoints booked before the run finishes\n"
"    stage: str;      // what the current stage does (the audit's label)\n"
"    done: bool;      // the last stage ran\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl CustomFuture {\n"
"    fn new(steps: u32, stage: str) -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { steps: steps, stage: stage, done: false };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    /// One stage of work — what one resumption advances. `false` when\n"
"    /// no stages are left: the runner's completion signal.\n"
"    fn advance(mut self) -> bool {\n"
"        if (self.done) {\n"
"            return false;\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (self.steps == 0) {\n"
"            self.done = true;\n"
"            return false;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self.steps -= 1;\n"
"        return true;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"future\");\n"
"    let mut f = CustomFuture.new(3, \"poll\");\n"
"    let mut polls = 0;\n"
"    while (f.advance()) {\n"
"        polls += 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"3 steps took {polls} advancing polls, then advance() "
"answered false (done={f.done})\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"struct CustomFuture {\n"
"    steps: u32;      // checkpoints booked before the run finishes\n"
"    stage: str;      // what the current stage does (the audit's label)\n"
"    done: bool;      // the last stage ran\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"impl CustomFuture {\n"
"    fn new(steps: u32, stage: str) -> Self {\n"
"        return Self { steps: steps, stage: stage, done: false };\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    /// One stage of work — what one resumption advances. `false` when\n"
"    /// no stages are left: the runner's completion signal.\n"
"    fn advance(mut self) -> bool {\n"
"        if (self.done) {\n"
"            return false;\n"
"        }\n"
"        if (self.steps == 0) {\n"
"            self.done = true;\n"
"            return false;\n"
"        }\n"
"        self.steps -= 1;\n"
"        return true;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"future\");\n"
"    let mut f = CustomFuture.new(3, \"poll\");\n"
"    let mut polls = 0;\n"
"    while (f.advance()) {\n"
"        polls += 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    log.info(f\"3 steps took {polls} advancing polls, then advance() "
"answered false (done={f.done})\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:106
msgid "The trait surface: a user impl of a built-in trait"
msgstr "trait 表面：内置 trait 的用户 impl"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:108
msgid ""
"`Future` is an engine-named built-in trait — the engine weaves it for every "
"`async fn`'s hidden frame — but built-in traits are engine _named_, not "
"engine _closed_. A hand-written machine registers through the ordinary "
"nominal path, one impl block, and rides the same drive law ([Traits and "
"dispatch](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)):"
msgstr "`Future` 是一个引擎命名的内置 trait——引擎为每个 `async fn` 的隐藏帧织入它——但内置 trait 是引擎_命名_的，不是引擎_封闭_的。手写的机器通过普通的名义路径注册，一个 impl 块，就骑上同一条驱动法则（[trait 与分派](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)）："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:114
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Future<nil> for CustomFuture {\n"
"    fn yield(self, cx: RunContext) {\n"
"        // the ledger view: the frame's resume state, read as data\n"
"        let at = cx.checkpoint();\n"
"        // the cancellation probe: a cancelled frame stops advancing —\n"
"        // the audit sees it as \"died here, did not advance\" — and runs\n"
"        // its drop path instead of the next stage\n"
"        if (cx.cancelled()) {\n"
"            self.done = true;\n"
"            self.stage = f\"{self.stage}@{at}:cancelled\";\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"impl Future<nil> for CustomFuture {\n"
"    fn yield(self, cx: RunContext) {\n"
"        // the ledger view: the frame's resume state, read as data\n"
"        let at = cx.checkpoint();\n"
"        // the cancellation probe: a cancelled frame stops advancing —\n"
"        // the audit sees it as \"died here, did not advance\" — and runs\n"
"        // its drop path instead of the next stage\n"
"        if (cx.cancelled()) {\n"
"            self.done = true;\n"
"            self.stage = f\"{self.stage}@{at}:cancelled\";\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:130
msgid ""
"The receiver **is** the frame — the machine's fields are its state — and the "
"context is the only handle a resumption needs. The frozen context protocol "
"reads as data: `checkpoint` answers this frame's resume state, `cancelled` "
"answers the task's abort flag. Cancellation is a value the frame inspects, "
"not an exception it catches."
msgstr "接收者**就是**帧——机器的字段就是它的状态——而上下文是一次恢复所需的唯一句柄。冻结的上下文协议按数据来读：`checkpoint` 回答本帧的恢复状态，`cancelled` 回答任务的中止标志。取消是帧检查的一个值，不是它捕获的异常。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:136
msgid "The user launcher"
msgstr "用户启动器"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:138
msgid ""
"The engine's standard launcher set (`launch_future`, `LaunchedFutureHandle`, "
"`sleep`) is ordinary code any module may re-spell — that is the point of "
"`launch_custom`. It supplies the driving and the audit over the same "
"`Future` surface, so the machine never knows which launcher started it:"
msgstr "引擎的标准启动器套装（`launch_future`、`LaunchedFutureHandle`、`sleep`）是任何模块都可以重新拼写的普通代码——这正是 `launch_custom` 的意义所在。它在同一 `Future` 表面上提供驱动与审计，所以机器永远不知道是哪个启动器启动了它："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:154
msgid ""
"The returned `CustomLaunched` receipt is deliberately **not** a future — it "
"cannot be awaited, and it is not re-launchable (that is a type error, never "
"a runtime check). Its one real member is the cancel edge, which flags the "
"task and lets the loop's re-drive run the probe:"
msgstr "返回的 `CustomLaunched` 回执刻意**不是** future——它不能被 await，也不能再次启动（那是类型错误，绝不是运行时检查）。它唯一真正的成员是取消边：标记任务，让循环的再驱动去跑那个探测："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:178
msgid ""
"Alongside sits `audit_drive`, the audit twin of the engine loop's drive "
"columns: run a stage, count the resumption, stop on completion."
msgstr "旁边还坐着 `audit_drive`，引擎循环各驱动列的审计孪生：跑一个阶段，记一次恢复，完成即停。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:181
msgid "Scope, honestly"
msgstr "范围，如实相告"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:183
msgid "Two boundaries to keep straight when you read this file:"
msgstr "读这个文件时要分清两条边界："

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:185
msgid ""
"**User futures are launcher-drivable** — the driving loop finds the "
"`Future::yield` row in the vtable, exactly as it does for woven frames."
msgstr "**用户 future 可被启动器驱动**——驱动循环在 vtable 里找到 `Future::yield` 行，与对待织入帧完全一样。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:188
msgid ""
"**`await` targets engine-woven futures only** in the current build (async-fn "
"results and `sleep`); awaiting an arbitrary user impl, and joining "
"concurrent futures, land with the next async milestone."
msgstr "**`await` 只面向引擎织入的 future**（当前构建中：async fn 的结果与 `sleep`）；await 任意的用户 impl，以及 join 并发的 future，要等下一个异步里程碑。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:192
msgid ""
"So today the file is a parse-checked design corpus and a teaching document: "
"the shape of the weave, the shape of a launcher, and the proof that the "
"future trait is a user-extensible surface — not a runnable demo. When you "
"want the runnable version of the same story, read [06 — GitHub viewer "
"CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md), and for the model behind it, [the async "
"model](../core-concepts/async-model.md)."
msgstr "所以今天这个文件是一份解析受检的设计语料和教学文档：织造的形状、启动器的形状，以及 future trait 是用户可扩展表面这份证明——不是可运行的演示。想要同一个故事的可运行版本，去读[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)；想看背后的模型，去读[异步模型](../core-concepts/async-model.md)。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:201
msgid ""
"`async fn` compiles to a hidden frame implementing `Future` — this file "
"spells that frame out in user source."
msgstr "`async fn` 编译为实现 `Future` 的隐藏帧——本文件在用户源码里把这个帧拼写出来。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:203
msgid ""
"Built-in traits are engine-named, not engine-closed: `impl Future<nil> for "
"YourType` registers through the ordinary path."
msgstr "内置 trait 是引擎命名的，不是引擎封闭的：`impl Future<nil> for YourType` 走普通路径注册。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:205
msgid ""
"Cancellation is data the frame reads (`cx.cancelled()`), and every "
"checkpoint is observable (`cx.checkpoint()`)."
msgstr "取消是帧读取的数据（`cx.cancelled()`），而每个检查点都可观察（`cx.checkpoint()`）。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:207
msgid ""
"A launcher is just code: driving + audit over the public `Future` surface, "
"re-spellable by any module."
msgstr "启动器只是代码：公共 `Future` 表面上的驱动 + 审计，任何模块都可重新拼写。"

#: src/examples/04-custom-async.md:209
msgid ""
"The file is parse-only by disclosure; the runnable harness is follow-up work "
"— the machine itself is plain rut (it ran above), but nothing launches or "
"drives it as a future yet."
msgstr "本文件按明示仅限解析；可运行骨架是后续工作——机器本身是普通 rut（它在上面跑过了），但还没有任何东西把它作为 future 启动或驱动。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:3
msgid ""
"One page app — a todolist with a simulated server — where **every DOM move "
"and every timer goes through ten declared host crossings**, and the page's "
"brain is a rut project of **two packages**. `ui` is the framework: an atom "
"store (the jotai shape, in rut), a widget type, a keyed diff, and a "
"component vocabulary. `biz` is the domain: the todolist machine expressed as "
"store mutations, plus the app shell. The host — web-sys on wasm32 in the "
"browser, a fake-DOM twin on native in the tests — owns the loop; rut owns "
"the state. Pure rut: no event loop, no async keywords on the rut side; every "
"asynchronous fact enters through a door named for its event."
msgstr "一个整页应用——带模拟服务器的待办清单——其中**每一次 DOM 移动、每一个定时器都穿过十条已声明的宿主跨越**，而页面的大脑是一个**双包**的 rut 项目。`ui` 是框架：一个原子存储（jotai 的形态，用 rut 写）、一个部件类型、一个键控 diff，以及一套组件词汇。`biz` 是领域：表达为存储变更的待办清单机器，加上应用外壳。宿主——浏览器里是 wasm32 上的 web-sys，测试里是原生的假 DOM 孪生——拥有循环；rut 拥有状态。纯 rut：rut 一侧没有事件循环，没有 async 关键字；每个异步事实都经由一扇以自身事件命名的门进入。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:17
msgid "# the twin + the law (95 tests), from the repo root\n"
msgstr "# 孪生 + 法则（95 个测试），从仓库根目录\n"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:19
msgid "# the through-the-artifact gate (node tier + browser tier)\n"
msgstr "# 穿过产物的门禁（node 层 + 浏览器层）\n"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:22
msgid ""
"`cargo test` runs the whole story on the **fake-DOM twin** — a HashMap "
"element tree with real DOM semantics and a virtual timer clock — over the "
"same rut sources the browser runs. The e2e script builds nothing silently "
"and skips nothing silently: tier 1 (plain node) drives the real wasm "
"artifact through the loader's own ABI on a fake DOM; tier 2 (when "
"geckodriver + Firefox exist) types and clicks the live page."
msgstr "`cargo test` 在**假 DOM 孪生**上跑完整故事——一棵带真实 DOM 语义的 HashMap 元素树加一个虚拟定时器时钟——跑在与浏览器相同的 rut 源码上。e2e 脚本不悄悄构建任何东西，也不悄悄跳过任何东西：tier 1（纯 node）在假 DOM 上经加载器自己的 ABI 驱动真实的 wasm 产物；tier 2（当 geckodriver + Firefox 存在时）在活页面上打字、点击。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:30
msgid "To open the page yourself:"
msgstr "自己打开这个页面："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:40
msgid ""
"What you'll see: type a title — the status line echoes the typing and the "
"counts never move (the draft is not a counts dependency). Press Add — an "
"italic _pending_ line paints immediately, the counts line flips to `1 in "
"flight`, and ~400 ms later the committed row replaces it. Toggle a row — the "
"title goes italic for ~250 ms, then the check fills and the title strikes "
"through. The row animates because the keyed diff **kept the node alive** — "
"nothing is cleared and rebuilt, ever."
msgstr "你会看到：输入一个标题——状态行回显输入，计数纹丝不动（草稿不是计数的依赖）。按 Add——一行斜体的_待定_立即绘制出来，计数行翻成 `1 in flight`，约 400 毫秒后提交的行取而代之。切换一行的状态——标题斜体约 250 毫秒，然后勾选填上、标题划线。行之所以有动画，是因为键控 diff **让节点保活**——任何东西都不会被清空重建，永远。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:51
msgid "The ABI is the page: `main` plus the doors"
msgstr "ABI 就是页面：`main` 加各扇门"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:53
msgid ""
"`rut/biz/app.rut` — the boot turn builds the app container and returns it as "
"an `opaque` (rut has no mutable module state, so the host holds the state "
"and re-passes it every turn — the [00 — Todolist](00-todolist.md) pattern at "
"page scale):"
msgstr "`rut/biz/app.rut` ——启动回合构建应用容器并把它作为 `opaque` 返回（rut 没有可变的模块状态，所以宿主持有状态并每回合回传——[00 — 待办清单](00-todolist.md)模式在页面尺度上的应用）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:58
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn main() -> opaque {\n"
"    let boot: World = world_boot(\"booted — type a title, press Add\");\n"
"    let root = AppRoot {\n"
"        world: boot,\n"
"        t1: t1_mount(\"app\"),\n"
"    };\n"
"    paint(root);\n"
"    return opaque(root);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"entry fn main() -> opaque {\n"
"    let boot: World = world_boot(\"booted — type a title, press Add\");\n"
"    let root = AppRoot {\n"
"        world: boot,\n"
"        t1: t1_mount(\"app\"),\n"
"    };\n"
"    paint(root);\n"
"    return opaque(root);\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:70
msgid ""
"Every asynchronous fact enters through a door named for its event — "
"`on_click`/`on_input` for DOM events, `on_timer` for the clock. Each door "
"re-passes the container and answers the entry-err pair: `(opaque(c), \"\")` "
"on a clean turn, `(nil, why)` on a soft failure the pump reports _while "
"keeping the page alive_."
msgstr "每个异步事实都经由一扇以自身事件命名的门进入——DOM 事件走 `on_click`/`on_input`，时钟走 `on_timer`。每扇门都回传容器并回答入口-err 对偶：干净回合回答 `(opaque(c), \"\")`，软失败回答 `(nil, why)`，由泵在_保住页面性命_的同时上报。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:76
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"fn dom_event(mut r: AppRoot, id: str, detail: str) -> (?opaque, str) {\n"
"    let booked = t1_event(r.t1, id, detail);\n"
"    let req = opaque.downcast<Req>(booked);\n"
"    if (req != nil) {\n"
"        tim_after(req.latency, req.tag);\n"
"    }\n"
"    paint(r);\n"
"    return (opaque(r), \"\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"fn dom_event(mut r: AppRoot, id: str, detail: str) -> (?opaque, str) {\n"
"    let booked = t1_event(r.t1, id, detail);\n"
"    let req = opaque.downcast<Req>(booked);\n"
"    if (req != nil) {\n"
"        tim_after(req.latency, req.tag);\n"
"    }\n"
"    paint(r);\n"
"    return (opaque(r), \"\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:88
msgid ""
"The \"server\" is a request table, not a scheduler: adding never touches the "
"list — the machine books a request and the app books one `tim_after(latency, "
"tag)`; the list changes only when the timer's turn runs the answer mutation "
"(per-kind latency, so deadline-ordered commits are visible across kinds)."
msgstr "这个\"服务器\"是一张请求表，不是调度器：添加从不触碰列表——机器登记一个请求，应用登记一次 `tim_after(latency, tag)`；列表只在定时器的回合运行应答变更时才改变（按类型各异的延迟，因此按截止时间排序的提交在不同类型间可见）。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:94
msgid "The ten crossings"
msgstr "十次跨越"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:96
msgid ""
"`web.d.rut` (flat at the example root, registered by hand in both lanes) "
"declares the whole host surface. Elements cross as `opaque` handles; "
"everything else is strings, ints, and bools — no app names, no data "
"shipping, no callbacks ([the host "
"boundary](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)):"
msgstr "`web.d.rut`（平铺在示例根目录，两条通道都手工注册）声明了全部宿主表面。元素以 `opaque` 句柄跨越；其余一切都是字符串、整数和布尔——没有应用专名，没有数据搬运，没有回调（[宿主边界](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md)）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:115
msgid ""
"A wiring bug is loud: a missing id traps (`web::ui_get: no element '#x'`), a "
"kind mismatch names both sides. The host never grew an app-specific crossing "
"— the entire widget system fits over these ten rows, unchanged."
msgstr "接线错误是响亮的：缺失的 id 触发陷阱（`web::ui_get: no element '#x'`），类型不匹配会点名双方。宿主从未长出任何应用专属的跨越——整个部件系统就架在这十行之上，分毫未改。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:120
msgid "The store: jotai's shape over private traits"
msgstr "存储：私有 trait 之上的 jotai 形态"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:122
msgid ""
"`rut/ui/store.rut` is the kernel. Handles are keys, not objects — "
"`Source<T>`, `Derived<T>`, `Mutation<A, R>` carry ids and have no logic of "
"their own beyond routing through their store. The machinery traits are "
"**module-private**, so the domain package cannot name them even to import "
"them — which is how \"a derived cell is not writable\" is enforced at the "
"type level ([Traits and dispatch](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)):"
msgstr "`rut/ui/store.rut` 是内核。句柄是键，不是对象——`Source<T>`、`Derived<T>`、`Mutation<A, R>` 只携带 id，除经由所属存储路由之外没有任何自己的逻辑。机制 trait 是**模块私有的**，领域包连 import 它们的名字都拿不到——\"派生单元不可写\"就是这样在类型层面强制执行的（[trait 与分派](../core-concepts/traits-and-dispatch.md)）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:130
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"trait Readable<T> {\n"
"    fn atom_id(self) -> u32;\n"
"    fn materialize(self, st: Store) -> nil; // first touch: the seed lands\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"trait Writable<A, R> {\n"
"    fn atom_id(self) -> u32;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"trait Readable<T> {\n"
"    fn atom_id(self) -> u32;\n"
"    fn materialize(self, st: Store) -> nil; // first touch: the seed lands\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"trait Writable<A, R> {\n"
"    fn atom_id(self) -> u32;\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:141
msgid ""
"Freshness is **pull-on-read**: a write bumps a generation, and a `get` "
"recomputes a stale derived at most once per write-set. There is no flush "
"step anywhere. Dependencies are **discovered, never declared** — the "
"`ctx.get` calls inside a derive closure ARE the dependency list, re-recorded "
"on every recompute. The domain's counts line is the worked example "
"(`rut/biz/world.rut`):"
msgstr "新鲜度是**读时拉取**：一次写入 bumps 一个代数，`get` 至多在每个写集内把过期的派生重算一次。任何地方都没有冲刷步骤。依赖是**发现的，不是声明的**——derive 闭包内部的 `ctx.get` 调用就是依赖列表，每次重算都重新记录。领域的计数行就是完整的示范（`rut/biz/world.rut`）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:148
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"let counts$ = store.derive(fn (ctx) -> str {\n"
"    let items = ctx.get(items$);\n"
"    let reqs = ctx.get(reqs$);\n"
"    let mut open = 0;\n"
"    for (let t of items) {\n"
"        if (t.done == false) {\n"
"            open += 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    let done_n = items.len() - open;\n"
"    return f\"{open} open | {done_n} done | {reqs.len()} in flight\";\n"
"});\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"let counts$ = store.derive(fn (ctx) -> str {\n"
"    let items = ctx.get(items$);\n"
"    let reqs = ctx.get(reqs$);\n"
"    let mut open = 0;\n"
"    for (let t of items) {\n"
"        if (t.done == false) {\n"
"            open += 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    let done_n = items.len() - open;\n"
"    return f\"{open} open | {done_n} done | {reqs.len()} in flight\";\n"
"});\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:163
msgid ""
"Writes go through mutation fns — `add_m`, `toggle_m`, `remove_m`, `answer_m` "
"— multi-step write programs that run in the one write lane; the machine's "
"counters are sources too, because with no domain container there is nowhere "
"else for state to live."
msgstr "写入经由变更 fn——`add_m`、`toggle_m`、`remove_m`、`answer_m`——运行在唯一写车道上的多步写程序；机器的计数器也是 source，因为没有领域容器，状态就无处可住。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:168
msgid "Widgets are data; the diff does the DOM"
msgstr "部件是数据；diff 负责 DOM"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:170
msgid ""
"`view(r)` is a pure function from app state to a `Widget` tree — it runs no "
"crossing and reads nothing (reads are reactive _props_, resolved at the "
"render door). `t1_render` diffs the new tree against the previous one held "
"in `T1Root` and fires only deltas: match children by key, patch in place, "
"re-append on reorder, retire gone keys' listeners. Nothing changed = nothing "
"fires ([HashMaps and sets](../reference/builtin-generic-types.md) carry the "
"path-keyed tables):"
msgstr "`view(r)` 是从应用状态到 `Widget` 树的纯函数——它不做任何跨越，也不读取任何东西（读取是响应式的 _props_，在渲染门上解析）。`t1_render` 把新树与 `T1Root` 持有的上一棵树做 diff，只触发增量：按键匹配子节点、就地打补丁、重排时重新追加、为消失的键注销监听器。没有变化 = 什么都不触发（路径为键的表由[HashMap 与集合](../reference/builtin-generic-types.md)承载）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:179
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"pub struct T1Root {\n"
"    parent: opaque; // the mounted root element\n"
"    prev: ?Widget = nil; // the previous tree — the diff's left side\n"
"    els: HashMap<str, opaque>; // path -> live handle (ops application)\n"
"    regs: HashMap<str, Ev>; // listener id (as crossed) -> the\n"
"    // widget's event wiring (a data-shaped binding)\n"
"    lids: HashMap<str, i64>; // path -> listener id (retirement)\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rut\n"
"pub struct T1Root {\n"
"    parent: opaque; // the mounted root element\n"
"    prev: ?Widget = nil; // the previous tree — the diff's left side\n"
"    els: HashMap<str, opaque>; // path -> live handle (ops application)\n"
"    regs: HashMap<str, Ev>; // listener id (as crossed) -> the\n"
"    // widget's event wiring (a data-shaped binding)\n"
"    lids: HashMap<str, i64>; // path -> listener id (retirement)\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:190
msgid ""
"Event wiring rides the widgets as **data, not closures** — a row's toggle "
"mutation carries its argument bound (`.on_row(w.toggle_row, t.id)`), and the "
"framework resolves a firing listener id to that wiring. Styling is a token "
"contract: the stylesheet keys only the lowered `t1-*` tokens, and the app "
"spells no class."
msgstr "事件接线以**数据而非闭包**的形式骑在部件上——一行的 toggle 变更带着已绑定的实参（`.on_row(w.toggle_row, t.id)`），框架把触发的监听器 id 解析到那份接线。样式是一份 token 契约：样式表只认_lower_ 之后的 `t1-*` token，应用不写任何 class。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:196
msgid "Two packages, two manifests"
msgstr "两个包，两份清单"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:198
msgid ""
"A real project is not one file — but the package boundary is also the "
"privacy boundary, which is why there are exactly two ([Project structure and "
"rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)):"
msgstr "真实的项目不止一个文件——但包边界同时是隐私边界，这正是只有两个包的原因（[项目结构与 rut.toml](../reference/project-structure.md)）："

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:202
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# rut/biz/rut.toml — the project root\n"
"name = \"app\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./biz.rut\"\n"
"entry.libs = [\"./domain.rut\", \"./world.rut\", \"./app.rut\"]\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"ui = { path = \"../ui\" }\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../../../../rut/pouch\" }\n"
"nmapset = { path = \"../../../../rut/nmapset\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"# rut/biz/rut.toml — the project root\n"
"name = \"app\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./biz.rut\"\n"
"entry.libs = [\"./domain.rut\", \"./world.rut\", \"./app.rut\"]\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"ui = { path = \"../ui\" }\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../../../../rut/pouch\" }\n"
"nmapset = { path = \"../../../../rut/nmapset\" }\n"
"```"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:214
msgid ""
"`entry.libs` splices several files into ONE module (base first, array "
"order), so a name private to `store.rut` is visible to `components.rut` and "
"to nothing outside `ui` — single-file privacy, kept at package scale. `ui` "
"is marked `inline = true` (its generic exports splice by law), and the "
"native lane mounts the _directory_ — the manifest, not a Rust fn, is the "
"module list. The wasm lane mounts the same packages by hand as a mirror, and "
"a test pins both lanes to byte-identical binaries."
msgstr "`entry.libs` 把多个文件拼接成一个模块（基文件在前，按数组顺序），所以 `store.rut` 私有的名字对 `components.rut` 可见，对 `ui` 之外的一切不可见——单文件隐私，保持在包尺度。`ui` 被标为 `inline = true`（它的泛型导出依法拼接），原生通道挂载_目录_——清单就是模块列表，而不是某个 Rust fn。wasm 通道作为镜像手工挂载同样的包，并且有一个测试把两条通道钉在逐字节相同的二进制上。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:225
msgid ""
"The page ABI is `main` plus doors named for their events; state lives in the "
"container the host re-passes every turn."
msgstr "页面 ABI 就是 `main` 加各扇以其事件命名的门；状态活在宿主每回合回传的容器里。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:227
msgid ""
"Ten thin crossings carried an entire reactive framework — the host stayed "
"generic and never learned the word \"todo\"."
msgstr "十条薄跨越扛起了整个响应式框架——宿主保持通用，从未学会\"todo\"这个词。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:229
msgid ""
"The store is jotai's shape in rut: discovered deps, pull-on-read freshness, "
"mutations as the write lane, and type-level non-writability through private "
"traits."
msgstr "存储是 rut 里的 jotai 形态：发现的依赖、读时拉取的新鲜度、作为写车道的变更，以及透过私有 trait 达成的类型级不可写。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:232
msgid ""
"Widgets are values; the keyed diff is the only thing that speaks DOM, and "
"patch-in-place is what makes the UI animatable."
msgstr "部件是值；键控 diff 是唯一会讲 DOM 的东西，而就地打补丁正是 UI 可动画的原因。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:234
msgid ""
"Soft failures are data (`(nil, why)` and the pump keeps draining); a panic "
"alone kills the page, loud."
msgstr "软失败是数据（`(nil, why)`，泵继续排空）；只有 panic 才杀死页面，而且死得响亮。"

#: src/examples/05-todolist-web.md:237
msgid ""
"The async shape this page _simulates_ (the request table + timers) is the "
"real thing in [06 — GitHub viewer CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md); the store's "
"building blocks are in [the swappable packages](../reference/stdlib.md)."
msgstr "本页_模拟_的异步形态（请求表 + 定时器）在[06 — GitHub 查看器 CLI](06-github-viewer-cli.md)里是真家伙；存储的构件在[可替换的包](../reference/stdlib.md)。"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:3
msgid ""
"`rgh` lists and downloads files from public GitHub repositories over the "
"jsDelivr CDN — no GitHub API, no tokens. Its **brain is a rut async free "
"fn**: argv carving, the URL building, the tree JSON decode, the human-size "
"formatter, every message and exit code run in the VM. The Rust half is a "
"pure embedder: mount packages, bind host bodies, launch the brain, pump the "
"driving loop to idle, exit with the brain's i32 (`0` ok, `1` runtime error, "
"`2` usage). This is the worked example for the std `http` lane's redesigned "
"face — `HttpClient`, builder-style construction, and async-only send with "
"true streaming."
msgstr "`rgh` 经由 jsDelivr CDN 列出并下载公开 GitHub 仓库中的文件——不用 GitHub API，不用令牌。它的**大脑是一个 rut 异步自由函数**：argv 切分、URL 构建、树状 JSON 解码、人性化尺寸格式化，每一条消息与每一个退出码都在 VM 里运行。Rust 那一半是纯粹的嵌入方：挂载包、绑定宿主函数体、启动大脑、把驱动循环泵送到空闲、带着大脑的 i32 退出（`0` 正常，`1` 运行时错误，`2` 用法错误）。这是 std `http` 链路重塑后新面孔的完整示范——`HttpClient`、builder 式构建，以及只异步的 send 加真正的流式传输。"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:19
msgid "# the offline suite — zero network\n"
msgstr "# 离线套件——零网络\n"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:20
msgid "# opt-in live CDN check\n"
msgstr "# 可选的线上 CDN 检查\n"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:23
msgid ""
"`list` prints one line per file, depth-first in the API's own order "
"(directories are walked, never printed):"
msgstr "`list` 每个文件打印一行，按 API 自身的顺序深度优先（目录被遍历，从不打印）："

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:30
msgid ""
"The size ladder is `N B` under 1024, then KiB/MiB/GiB with one decimal only "
"when the remainder is nonzero (`1536` → `1.5 KiB`, `1048577` → `1.0 MiB`); "
"the last column is the first 8 characters of the entry's base64 integrity "
"hash, or `-` when absent. The offline suite rides a **fixture lane** keyed "
"on method + URL with a virtual clock — the fixture map's keys ARE the "
"assertions — and covers every usage error, the boundary tree's exact output, "
"streamed binary downloads verified byte-verbatim, wire deaths, and status "
"mappings."
msgstr "尺寸阶梯在 1024 以下是 `N B`，之后是 KiB/MiB/GiB，只有余数非零时才带一位小数（`1536` → `1.5 KiB`，`1048577` → `1.0 MiB`）；最后一列是条目 base64 完整性哈希的前 8 个字符，缺席时为 `-`。离线套件骑在一条按方法 + URL 为键、配虚拟时钟的**夹具链路**上——夹具表的键就是断言本身——并覆盖每一种用法错误、边界树的精确输出、逐字节校验的流式二进制下载、线路死亡，以及状态码映射。"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:41
msgid "The brain is async; the host launches and pumps"
msgstr "大脑是异步的；宿主启动并泵送"

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:43
msgid ""
"`rgh.rut` — the entry point is one `boot` fn: the host crosses argv in as a "
"single `\\n"
"`\\-joined string (no arg lists in the crossing set), and `boot` launches "
"the brain with the standard launcher ([Tasks](../reference/tasks.md)):"
msgstr "`rgh.rut` ——入口是一个 `boot` fn：宿主把 argv 以单个 `\\n`\\-连接的字符串跨越进来（可跨越集合里没有参数列表），`boot` 用标准启动器启动大脑（[任务](../reference/tasks.md)）："

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:54
msgid ""
"The embedder then pumps the driving loop to idle — real reqwest workers "
"settle the completers from their threads, and the process's one-way `exit` "
"row fires mid-pump:"
msgstr "嵌入方接着把驱动循环泵送到空闲——真实的 reqwest worker 从各自的线程落定 completer，而进程的单向 `exit` 行在泵送中途触发："

#: src/examples/06-github-viewer-cli.md:63
msgid "\"rgh: trap: {} — {}\""
msgstr "\"rgh: trap: {} — {}\""

