#: src/reference/lexical-structure.md:85
msgid "Naming conventions (enforced)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lexical-structure.md:87
msgid ""
"**Types are PascalCase** — user types and parameterized builtins: `Vec<T>`, "
"`[T]`, `Weak<T>`, `opaque`, `Task<T>`, `Point`, `Drawable`. Scalars and "
"simple buffers stay lowercase: `i32`, `u8`, `f32`, `bool`, `str`, `bytes`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lexical-structure.md:91
msgid ""
"**Functions and methods are lower_snake_case** — `unwrap_or(d)`, `push(v)`, "
"`checked_add(y)`, `spawn_worker(..)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lexical-structure.md:93
msgid ""
"**Construction is a method call, never a type-call.** User classes construct "
"through their own class methods: `Rect.new(3, 4)`, `Rect.from(other)`, "
"`Version.parse(s)` — see [Classes and constructors](classes.md). Only "
"builtin surfaces keep call forms: `bytes.zeroed(n)`, `Weak(v)`, `opaque(v)`, "
"the repeat `[v; n]`, and `Vec<T>.from(..)` (see [Builtin generic "
"types](builtin-generic-types.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lexical-structure.md:100
msgid ""
"The trailing-`$` marker is kept meaningful by this style rule alone; the "
"compiler attaches no semantics to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/modules-and-visibility.md:3
msgid ""
"Module scope contains **declarations only** — every statement lives inside a "
"function, and **loading a module executes nothing**. Visibility is private "
"by default, with package-scoped forms for libraries."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/modules-and-visibility.md:7
