msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:59
msgid ""
"**Fixed-size cell slots in the arena.** Cells are one fixed-size record "
"carved from 1024-slot chunks with a free list; a dead slot is reused by the "
"next mint. Reuse is invisible except in `heap_usage`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:62
msgid ""
"**The block store.** Every _variable-size_ payload — string octets, array "
"element runs — lives in a block carved from size-classed pages the VM owns:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:65
msgid ""
"Size classes 16 B … 2 KiB (multiples of 8); small blocks come from 32 KiB "
"pages via per-class free lists plus a single-slot LIFO cache for the churn "
"pattern (a temp dies, the same size is minted again)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:68
msgid ""
"In-place growth within a class keeps append-accumulation loops linear; the "
"block header carries the class-rounded capacity, so free re-derives the "
"class with no side table."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:71
msgid "Large blocks (> 2 KiB) get dedicated allocations, freed wholesale."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:72
msgid ""
"Blocks are 1:1 with their cell (the cell is the counted unit) and **never "
"move**, so a raw `&[u8]` into the store stays valid for the cell's life."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:75
msgid ""
"**Immortal singletons.** Interned string literals and dataless enum variants "
"live in a slab freed only at `Vm` drop; they carry the `rc == 0` sentinel."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:78
msgid ""
"**The `opaque` store.** Every rut `opaque` value lives in a slab of two-kind "
"entries (rut value / host payload) with its own borrow guards; entries "
"charge their bytes on insert and refund on death, so the budget and the "
"receipts stay honest."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:82
msgid ""
"**No compaction in v1.** Non-moving keeps host borrows into `Vec` buffers "
"sound and freelists trivial."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:84
msgid ""
"**Cells are addressed by raw pointer** in the slot word. A 32-bit handle "
"design was prototyped and reverted on measurement: ref-heavy workloads paid "
"+8–15% for the decode chain per slot read."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:88
msgid "Deterministic teardown"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/vm-heap.md:90
msgid ""
"Teardown mirrors the destruction rules: the host drops its references, "
"releases run inline ([the Rc heap](rc-heap.md)), and `Vm::drop` frees the "
"survivors wholesale — leaked cycles included — after emitting the leak "
"report. The heap never outlives the `Vm`, and no rut cell can outlive the "
"heap."
msgstr ""

