#: src/reference/tasks.md:31
msgid ""
"It is **not re-launchable**: `launch_future(h)` is a type error for the same "
"reason. A future is consumed exactly once — by `await` or by "
"`launch_future`, never both, never twice."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:34
msgid ""
"One member: `abort()` — `true` if the frame was flagged and re-enqueued, "
"`false` when it had already finished (a repeat abort is stable and harmless)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:38
msgid "Cancellation"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:40
msgid ""
"`abort()` flags the frame's cancellation and re-enqueues it. **The probe at "
"its next checkpoint is the only place cancellation becomes observable** — it "
"never interrupts mid-expression."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:44
msgid "At the probe, the frame runs its **drop path**:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:46
msgid "the pending edge is cleared — a pending `sleep` dies with the frame;"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:47
msgid ""
"every local with a cleanup runs it **deterministically, in reverse "
"declaration order** (`on_drop` callbacks fire, [the Rc heap](rc-heap.md));"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:50
msgid "the state retires (null) — later `abort()` calls answer `false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:52
msgid ""
"Inside a future impl, `cx.cancelled()` reads the same flag as data, so a "
"hand-written frame can honor cancellation at its own pace ([the host futures "
"bridge](host-futures.md)). Cancellation is synchronous at the engine level "
"(flag + re-enqueue); a frame parked on a host future only observes the flag "
"when the loop drives it again."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:58
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"class Drops {\n"
"    n: u32;\n"
"    fn note(mut self, len: u32) { self.n += 1; }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"async fn job(cx: RunContext, seen: ?Drops) -> nil {\n"
"    let buf: ?bytes = bytes.zeroed(64);\n"
"    on_drop(buf, fn (b: ?bytes) { seen.note(b.len()); });\n"
"    await sleep(5000);\n"
"    // if `job` is aborted while parked here, the probe at the sleep\n"
"    // checkpoint runs the drop path: seen.note fires, then buf releases\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:73
msgid "Join (specified)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:75
msgid ""
"There is no `spawn` and no `Task<T>`. The receipt is the join surface: "
"`await h` joins the launched future and produces its completion value. Until "
"the join tier lands, `await h` diagnoses with the join law and the receipt "
"stays non-awaitable."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:80
msgid ""
"Planned laws: joining an already-cancelled receipt yields the cancelled "
"case, never a trap; join re-enqueues the awaiter the same way an in-body "
"`await` parks, so the value surfaces on the driving loop, not through a "
"callback."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:85
msgid "`select` (specified)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:94
msgid ""
"`await select { .. }` races futures; the **winner's value drives its arm**; "
"the losers are dropped — which means **cancelled** (their drop paths run, "
"pending sleeps die with them)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:97
msgid ""
"Arms use `->` like `when`: `fut -> expr` discards the resolved value; `fut x "
"-> expr` binds it to `x` (arm-local binding)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:99
msgid ""
"`select_all(futs)` (stdlib, built on `select`) resolves with the first ready "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:102
