"The grammar parses today; the semantics are gated with \"`await select` is "
"not in this build\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:105
msgid "Structure and fairness"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:107
msgid ""
"v1 tasks are **unstructured**: aborting a frame does not abort frames it "
"awaits. Structured scopes — `scope { .. }` cancelling children on exit — are "
"the specified remedy."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:110
msgid ""
"The ready ring is **round-robin**: each drive runs a frame to its next park "
"or completion, so one greedy future cannot starve the queue. Task priorities "
"are not in the model."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:113
msgid ""
"`vm.pending_tasks()` counts ready frames, armed timers, and host futures "
"parked on Completers — the embedder's idle test ([async and "
"await](async.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/tasks.md:116
msgid ""
"A trap inside a launched future propagates out of `run_ready()` / `drive()`; "
"the frame is retired either way, and its locals ran their drop path."
msgstr ""

