#: src/reference/stdlib.md:170
msgid "`nmapset` — `HashMap`/`HashSet`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:172
msgid ""
"Thin wrappers over the native key table (`nmap_host` rows): the whole state "
"is one `opaque` handle, every method one host call."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:175
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"pub class HashMap<K requires i8 | i16 | i32 | i64 | u8 | u16 | u32 | u64 | "
"bool | str | bytes, V> {\n"
"    pub fn new() -> Self;\n"
"    pub fn with_capacity(n: i32) -> Self;\n"
"    pub fn put(mut self, k: K, v: V) -> bool;      // true = newly inserted\n"
"    pub fn get(self, k: K) -> ?V;                  // the STORED cell, not a "
"copy\n"
"    pub fn has(self, k: K) -> bool;\n"
"    pub fn remove(mut self, k: K) -> bool;\n"
"    pub fn len(self) -> i32;\n"
"}\n"
"pub class HashSet<T requires ..same key set..> { new, with_capacity, put, "
"has, remove, len }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:188
msgid ""
"Laws: the key set is closed (no floats — no stable equality; encode a custom "
"key canonically to `bytes`); `get` answers the stored cell, so two gets of "
"one key name one value until a replace; values release host-side. `str` keys "
"hash by content; `str` keys also carry `*_range(parent, off, len)` members "
"keyed by a byte range of the parent string — a range key is the same key as "
"its content, with no key cell minted on a probe ([string "
"views](string-views.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:196
msgid "`calc` — the `Math` namespace"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:198
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use calc::{ Math };\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"t\");\n"
"    let x = 3.0f64;\n"
"    let y = 4.0f64;\n"
"    let d = Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y);\n"
"    let a = Math.abs(x);\n"
"    let hf = Math.sqrt_f(2.0);            // f32 twin — the width is in the "
"name\n"
"    log.info(f\"{d} {a} {hf}\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:217
msgid ""
"Functions (each with an `_f` f32 twin): `sqrt`, `floor`, `ceil`, `round`, "
"`trunc`, `exp`, `ln`, `log2`, `log10`, `sin`, `cos`, `tan`, `asin`, `acos`, "
"`atan`, `sinh`, `cosh`, `tanh`, `pow`, `atan2`, `hypot`, `copysign`, `fma`, "
"plus the float helpers `abs`, `min`, `max`, `signum`. Constants: `Math.PI`, "
"`TAU`, `E`, `SQRT_2`, `LN_2`, `LN_10`, `LOG2_E`, `LOG10_E`, `INFINITY`, "
"`NEG_INFINITY`, `EPSILON`, `MAX`, `MIN`, `MIN_POSITIVE`. Integer numeric "
"methods are core's, not `calc`'s."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:225
msgid "`json` — the serde package"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:227
msgid ""
"Pure rut, `inline = true`, zero host fns — a json mount adds no host "
"bindings."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:239
msgid ""
"**The pair law**: `(?T, ?E)` with exactly one nil — success = `(value, "
"nil)`, failure = `(nil, err)`. Encode returns `?EncodeJsonError` because a "
"cyclic structure is expected, recoverable data, not a trap."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:242
msgid ""
"**Direct decode**: no intermediate document; a type's `decode` reads its "
"expectations straight off the cursor. A `Vec<Row>` decode mints exactly the "
"program's values, once."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:245
msgid ""
"**Numbers**: `i64` accepts integer lexemes only (overflow/decimal lexeme = "
"`WrongType`, never a silent wrap); `f64` parses IEEE-exact in the common "
"range, ±1 ulp beyond (disclosed); encode renders the shortest round-trip "
"decimal."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:249
msgid ""
"**Depth**: capped at 128 both directions, recoverable "
"(`DecodeErrorKind::Depth` / `EncodeErrorKind::Depth`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:251
msgid ""
"**Errors**: payloadless kind enums + fixed-field structs — `DecodeErrorKind "
"{ Unexpected, Truncated, InvalidUtf8, WrongType, Depth, Trailing }`, "
"`EncodeErrorKind { Depth, NotFinite, KeyUnsupported }`; decode details carry "
"`at`/`got`/`expected`, encode details carry `at` and the lazily built "
"`$.rows[3].name` path."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:256
msgid "`decodeJsonBytes` is strict UTF-8 (`InvalidUtf8`), never lossy."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:257
msgid ""
"**Ownership**: json owns the traits; all container impls live in json, gated "
"by peer groups — `Vec` rows activate when `pouch` is anywhere in the "
"consumer's closure, the map/set rows when `nmapset` is ([dependency "
"kinds](dependency-kinds.md)). A consumer without the peers mounts json light."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:262
msgid ""
"The writer accumulates through `strbuild`'s `StringBuilder`; the reader "
"rides the core `str.scan`/`starts_with` primitives and O(1) string views."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:266
msgid "`strbuild` — the builder"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib.md:268
msgid ""
"```rut\n"
"use ink::{ Logger };\n"
"use strbuild::{ StringBuilder };\n"
"\n"
"pub fn main() {\n"
"    let log = Logger.new(\"t\");\n"
"    let k = \"name\";\n"
"    let mut b = StringBuilder.with_cap(1024);   // octet hint\n"
"    b.append(f\"{k}=\");\n"
"    b.append_code(0x21);\n"
"    let s = b.build();                          // the ONE materialization\n"
"    log.info(s);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

