#: src/reference/frontend.md:132
msgid ""
"Two decisions need more than 4 tokens and use **scans** — read-only, "
"commit-once, never a guess:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:135
msgid ""
"**Lambda vs parenthesized expression.** Scan to the matching `)`; it is a "
"lambda iff the tokens form a valid parameter list and `=>` follows (an "
"optional `-> Type` may sit between). Otherwise a comma inside the parens "
"errors at the comma — rut has no tuples-as-expressions spelling — with a "
"note: _if you meant a lambda, add `=>`_."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:140
msgid ""
"**Generic call vs `<` comparison** (`Vec<f32>(n)` vs `a < b > (c)`). Scan "
"from the `<` tracking angle depth; a `>>`/`<<` consumed where a "
"closer/opener is expected counts as two, so `Vec<Vec<i32>>` needs no "
"re-lexing. Generic arguments commit iff depth returns to 0 on a `>` and the "
"very next token is `(`. `a < b > (c)` is not expressible unparenthesized — "
"write `(a < b) > (c)`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:147
msgid ""
"Scans never mutate parser state. Peeking at arbitrary distance is allowed; "
"checkpoint/rollback is not — the API does not exist, so the monotone-cursor "
"invariant (debug-asserted) cannot be violated, even during error recovery."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:151
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:153
msgid ""
"Within a file the parser resynchronizes at `;`, `}`, or the token after a "
"balanced block and keeps parsing — a file yields many diagnostics, not one. "
"Resync only ever skips forward."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:159
msgid ""
"The mode is chosen by file extension: `Mode::Impl` for `.rut`, `Mode::Decl` "
"for `.d.rut`. Both share one grammar; declaration mode adds the surface "
"declarations — `host fn`, `host struct`, `builtin fn`, `builtin class`, "
"`builtin trait` — and **forbids bodies**: any block, impl blocks included, "
"is rejected with _implementation in a declaration file_. Implementation mode "
"rejects `host`/`builtin` with the mirror message. The full surface and how "
"bodies bind at load time live in [Host fns and declaration "
"files](host-fns.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:168
msgid ""
"Declarations-only module scope is enforced by the parser itself: a statement "
"at module top level is a syntax error, not a semantic one. The grammar "
"itself is specified in [Lexical structure](lexical-structure.md) and "
"[Modules and visibility](modules-and-visibility.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:173
msgid "The AST"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:175
msgid ""
"Nodes are plain records in one arena; children are `NodeId`s into it. Spans "
"sit on every node; there are no `String` keys — names are `IdentId`s into an "
"interner that lives in `rut-core`, shared by the AST, the type table, and "
"the module binary's name table. The interner pre-interns a fixed well-known "
"table (`rut_core::sym`: `self`, `Self`, `nil`, `main`, `__iterate`, the "
"builtin members, the primitives, …), so ids below `well_known_len` mean the "
"same name in every interner instance and special names compare as `IdentId` "
"equality, never by text."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:189
msgid "// items\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:193
msgid "// fields only\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:194
msgid ""
"// fields only —\n"
"                                                           // methods live "
"in impls\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:199
msgid ""
"// .d.rut only\n"
"    // statements\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:202
msgid "// expressions\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:209
msgid "// postfix ?\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:210
msgid "// holes are NodeIds\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:215
msgid ""
"Stable `NodeId`s are the rest of the pipeline's currency: the checker keys "
"side tables by node id, diagnostics reach spans through them, and the LSP, "
"formatter, and dumper hold copyable references with no reparenting."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:219
msgid ""
"What the AST does **not** contain: no `new`, no `switch`/`case`, no `?.` or "
"`??` — the lexer rejects those words before parsing. There are no paren "
"nodes either: the parse's grouping _is_ the tree."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:223
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:230
msgid ""
"One renderer serves every frontend stage: a primary line with a caret span, "
"secondary labels, and notes, all over byte offsets "
"(`rut_lexer::diag::render_diags`). Rendering sorts by span so multi-file "
"output is stable. Suggestions are part of the message set: _did you mean "
"`when`?_ for `switch`/`match`; _bind it to a name first_ for string literals "
"in format-string holes; _classes have no instance literal — use "
"`Circle(..)`_ for `Circle { .. }` on a class."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:238
msgid ""
"The compile stops before IR if any diagnostic exists — a module with "
"diagnostics never produces bytecode. See [Diagnostics, traces, and "
"symbolication](diagnostics.md) for the runtime half of the story."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:243
msgid "The formatter"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:245
msgid ""
"`rut fmt` (crate `rut-fmt`, CLI subcommand) reprints a parsed-clean module "
"from the AST:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:248
msgid ""
"**Comment gap-scan** — comments live in the byte gaps between token spans, "
"so the formatter recovers every `//` and block comment with zero "
"lexer/parser changes: trailing runs go on their element's line, own-line "
"runs at the enclosing indent."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:252
msgid ""
"**Parens and literals re-derived** — the printer re-parens only where flat "
"precedence would invert the tree, re-spells floats shortest round-trip from "
"their bits, and re-quotes strings by the exact inverse of the lexer's escape "
"set (`0xff` legitimately becomes `255`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:256
msgid ""
"**Tested invariants** — every corpus file formats, reparses clean, and is "
"idempotent (`fmt(fmt(x)) == fmt(x)`); probe programs run through the full "
"pipeline before and after formatting and log identical output."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:259
msgid ""
"**Refusal law** — a source with diagnostics is refused: rendered "
"diagnostics, exit 1, nothing rewritten. The formatter never guesses."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:261
msgid ""
"**Style is the package's** — the nearest ancestor `rut.toml`'s `[style]` "
"block sets `indent_width` (1–8, default 4) and `max_width` (≥ 20, default "
"100); no manifest means defaults. See [Project structure and "
"rut.toml](project-structure.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:266
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/frontend.md:268
msgid ""
"The corpus is the conformance suite: every `examples/**/*.rut`, "
"`examples/**/*.d.rut`, and playground classic must parse with zero "
"diagnostics. Parser invariant tests include 100k-deep `((((`, `[[[[`, "
"`{{{{`, unary chains, and nested generic arguments — each yields exactly one "
"_nesting too deep_ diagnostic — and fuzz targets assert no host stack "
"overflow and no cursor rollback. Formatter tests pin the round-trip and "
"idempotence laws above."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:3
msgid ""
"Compilation is AOT, in-process, and deterministic. There is no JIT and no "
"deoptimization: whatever the checker proves is final, and the emitted "
"bytecode is the whole story."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:17
msgid ""
"The unit of compilation is the module. A `.d.rut` declaration surface runs "
"through resolve/typecheck and stops there — it has no bodies, so it "
"publishes a signature surface, never code."
msgstr ""

