#: src/reference/compiler.md:35
msgid ""
"The middle stages are deliberately **one crate**: the checker's "
"monomorphization queue drives the body compiler and the body compiler "
"reports new instantiations back through the checking context. The fusion "
"keeps instantiation admission exact — every substitution-completing call "
"site is checked against its inline `requires` bounds as it is compiled."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:41
msgid "Resolve"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:43
msgid "Name resolution walks the AST and binds every path to a symbol:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:45
msgid ""
"`use` imports resolve against the mounted session — exact, single-step: a "
"use path resolves only if a module with that name is mounted. Missing "
"modules diagnose against the consumer manifest (see [Loading](loading.md) "
"and [Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:49
msgid ""
"`Self` binds inside impls; `pub` visibility is checked per [Modules and "
"visibility](modules-and-visibility.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:51
msgid ""
"Struct-vs-class is decided here: literals are legal only for structs; "
"classes construct through their class methods."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:53
msgid ""
"`is` expressions resolve their right-hand side to a concrete type or a trait "
"instantiation id; `is` on an erasure-typed receiver answers by the box (see "
"[opaque — erasure and downcast](opaque.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:56
msgid ""
"`host`/`extern` surface references resolve against the declaration surfaces "
"of the packages the module imports, with slot ids attached to every member "
"reference."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:60
msgid "Typecheck"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:62
msgid ""
"Bidirectional inference: expected types flow down, literal types flow up. "
"Every expression node is decorated with a type id (an index into the "
"module's type table). Generic calls get their instantiation inferred or take "
"it explicitly (`downcast<Point>(o)`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:67
msgid "Laws enforced here:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:69
msgid ""
"**The `==` law** — primitives and `str` compare by value; every other cell "
"type compares by identity; nullable `?T` operands and tuple operands are a "
"compile error (_pattern-match instead_ — destructure the pair). A lint flags "
"`==` between two obviously fresh composites."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:73
msgid ""
"**`is` folding** — when the receiver's static type already answers the "
"question (a concrete receiver, `d: I is I`), the expression folds to a "
"constant and an always-true/false lint fires."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:76
msgid ""
"**Union bounds** — a generic parameter's `requires T1 | T2` bound is checked "
"at every site that completes the substitution ([Type aliases and union "
"bounds](type-aliases.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:79
msgid ""
"**The crossing rule** — an `entry fn`'s published signature may only use "
"types that cross the host boundary: primitives, `str`, `bytes`, `opaque`, "
"`?T` over a crossing type (nil-flattened), and tuples of crossing types. A "
"violation is a compile error, so a bad surface never reaches the embedder at "
"load time ([The host boundary](../core-concepts/host-boundary.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:84
msgid ""
"**The orphan rule** — `impl Trait for Type` is legal only in a package that "
"defines the trait or the type. Trait impls for foreign pairs are a "
"compile-time rejection, not a link-time surprise ([Traits and "
"dispatch](traits.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:89
msgid "Monomorphization"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:91
msgid ""
"Generic functions never reach a binary. The checker's instantiation queue "
"compiles one concrete copy per substitution; the queue closes because "
"instantiating a body can enqueue more. Instantiation names (`[i32]`, "
"`Vec<f32>`) are synthesized into the shared interner, and `type_id<T>()` "
"folds to a constant from the type table at this point — it never executes at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:98
msgid ""
"The same law has a packaging consequence: a module exporting a **generic "
"function or generic class** cannot be linked against (a linked surface "
"carries only monomorphic exports). Such packages set `inline = true` in "
"their manifest — the graph compiler splices their source into every consumer "
"instead of linking them (`ink`, `json`, `nmapset`, `strbuild`, `async_host`, "
"`http`). See [Project structure and rut.toml](project-structure.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:105
msgid "The type lattice"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:107
msgid ""
"In a no-JIT VM, compile-time type knowledge is the only knowledge. The IR "
"tracks a per-value lattice:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:114
msgid "**Exact types** compile to direct calls and known layouts."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:115
msgid ""
"**Trait-typed values** (`d: Drawable`) are unsized: the payload lives in a "
"heap cell and the slot stores the cell handle. One indirect vtable call per "
"multi-origin use; fields are inaccessible; no inlining without evidence. The "
"cost is per-call, never per-field — and when a call's receiver is statically "
"concrete (a sealed impl set, a monomorphic body), the call devirtualizes at "
"body-compile time and the dispatch overhead is zero."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:122
msgid ""
"**Erasure sits off the lattice.** The `opaque` primitive is reached only "
"through the type-call `opaque(v)`, and `opaque.downcast<T>(o)` is the "
"refinement: the successful branch re-enters the _exact_ lattice position, so "
"downstream code optimizes as if nothing was erased. Downcast checks are pure "
"dataflow — repeated checks CSE, invariant ones hoist, and a chain over one "
"cell folds to a type-id switch. What the compiler must **not** assume is the "
"type inside a box at a given program point; speculative devirtualization "
"through `opaque` is JIT behavior and does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:131
msgid ""
"**The slice tier** parallels trait widening: `Array<T, N> | Vec<T> "
"(concrete)  >  Slice<T> view (unsized)`. `N` is part of the type's identity; "
"slices are never boxed or erased."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:135
msgid ""
"The intended program shape: exact types on the hot path, trait-typed values "
"where polymorphism is real, `opaque` only inside heterogeneous storage. "
"Lints flag `downcast` in loop bodies and erasure crossing non-storage "
"function boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:140
msgid "Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:142
msgid "A fixed pipeline with no flags:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:144
msgid ""
"**Folding** — constant arithmetic, `type_id<T>()`, `Array<T, N>.len()` → the "
"constant `N` (with const-index bounds checks folded against it), "
"statically-decided `is` probes, dead branches."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:147
msgid ""
"**Inlining** — single-callee calls and small bodies (a callee op-count "
"budget). Cross-module inlining after linking is future work; v1 binaries "
"carry no cross-function inlined code."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:150
msgid ""
"**CSE / LICM** over pure operations — type-id loads, downcast checks, field "
"loads on immutable records."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:152
msgid ""
"**Peephole + SROA** — the rewriters re-intern operand pools on register "
"remap, so pool sharing stays consistent (see [Typed "
"bytecode](typed-bytecode.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:155
msgid ""
"**Pattern lowering** — downcast chains become one type-id load plus a jump "
"table; `when` on enums lowers to `brtable` over the member value."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:158
msgid ""
"The pipeline is honest by construction: there is no tier-2 to fall back on, "
"so the emitted code must be right the first time. Every gate measures "
"against the example programs and the benchmark corpus."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:162 src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:171
msgid "Async lowering"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:164
msgid ""
"`async fn` compiles to a state machine: each `await` is a checkpoint state "
"in the hidden frame, resume dispatch is the existing jump-table op, locals "
"become frame fields, and suspension is a plain return. The op set grows zero "
"rows for this — the driven half is an ordinary trait-vtable call through the "
"future's `yield` row. The full protocol lives in [Async and await](async.md) "
"and [Tasks](tasks.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:171 src/reference/module-binary.md:77
msgid "Determinism"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/compiler.md:173
msgid ""
"Same source + same dependency versions + same compiler version ⇒ "
"byte-identical output. Serialization is ordered and little-endian "
"everywhere, and the graph compiles dependencies in a fixed post-order before "
"flattening. This is what makes compile caches content-addressable, bundles "
"diffable, and trace restoration by recompilation possible ([Diagnostics, "
"traces, and symbolication](diagnostics.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:3
msgid ""
"The compiler's output — and the VM's input — is **LIR**: a flat op stream "
"per function over typed registers. Every register has a static type recorded "
"in the function's signature, and the load-time verifier re-checks all of it "
"([Module binary and verification](module-binary.md)). The op definitions "
"live in `rut-core/src/ops.rs`; the VM that executes them in [VM "
"core](vm-core.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:10
msgid "Registers and functions"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:12
msgid ""
"Registers are `u16` indices into a per-frame `Vec<Slot>`; a register file "
"can never reach `u16::MAX`, which is reserved as the `NOREG` sentinel for "
"optional single-register operands (a call destination, a native receiver). "
"One function:"
