msgid "// pc -> (line, col), parallel to spans\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:30
msgid "// Some = bodyless host fn (thunk)\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:34
msgid ""
"`host_id` is the one name kind carried as an interner id: a host function is "
"a bodyless `FuncCode` whose `call` dispatches to the embedder's registered "
"body instead of interpreting ([Embedding](embedding.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:38
msgid "Operand pools"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:40
msgid ""
"No op owns a heap allocation. The variadic operand lists — call arguments, "
"record/array/capture element registers, branch-table arms — live in "
"**per-function pools** (`FuncCode::argv` for register lists, "
"`FuncCode::labels` for branch targets); each op carries an `(off, argc)` "
"span into its own function's pool. Consequences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:46
msgid ""
"`Op` is a fixed **24 bytes** — pinned by a compile-time assert, with a "
"never-constructed `Op::Pad` variant holding the reasoning. The natural "
"16-byte stride measured +13% on the interpreter gate (op-stream loads "
"aliasing register-file stores at power-of-two strides); 24 measures clean "
"and stays far narrower than the pointer-carrying layout it replaced."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:52
msgid ""
"Pools are append-only and **deduplicated at emission** — repeated argument "
"shapes share one entry. The empty list is the span `(0, 0)` and is never "
"stored. Optimizer rewrites re-intern on register remap; deleted ops orphan "
"their entries, which is dead weight, not corruption."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:56
msgid ""
"`argc` is `u16`: a list can name at most as many registers as the register "
"file holds. The emitter rejects literals beyond that bound."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:58
msgid ""
"**Method calls fold the receiver into the pool as `argv[0]`**, so the span "
"_is_ the callee's parameter list and one uniform copy loop transfers a frame "
"— no special-cased slot zero."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:61
msgid ""
"The binary format serializes the pools ahead of the code; the verifier "
"bounds-checks every span before execution."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/typed-bytecode.md:64
msgid ""
"Scalar ops are one opcode per operation — the kind (int vs float) is in the "
"opcode and the width in a `prim` operand, resolved by the compiler. The VM "
"never consults the type table for arithmetic and there is no runtime op "
"selector."
msgstr ""

