#: src/reference/project-structure.md:3
msgid ""
"One directory is one module; its `rut.toml` names the exact package it "
"answers to and how to reach its surface and body. This page is the manifest "
"grammar, the resolution laws, and where everything lives in the toolchain "
"tree."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:8
msgid "The manifest"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:10
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# rut/pouch/rut.toml — a body package\n"
"name = \"pouch\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./pouch.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"# rut/calc/rut.toml — a pure declaration surface (a host pkg)\n"
"name = \"calc\"\n"
"entry.type = \"./calc.d.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"# a consumer (an app directory)\n"
"name = \"app\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./app.rut\"\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"pouch = { path = \"../pouch\" }\n"
"ink   = { path = \"../ink\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:28
msgid "The keys, all of them:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:30
msgid "key"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:32
msgid "`name`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:32
msgid ""
"the package's use-path name: bare `[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` only. A scoped or quoted "
"spelling is a manifest error."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:33
msgid "`entry.lib`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:33
msgid "the body: one `.rut` file (or `.rutc`\\-style artifacts where supported)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:34
msgid "`entry.libs`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:34
msgid "ordered extra `.rut` files — the **multi-lib entry** (below)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:35
msgid "`entry.type`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:35
msgid ""
"the declaration surface: one `.d.rut` file. `entry.type` alone makes a "
"**host pkg** — a pure signature surface whose `host fn`s the embedder binds "
"at load ([Host fns and declaration files](host-fns.md))"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:36
msgid "`entry.ir`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:36
msgid "a compiled declaration cache (`.d.ir`), when present"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:37 src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:63
msgid "`[deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:37
msgid ""
"the transitively mounted dependencies — string-valued descriptors: `pkg = { "
"path = \"...\" }`, relative to this manifest. `optional` is rejected here."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:38
msgid "`[peer-deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:38
msgid ""
"presence-gated peers — descriptors accept `path`, `optional`, `lib` "
"([Dependency kinds](dependency-kinds.md))"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:39 src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:66
msgid "`[dev-deps]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:39
msgid "mounted only while building/testing this pkg itself"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:40
msgid "`host_scope`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:40
msgid ""
"the host-fn registration prefix when it must differ from the package name "
"(`rt` keeps its historical `rt:log` scope)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:41
msgid "`inline`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:41
msgid ""
"`true` forces source-inlining into every consumer instead of linking "
"(packages whose entries are generic functions or whose class methods must "
"resolve at the call site)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:42
msgid "`format`, `format_version`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:42
msgid ""
"bundle keys — ignored by directory loading, required by `rut pack` ([Module "
"bundles](bundles.md))"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:43
msgid "`[style]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:43
msgid ""
"formatter knobs: `indent_width` (1–8, default 4), `max_width` (≥ 20, default "
"100). Schema-free at the manifest layer — unknown keys ride; malformed "
"values are formatter errors, never compile errors. Resolution: the nearest "
"ancestor manifest of the formatted file; no manifest → defaults."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:45
msgid ""
"The parser accepts only the TOML subset the format uses (comments, `key = "
"\"string\"`, dotted keys, `[section]`, inline tables), so the driver stays "
"dependency-free and wasm-compatible. Descriptors are key/value maps; unknown "
"descriptor keys are line-targeted manifest errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:51
msgid "Resolution laws"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:53
msgid ""
"**Exact, single-step.** A use path resolves only if a module with that "
"`name` is mounted. Nothing is derived from directories or file layouts."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:56
msgid ""
"**The walk is recursive, with a cycle guard; first mount wins.** An "
"already-mounted name (the embedder's, the root's, or an earlier dep's) is "
"never overwritten — which is what makes peer presence-by-name sound: the "
"consumer's own path for a package always beats the declarer's `path`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:61
msgid ""
"**Name mismatch is an error.** A dep whose manifest `name` disagrees with "
"its key fails, naming both."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:63
msgid ""
"**The cross-table law.** A name in `[deps]` beside `[peer-deps]` or "
"`[dev-deps]` is an error naming both rows; peer + dev together is the "
"sanctioned pairing."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:66
msgid ""
"**`core` needs no `[deps]`** — the driver mounts it unconditionally; every "
"name still requires `use core::{ .. };` per [core and the swappable "
"packages](stdlib.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:70
msgid "The multi-lib entry"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:72
msgid "A package's body may be split across files:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:74
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"name = \"ui\"\n"
"entry.lib  = \"./ui.rut\"\n"
"entry.libs = [\"./store.rut\", \"./t1.rut\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:80
msgid ""
"The loader splices base-first, then `libs` in listed order, newline-joined, "
"into **one module** — one namespace, one visibility scope. A name private to "
"one file is visible to every other file of the package. The manifest is the "
"canonical order (the splice never reads a directory listing — same manifest "
"⇒ same module). A `libs` row without `lib`, a `.d.rut` element, or a file "
"named twice is a loud manifest error. This is assembly, not a language "
"include form — use paths stay inter-module."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:88
msgid ""
"Contrast with peer groups: group files are _presence-gated_ and therefore "
"impl-only; multi-lib files are unconditional and full module citizens — "
"types, functions, and `pub` surface are legal in any file."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:92
msgid "The toolchain tree"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:120
msgid ""
"Dependency line: `rut-lexer ← rut-ast ← rut-parser ← rut-driver → rut-lir → "
"rut-core ← rut-vm` (with `rut-vm-threaded` behind it), hosts (`rut-std`, "
"`rut-wasm`) on top, and `rut-cli`/`demo` above those. `rut-lsp` sits on the "
"frontend crates only — tokens, diagnostics, and symbols need no VM."
msgstr ""

