msgstr ""

#: src/reference/project-structure.md:147
msgid ""
"`demo/` is a React + rspack + TypeScript page over the wasm build. The wasm "
"ABI is two calls — `compile(src)` returning diagnostics, an AST dump, an IR "
"dump, and an optional binary; `run(binary, budget)` returning output lines, "
"an optional trap, and used fuel/heap — with every run bounded (default 10M "
"fuel / 4 MiB heap) so unbounded loops trap and resume instead of hanging the "
"page. The served artifact is deployed at "
"<https://playground.rut.hpp2334.com>."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:3
msgid ""
"Every package's `rut.toml` names the packages it relates to, and the _kind_ "
"of each relation decides how — and whether — it mounts. Three tables, one "
"grammar:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:7
msgid "**`[deps]`** — the transitively mounted dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:8
msgid ""
"**`[peer-deps]`** — **required by default**: not transitively pulled; the "
"_consumer_ must supply the peer. With `optional = true`, presence in the "
"consumer's closure mounts the integration; absence is inert."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:11
msgid ""
"**`[dev-deps]`** — mounted only when building/testing the package itself "
"(the program root), never in a consumer's world."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:14
msgid ""
"Peers are a _presence_ relation, not a _pull_ relation: the gate looks at "
"what the program's closure already contains and never adds a package. A "
"package is either pulled transitively (`[deps]`) or required of the consumer "
"/ held for development (`[peer-deps]`/`[dev-deps]`) — never both."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:20
msgid "The grammar"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:22
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# rut/json/rut.toml — the reference shape\n"
"name = \"json\"\n"
"entry.lib = \"./json.rut\"\n"
"inline = true\n"
"\n"
"[deps]\n"
"strbuild = { path = \"../strbuild\" }\n"
"\n"
"[peer-deps]\n"
"pouch   = { path = \"../pouch\",   optional = true, lib = "
"\"./group-pouch.rut\" }\n"
"nmapset = { path = \"../nmapset\", optional = true, lib = "
"\"./group-nmapset.rut\" }\n"
"\n"
"[dev-deps]\n"
"pouch   = { path = \"../pouch\" }\n"
"nmapset = { path = \"../nmapset\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:40
msgid ""
"Keys are bare package names — the same `[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` law as `name`; a "
"dep-table key outside it is a line-targeted manifest error."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:42
msgid ""
"`[peer-deps]`/`[dev-deps]` descriptors accept exactly three keys: `path` "
"(string, directory-time), `optional` (the one bool the inline grammar "
"learns), and `lib` (string; the peer-gated integration file). Anything else "
"is the strict-manifest error. `[deps]` keeps string-valued descriptors and "
"**rejects** `optional` — it has no options."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:48
msgid ""
"`optional` defaults to `false` — required by default. The zero-dep spelling "
"`{ path = \"..\" }` is valid in all three tables."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:50
msgid ""
"A `lib` ending in `.d.rut` is a load error: the integration must be a `.rut` "
"source — a declaration surface does not gate."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/dependency-kinds.md:52
msgid ""
"**The cross-table law**: a name riding `[deps]` beside `[peer-deps]` or "
"`[dev-deps]` is a manifest error naming both rows — _`pouch` appears in both "
"`[deps]` and `[peer-deps]` — a package is either pulled transitively or "
"required of the consumer, never both_. Peer + dev together is the sanctioned "
"pairing: integration-if-present for consumers, always-present while "
"developing the package itself."
msgstr ""

